//@version=6
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Liquidity + Supply/Demand + Price Action — v11
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// v11 CHANGELOG — NEWEST. Eighth pass, built ON v10 (v10 kept intact beside
// this file). Three briefs: (1) remaining causal bugs, (2) Quasimodo restored
// and Silver Bullet made faithful to the ICT rule, (3) token efficiency to pay
// for both. NOT compiled locally — load in TradingView and report any error
// text verbatim. v10 itself was never compiled after its own V10-18 removals,
// so the ~94,000-token estimate under it is UNVERIFIED; see the BUDGET note.
//
// V11-01 P0 · THE TP LADDER WAS MEASURED AGAINST A DIFFERENT STOP THAN THE RR
//    GATE. f_v5Gate (M17B) ran the target engine against the highest-ranked RAW
//    candidate's stop — machine > model > engine — but MODULE 19 draws and
//    tracks the ACCEPTED producer's stop. When the machine raised a wide stop
//    and an engine won the bar, TP2 was "the best fresh level paying ≥ rrMult ×
//    the MACHINE's risk" printed against the ENGINE's risk: the E-line RR, the
//    alert RR and the tracked TP2 were all the RR of a trade nobody took. The
//    ladder now re-runs the SAME f_tgt with the stop the trade actually uses.
//    The GATE is deliberately unchanged — it must judge the candidate it
//    ranked. (MODULE 19 / 20)
// V11-02 P1 · THE SILVER BULLET COULD ARM, SHIFT AND ENTER ON ONE CANDLE.
//    f_p7Sb walked 0→1→2→fire inside a single bar pass, so a sweep + MSS +
//    FVG tap on one candle was a complete 3-stage "narrative" — the exact
//    double-count V9-07 closed in the tier ladder, still open in the model.
//    Every transition now needs a LATER bar than the one before it. (M16D)
// V11-03 P1 · THE BREAKOUT-TRAP CLASSIFIER WAS A BACK DOOR AROUND V10-09.
//    V10-09 tightened f_sweepQual so a wick is not a sweep (grade 2 needs a firm
//    close-back AND penetration) — then f_brkTrap armed on ANY close beyond a
//    level, any body, and fired on ANY close back inside, writing grade 3 /
//    type 7 (the highest liquidity class the script has) straight into the sweep
//    memory. A one-tick close through a swing low and a one-tick close back was
//    an "institutional breakout trap" that armed the primary machine. The break
//    must now be displacement-grade OR penetrate ≥ 0.25 ATR, and the reclaim
//    must clear the level firmly — the same evidence a swing sweep needs. (M5)
// V11-04 P2 · MACHINE POI TIER preferred a generic zone (4) over an OTE tap (3)
//    when both were true, because the ternary tested tapZone first. The better
//    location now wins; the zone still supplies the anchor. Plus: a QUASIMODO
//    zone tap is tier 3, not 4 (V11-07). (MODULE 17)
// V11-05 P2 · execAEff = v8ExecA + 10 in LOW volatility could exceed 100, and
//    f_execQ is capped at 100 — tier A was unreachable in a quiet tape at high
//    v8ExecA settings. Clamped. (MODULE 16)
// V11-06 P2 · "entry refused · —" on the machine's Setup row when the arbiter
//    voided the machine but accepted another producer (rejL had been cleared to
//    "—" that bar). Reads "entry refused (arbiter)" now. (MODULE 17)
// V11-07 · QUASIMODO RESTORED — and rebuilt on the right definition. v9's QM was
//    "close through the last LH → demand between the two lows flanking it", it
//    needed the whole MODULE 12B HH/HL swing registry, and V10-18 deleted both
//    for the token cap. The classic bullish Quasimodo is L1 → H1 → L2 < L1 (the
//    HEAD takes L1's sell-side liquidity) → a displaced close back above H1 (the
//    right-shoulder break). The level that matters — the QML — is the LEFT
//    SHOULDER L1, the level that was raided, and the invalidation is the head.
//    Both are already in the sweep memory the instant an MSS lands: lastSslLvl
//    IS the raided level and lastSslExt IS the head. So a QM zone is now pushed
//    into the EXISTING zone registry on mssUp / mssDn spanning [head … QML],
//    with no swing registry at all. It inherits the whole v10 lifecycle the v9
//    version never had — visits, mitigation %, life state (FRESH → DEAD), age,
//    spent, dedup, the target map, the anti-chase and the POI-used memory — and
//    it is POI tier 3 for the ladder, the score and the machine. The P7 QM
//    model returns with it (p7mQm), entering on a confirmed rejection inside the
//    QML with the stop under the head. (MODULES 13 / 16 / 16D / 17)
// V11-08 · SILVER BULLET — MACRO-WINDOW FIDELITY. ICT's rule is that the WHOLE
//    sequence happens inside the killzone hour: liquidity is taken, price
//    displaces and shifts, and the entry is the FVG that displacement leg itself
//    created. v10 gated only the ENTRY on the window (a 20:00 raid could arm a
//    10:15 entry through the 15-bar stage budget), armed on a PDH/PDL sweep
//    alone, and entered on ANY nearest entry-grade FVG — a gap from hours
//    earlier could be the trigger. v11: arm on ANY quality sweep of the unified
//    liquidity memory printed THIS bar and inside the window · shift inside the
//    window on a later bar · enter on the SHIFT LEG'S OWN FVG (the f_shift
//    lineage, inShFvgL / inShFvgS) inside the window, in discount, on a
//    confirmation candle. The stop is under the FVG and the raid wick, not the
//    entry candle. Strictly fewer and better-located SB signals. (MODULE 16D)
// V11-09 · TOKEN SWEEP to pay for the above (all provably dead after V10-18):
//    P4Zone.kind / .flipped / .volTag (only "OB" is ever created; KEY and BASE
//    went in v7 / v4) · f_p4Col (its `kind` argument was unused and it had one
//    call site) · f_p4Vis (collapsed to p4ShowOb) · the `ultimate` flag returned
//    by f_p3Nearest (never read — the preference logic that USES it stays) ·
//    f_p3Life's return value (documented unread in v10) · the two level slots
//    returned by f_p3Hidden (never read). Net effect on the cap is still a small
//    INCREASE — see the BUDGET note at the end of this header.
// BUDGET · v10 hit CE10117 at 106,706 on its first load and removed the trap
//    engine and the P1 / QM engines (V10-18) for an ESTIMATED ~94,000. That
//    number was never re-measured. v11 adds roughly +250 compiled tokens net
//    (QM ≈ +450, SB ≈ +90, the six fixes ≈ +170, the sweep ≈ −450). If CE10117
//    appears, the ranked levers are unchanged and all still available: the IB /
//    doji triggers (~1,650) · dashboard debug rows 18–19 (~600) · the MFE / MAE
//    tracker (~480) · a library split of the pure helpers. Every v11 change is
//    tagged `v11` / `V11-nn` in the source for bisecting.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Liquidity + Supply/Demand + Price Action — v10
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// v10 CHANGELOG — NEWEST. Seventh forensic audit (of v9) + CAUSAL ENTRY upgrade.
// Brief: fewer, better-located, causally complete entries. Nothing here adds a
// signal path; every change either fixes a defect or removes a way for a weak /
// stale / recycled setup to reach the label. Full report: AUDIT-v10.md beside
// this file. NOT compiled locally — load in TradingView and report any error
// text verbatim (see the BUDGET note at the end of the header: v9 declared
// itself ~99.5 % of the CE10117 token cap and was never compiled either).
//
// V10-01 P0 · P2 OFF KILLED EVERY SIGNAL. f_p2Dist returned na for every target
//    when "Enable the v4 liquidity distance map" was OFF; the RR gate reads
//    `not na(rr)`, so rrOkL / rrOkS were false on every bar and the machine,
//    the engines and the models were all refused with "no target". The tooltip
//    promised a fallback to the last swing. Fallback now: last fresh swing +
//    the external map (ext swing · PDH/PDL · PWH/PWL). No target = refused;
//    na never silently kills a valid setup. (MODULE 13B)
// V10-02 P1 · MSS → DISPLACEMENT HAD NO CAUSALITY. Tier A's structure leg was
//    `recentMss (10 bars) AND dispUpLive (any big candle in 10 bars)`: an MSS
//    nine bars ago plus an unrelated impulse now = A. New SHIFT LINEAGE
//    (f_shift): the displacement must print ON the shift candle or within
//    maxDispDelay bars after it; the shift-leg FVG must be created between
//    the sweep and maxFvgDelay bars after the shift; both are remembered with
//    the shift they belong to and die with it. (MODULE 6)
// V10-03 P1 · STALE MSS. TRIG_LOOK (10) was the only age test for A / A+.
//    Structure age is graded: ≤ 1 bar strongest · ≤ mssAgeAp (3) A+ · ≤
//    mssAgeA (5) A · older = B at most. (MODULE 6 / 16 / 18)
// V10-04 P1 · TARGET ENGINE. RR was measured to the NEAREST opposing level, so
//    a swing 1.2 R away refused a setup whose external target paid 3 R, and a
//    level inside 1 R was never called what it is — a blocked path. f_tgt:
//    collect fresh targets (nearest · external · HTF objective) → drop taken /
//    wrong-side / inside-noise → nearest opposing fresh liquidity must be ≥
//    minPathR (1 R) or the PATH IS BLOCKED → TP2 = best fresh level paying ≥
//    rrMult (else ≥ v5MinRr, flagged short) → RR to TP2. The machine's ACTIVE
//    state resolves against the real TP2. (MODULES 13B / 17B / 19)
// V10-05 P1 · RETEST DWELL + DEPTH. A visit that sits inside the anchor for six
//    bars was still "the first retest". Dwell is counted per visit (1–2 A+ ·
//    3 A · 4–5 B · > maxRetDwell = FIRST RETEST FAILED), penetration depth is
//    measured (shallow < retDepthLo % · optimal · deep · > 100 % by close =
//    violated) and both feed the score and the tier. (MODULE 17)
// V10-06 P1 · POI LIFECYCLE. Zones carried a visit count and a binary "fresh";
//    typed FVGs a fill state but no visit count. Every S/D zone now has a
//    mitigation % and a life state FRESH → 1ST TOUCH → MITIGATED → WEAK → DEAD
//    (f_life); typed FVGs count visits (vis) and stop being entry-grade on the
//    2nd; zoneMaxTests default 3 → 2 so the 3rd test = DEAD. WEAK caps a POI
//    at tier A, DEAD is no POI. (MODULES 12C / 13 / 16)
// V10-07 P1 · SETUP ID + LINEAGE. Every armed setup gets SETUP-n and remembers
//    the bar of its liquidity event, shift, displacement, shift-leg FVG, first
//    retest and its target; the journal prints the chain. The two machines are
//    one direction-generic function (f_machine) — ~100 lines less at global
//    scope (CE10295 relief) and one place for the retest rules. Its refused
//    entry now records WHY on the Setup row. (MODULE 17 / 18)
// V10-08 P1 · SHIFTED WITHOUT AN ANCHOR waited retWait (20) bars for ANY later
//    FVG. Now: no shift-leg FVG within maxFvgDelay bars and no tapped zone =
//    "no shift-leg FVG" → invalidated. (MODULE 17)
// V10-09 P1 · BREAKOUT TRAP as a liquidity event. RAID → SWEEP (one-candle
//    rejection, f_sweepQual) · RAID → BREAKOUT (close beyond) · BREAKOUT +
//    FAILURE (close back inside within TRAP_WIN bars) = BREAKOUT TRAP, written
//    to the sweep memory as type 7 grade 3, so trap → MSS → displacement → FVG
//    → first retest is a machine setup. f_sweepQual grade 2 now needs BOTH a
//    firm close-back and real penetration (a wick is not a sweep). (MODULE 5)
// V10-10 P1 · ENTRY QUALITY SCORE 0–100 replaces the v3 alignment score:
//    liquidity 15 · HTF 15 · POI 15 · shift 15 · displacement 10 · FVG 10 ·
//    retest 10 · target 5 · session 5. It can only REMOVE a tier (A ≥ scoreA,
//    A+ ≥ scoreAp) and < minScore (60) is NO TRADE. Hard gates stay hard. The
//    label reads "A+ LONG · L3 · 93". (MODULE 18)
// V10-11 P1 · HARD NO-TRADE ENGINE. Every refusal has a named reason: stale
//    shift · no causal displacement · no shift-leg FVG · POI dead/weak · retest
//    #n · dwell · path blocked · no target · RR · HTF conflict · chop · extreme
//    volatility · pre-news / reprice · chase · score. Shown on the dashboard
//    "⚙ No-trade" row (always, not only in debug). (MODULE 18 / 21)
// V10-12 P2 · THREE ENTRY LEVELS. L1 AGGRESSIVE = tier B (POI touch +
//    rejection) · L2 CONFIRMED = tier A (POI + liquidity + causal shift +
//    displacement + retest) · L3 INSTITUTIONAL = A+ with a shift-leg FVG.
//    Default filter is "A and above" (L2+); L1 must be opted into. (M18 / M20)
// V10-13 P2 · VOLATILITY REGIME from the ATR percentile (volLook bars): LOW
//    (≤ 20 %: A needs exec +10) · NORMAL · EXPANSION (≥ 80 %) · EXTREME (≥
//    volExtPct: machine only, anti-chase halved). Replaces the dead ltLowVol.
//    (MODULE 11)
// V10-14 P2 · NEWS: five states — NORMAL · PRE-NEWS (newsPreMin before a
//    window: no new entries) · NEWS RISK · POST-NEWS REPRICE (first newsRepMin
//    after: nothing enters the first impulse) · POST-NEWS CONFIRMATION (as v7:
//    machine may enter, engines need the whole narrative). (MODULE 8)
// V10-15 P2 · HTF LOCATION alone no longer passes the bias filter — the LTF must
//    also show a sweep in play AND an external shift (HTF POI + HTF conflict
//    without an LTF reversal model = refused). Correlation is a score modifier
//    (+2 / −3) as well as the A+ withhold. (MODULE 16 / 18)
// V10-16 P2 · CONFIRMATION QUALITY: wick rejection added to f_execQ (weights
//    re-balanced to 100); IB break, doji and HTF CRT / TBS now propose a REAL
//    stop (mother-candle low · window low · HTF candle low) instead of the
//    2-bar fallback that made their RR look excellent. (MODULE 9 / 14 / 16E)
// V10-17 P2 · F2 LATENT FAULT CLOSED for P3Zone / P4Zone: top / bot held as
//    data (box.get_* returned na once the 500-box cap evicted the drawing).
//    P7 BRK scan folded into the nearest-POI walk (one less `zones` loop).
// REMOVED (dead, proven by grep): ltLowVol / ltAtrAvg (never read) · tlTouchMin
//    (always 0) · ltP1…ltP7 (always true) · p3T67Trig* names (unread) · the v3
//    alignment score (ctx/liq/poi/trig/exec, f_decay, sesPts) — replaced by
//    the entry score. History comments v4–v8 condensed (comments compile to
//    nothing; the file is 900 lines shorter to read).
// NEW INPUTS (group "1 · Core engine — causality · retest · score (v10)"):
//    mssAgeA 5 · mssAgeAp 3 · maxDispDelay 2 · maxFvgDelay 3 · minDispQ 2 ·
//    maxRetDwell 5 · retDepthLo 33 · retDepthHi 66 · chasePoiAtr 1.5 ·
//    minPathR 1.0 · scoreA 80 · scoreAp 90 · volLook 200 · volExtPct 95 ·
//    newsPreMin 10 · newsRepMin 5. CHANGED DEFAULTS: tierMode "A and above" ·
//    minScore 60 (now the entry score) · zoneMaxTests 2.
// V10-18 P0 · CE10117 ON FIRST LOAD: "Compiled code contains too many tokens:
//    106706. The limit is 100256." Lever (1) applied: MODULE 16B liquidity-trap
//    engine removed (~280 dense lines; a candidate producer since v7; short-
//    biased 5:2). The trap concept lives on in the MODULE 5 breakout-trap
//    classifier that feeds the primary machine (V10-09). That alone left the
//    estimate ~1 % over, so the next heaviest low-yield module went too: the
//    MODULE 12B P1 HH/HL engine (~5,200 tokens; at default it fed only the
//    Strict "V4STR" layer, a rare flip invalidation and the Quasimodo zones)
//    with QM (~1,300) and the ·ev evidence count (metadata). The primary
//    structure engine (M6), every trigger engine, BPR, hidden CHoCH, the
//    trendlines and all dashboard rows stay. Estimated ~94,000 (≈ 6 % margin).
//    Full text of the removed modules stays in Demand + Price Action-9.pine
//    for a companion indicator. Remaining levers if the cap is hit again: IB /
//    doji triggers · dashboard debug rows · library split of the pure helpers.
//    Report the exact error text.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// v9 CHANGELOG (history). Sixth forensic audit (of v8) + INSTITUTIONAL ENTRY
// ACCURACY upgrade. Brief: fewer, cleaner, CAUSALLY valid entries — true first
// retest, true shift-leg FVG, protected structure, HTF validation, consumed
// liquidity, score dedup. Full report: AUDIT-v9.md beside this file.
// Budget 31,041 raw ≈ 99,470 TV (cap 100,256 CE10117; last known-good compile
// 31,112 raw). Every addition was paid for by a removal listed below. NOT
// compiled locally — load in TradingView and report any error text verbatim.
//
// V9-01 P0 · FIRST RETEST was a per-BAR flag (suLHit) that only demoted A+: a
//    retest lasting 3 bars lost A+ on its 2nd bar, and the THIRD touch of the
//    anchor was still tier A. A retest is now a VISIT (suLVisit / suLIn): the
//    first visit is the FIRST retest however many bars it lasts; leaving it
//    unconfirmed = FIRST RETEST FAILED → the setup is invalidated (v9FirstOnly,
//    ON) or later visits are capped at tier B (OFF). Dashboard states: SWEPT ·
//    AT POI · SHIFTED·no POI yet · POI set·await 1st retest · RETEST #n active ·
//    retest #n left · TRIGGERED. (MODULES 17 / 18 / 21)
// V9-02 P0 · SHIFT-LEG FVG was "the latest respected FVG created inside the last
//    10 bars" — a gap from BEFORE the sweep could become the anchor. The anchor
//    FVG must now be CREATED on or after the bar the leg began (suLLegBar = the
//    arming sweep bar, or the POI-tap bar when the leg starts at the POI), and
//    the anchor is never swapped once a retest visit has started. (MODULE 17)
// V9-03 P0 · HTF VALIDATION: chart 1H with HTF 15m was accepted and silently
//    treated as "HTF". htfOK / biasOK / cfgOK: the HTF and the bias-filter TF
//    must be ABOVE the chart TF, else EVERY signal is blocked and the dashboard
//    title reads "⚠ CONFIG: HTF ≤ chart" (Verdict + Reject rows say why). Auto
//    HTF maps D → W and W → M so it never equals the chart. (MODULES 9 / 16 / 21)
// V9-04 P1 · PROTECTED SWING was the leg's cumulative lowest low / highest high.
//    Now the LAST CONFIRMED PIVOT of the leg (the last HL before a bullish BOS,
//    the last LH before a bearish one); the leg extreme is the fallback when no
//    pivot confirmed inside the leg or the extreme printed after the last pivot.
//    f_structure takes the engine's own pivots (5 internal · 12 external). (M6)
// V9-05 P1 · CONSUMED LIQUIDITY stayed a target. f_taken lifecycle FRESH → SWEPT
//    / BROKEN → CONSUMED for swing · external swing · PDH/PDL · PWH/PWL; the
//    target map, the RR gate, the clean-path test and the TP ladder use fresh
//    levels only. Fresh again only when REPLACED (new pivot / day / week).
//    EQ pools are deleted on touch, so they are fresh by construction. (M5 / M13B)
// V9-06 P1 · FVG CREATION ≠ RETEST: the candle that CREATES a typed FVG counted
//    as "price at the FVG" (p6InFvgL) — tier A's POI leg and the SB / FVG4
//    models could fire on the displacement candle itself. The creation bar is
//    excluded from the nearest-entry-grade scan and the FVG4 scan. (M12C / M16D)
// V9-07 P1 · SCORE / TIER DOUBLE COUNTING: one candle could be the shift AND its
//    own retest in the engine ladder (MSS + displacement + FVG + reclaim on one
//    bar = A). Tier A now needs the shift bar BEFORE the entry bar. An engineered
//    pool that IS the in-play sweep (same bar) is scored once, not twice. (M16)
// V9-08 P1 · MSS GRADE — 1 external CHoCH · 2 MSS (+ quality sweep in play) ·
//    3 HIGH-QUALITY MSS (the shift candle is displacement-grade) — and a
//    DISPLACEMENT GRADE 0–3 (expansion · displacement: body ≥ dispFactor, ≥ 60 %
//    body, outer-30 % close · strong: + FVG created / 1.5 × / consecutive). The
//    machine's A needs MSS ≥ 2, A+ needs 3; CISD-only shift = B. (M6 / M17 / M18)
// V9-09 P1 · POI TIER — 1 HTF FVG POI · 2 corrected OB / shift-leg FVG · 3 OTE /
//    QM / BPR · 4 generic S/D · 5 none. A+ needs ≤ 2 for engines (poiTL/S) and
//    for the machine (suLPoiT); a generic zone caps at A. (M16 / M17 / M18)
// V9-10 P1 · ONE POI, ONE PRIMARY ENTRY: the POI of the last accepted signal per
//    side is remembered (machine anchor · zone · FVG · OB · QM); a candidate at
//    the same level (0.25 ATR) is refused until it ages out (zoneMaxAge). Reject
//    reason "POI used". (MODULE 18)
// V9-11 P2 · HTF LOCATION may pass the HTF bias filter: an entry candle INSIDE an
//    HTF FVG POI on its own side is not counter-trend (v9HtfLoc). HTF bias · HTF
//    location · HTF objective · LTF trigger are four different things. (M9 / M16)
// V9-12 P2 · REGIME × CLASS floor: TRENDING penalises a reversal, RANGING
//    penalises a continuation, TRANSITION / CHOP penalise everything (v5RegUp).
//    v8 penalised everything outside TRENDING regardless of class. (MODULE 17B)
// V9-13 P2 · TRAP / BREAKOUT QUALITY as a MANDATORY count (≥ 3 of 5, LT_MIN_Q):
//    short traps — poke depth · fast failure · close back below · bearish
//    displacement · structure shift; genuine breakouts — acceptance ≥ 2 bars ·
//    retest · displacement · structure · hold. A wick + one red candle is not a
//    trap. The count rides the label ("◬ TRAP LT-5 q4"). (MODULE 16B)
// V9-14 P2 · ANTI-CHASE from the POI edge: a machine entry must close within
//    POI_NEAR_ATR (1.5 ATR) of the anchor edge. Stage-3 "opposing displacement"
//    no longer kills a setup whose anchor HOLDS — that candle IS the fast retest
//    the machine was waiting for (V8-26 resolved). (MODULE 17)
// V9-15 P2 · TP LADDER from FRESH liquidity: TP1 = nearest resting liquidity when
//    it pays 1R–rrMult R · TP2 = nearest fresh level paying ≥ rrMult R (the
//    nearest itself or the external one: ext swing · PDH/PDL · PWH/PWL) · TP3 =
//    a fresh PWH/PWL (else PDH/PDL) beyond TP2. Each row says ·liq / ·1R / ·2R /
//    ·3R synthetic. The map returns the external level too (p2ExtUp/Dn). (M13B / M19)
// V9-16 P2 · FORENSIC JOURNAL (v9Journal): every signal label carries a record in
//    its tooltip — id · NY time · regime · news · corr · sweep age · shift q ·
//    disp q · POI tier @ price · FVG age · retest # · score · trap q. No table,
//    no ink. The label line still shows tier · class · liquidity · session ·
//    structure · POI · range side · HTF n/4 · exec · path · RR. (MODULE 20)
// V9-17 P2 · showEq gated EQ-pool DETECTION (a sweep type, a target, a P7 input).
//    Ink only now — same class as v5.3 F1 / v8 V8-06. (MODULE 4)
// REMOVED / FROZEN to pay for the above (~1,180 raw; each display-only,
//    behaviour-identical at its default, or a switch whose OFF re-enabled a
//    documented defect): f_txt passthrough · p5PinBull/BearRaw (= bullPin /
//    bearPin at the default ratio) · mssExtOnly / v8ShiftFirst / mcShiftExt /
//    v8ReqTgt / v5McFloor / kzNoAsia collapsed to ON · OTE box (showRange) ·
//    dashboard rows Alignment / ◎ FEM / ◇ v4 POI / ⚙ Sweep (type + age folded
//    into "Sweep in play") · 7 informational alert() lines ([LIQ] swing / EQ ·
//    [POI] ×2 · [TRIG] eCHoCH / CISD · [CTX] window ended) · inducement proxy
//    (+IDM) · optional break-even tracker (v8BeTp1) · dcPill · uiDrawOpt (=
//    p8TxtOpt) · showProt (= showStruct) · uiTrans (25) · tpMode · ltShowMarks
//    (= ltShowSetup) · 34 tuning knobs → constants at their defaults: confirmWin
//    5 · ibBodyAtr 1.0 · dojiMin 3 · tlTouchMin 0 · femWait 40 · p1EqTolAtr 0.05
//    · p1MaxSwings 30 · p3MaxKeep 6 · p3BreakAtr 1.2 · p3BosLook 10 · p3HchExp 40
//    · p4ObLook 10 · p4Max 12 · p7Win 15 · hPoiMaxTouch 3 · ltWickAtr 0.4 ·
//    ltWickRatio 1.5 · ltCmpLen 5 · ltCmpSens 0.5 · ltExpSens 1.2 · ltBrkStr 0.8
//    · ltNearAtr 2.0 · ltRetestAtr 0.5 · ltWaitBars 25 · ltInvAtr 1.0 · ltCd 10 ·
//    ltP1…ltP7 true. Inputs 183 → 138.
// NEW INPUTS: v9HtfLoc (ON) · v9FirstOnly (ON) · v9Journal (ON). Input GROUPS
//    renamed into the brief's taxonomy (1 Core engine · 2 Structure · 3
//    Liquidity · 4 POI · 5 Entry · 6 Risk · 7 Context · 8 Diagnostics · 9
//    Display) — group names only, so no saved value resets.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// HISTORY v3 → v8 (condensed in v10; the full text is in Demand + Price
// Action-9.pine). Design notes that still bind:
//   · OUTPUT BUDGET: plot + plotchar + bgcolor + alertcondition share ONE
//     64-slot budget and request.security series count on top. New visuals use
//     labels / lines / boxes; new alerts use alert(), never alertcondition.
//   · COMPILED TOKENS: cap 100,256 (CE10117). GLOBAL-SCOPE SIZE: cap CE10295 —
//     function bodies compile separately, so flat blocks are wrapped in f_*()
//     helpers returning tuples; state lives inside them as function-local var.
//   · REPAINT: every request.security uses lookahead_on WITH a [1] offset (the
//     documented non-repainting idiom — lookahead_off + [1] gave N−2 on
//     history). Every cross-bar state change traces to `confirmed`.
//   · Turtle-soup age via -ta.lowestbars()[1] + 1 is CORRECT (lowestbars ≤ 0).
//     Do not "fix" the sign.
//   · Display toggles never gate detection (v5.3 F1): a hidden family is drawn
//     transparent, never skipped. State is state, drawing is drawing.
//   · Zone geometry lives in data fields (v5.3 F2): box.get_* returns na once
//     the 500-box cap evicts a drawing.
//   · One sweep-quality slot per side; every writer grades ITS OWN candle
//     (v5.3 F3); same-bar writers keep the best of, a new bar recomputes.
//   · The arbiter (v7): every producer is a CANDIDATE; one direction per bar
//     or none; rank = tier × 10 + (2 − class), machine > model > trigger.
//   · v8: per-class stop slots; exec quality 0–100; HTF alignment 0–4;
//     liquidity type hierarchy; clean-path score; effective RR with cost.
//   · v5.3 F4: the machine resolves its own ACTIVE state (mcLSl / mcLTp2).
//   · v7 A2 / v8 V8-00: every sweep writer runs BEFORE the sslInPlay snapshot.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Signals evaluate on CLOSED bars only — use "Once per bar close" alerts.
// The confluence score is NARRATIVE ALIGNMENT, not win probability.
// Educational tool, not financial advice. Backtest before live use.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// max_bars_back: the v4 order-block scan indexes price with a SERIES offset
// (high[j], j from ta.lowestbars) — Pine cannot infer the needed history depth
// from that and its guess is what raises the RE1014x history/buffer errors.
// Declaring it removes the guess. v5.3: back to 300, matching the comment
// above and the original intent. v5.1's 200 was sized on the DEFAULT deepest
// offset (f_p4Key's low[pivLen + i] = 55); pivLen has minval 2 and no maxval,
// so a user-raised pivot length walks straight past 200 and re-opens RE1014x.
// max_bars_back is a history-buffer declaration, not a per-bar cost: it cannot
// change a single signal, only whether the script compiles at extreme inputs.
indicator("Liquidity + S/D + Price Action [MTF] v11", "LQ-SD-PA v11", overlay = true,
     max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500,
     max_bars_back = 300)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 1
// INPUTS
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
grpG = "1 · General"
pivLen     = input.int(5,     "Internal pivot length",                 minval = 2,  group = grpG)
extPiv     = input.int(12,    "External pivot length (major swings)",  minval = 5,  group = grpG)
atrLen     = input.int(14,    "ATR length",                            minval = 1,  group = grpG)
biasLen    = input.int(50,    "Bias EMA length (MTF table)",           minval = 5,  group = grpG)
showLevels = input.bool(true, "Show last swing high/low key levels",   group = grpG)

grpH = "7 · Context — HTF"
biasFilter = input.string("60", "HTF bias filter — block counter-trend entries",
     options = ["Off", "5", "15", "60", "240", "D"], group = grpH,
     tooltip = "Machine entries and B+ engine signals require this timeframe's last CLOSED candle to agree (close vs bias EMA). Off = context scored but never blocking.")
useHtfCrt = input.bool(true, "HTF CRT + Turtle-soup trigger candidates", group = grpH)
htfSel    = input.string("Auto", "HTF for CRT / TBS / POI", options = ["Auto", "15", "30", "60", "240", "D"], group = grpH)
hPoiMaxAge   = input.int(40, "HTF POI max age (HTF candles)",           minval = 5, group = grpH)
hPoiMaxTouch = 3               // v9 const: HTF POI candles inside before spent
v9HtfLoc = input.bool(true, "HTF POI location may override the HTF bias filter (v9 · v10 needs an LTF reversal model)", group = grpH,
     tooltip = "The bias filter blocks counter-EMA entries. ON: a candidate whose entry candle is INSIDE an HTF FVG POI on its own side passes the filter — HTF LOCATION outranks HTF BIAS for a reversal at the level. v10 (V10-15): only when the LTF shows the reversal model too — a sweep in play AND an external shift (MSS / CHoCH). An HTF POI on its own never justifies a counter-trend entry. The HTF alignment count, the tier ladder, the score's HTF bucket (bias conflict −5) and the range-side rule are unchanged, so such an entry is graded like any other.")

grpL = "3 · Liquidity"
showSweeps = input.bool(true,  "Mark liquidity sweeps (◆ / ◈)",         group = grpL)
sweepLook  = input.int(15,     "Sweep stays in play (bars)", minval = 1, group = grpL)
showEq     = input.bool(true,  "Track equal highs / lows (EQH / EQL)",  group = grpL,
     tooltip = "v9: ink only. EQ pools are ALWAYS detected (they are a sweep type, a liquidity target and a P7 input); OFF hides the dotted lines.")
eqTol      = input.float(0.15, "Equal level tolerance (ATR ×)", step = 0.05, minval = 0.05, group = grpL)
minArmQual = input.int(2,      "Min sweep quality to arm a setup (1–4)", minval = 1, maxval = 4, group = grpL,
     tooltip = "1 weak (reclaimed, shallow) · 2 valid (firm reclaim) · 3 strong (+outer-half close & displacement body) · 4 institutional (strong + structure shift while in play).")
showPdwl   = input.bool(true,  "Previous day / week high–low lines",    group = grpL)

grpM = "2 · Structure"
showStruct = input.bool(true,  "Label BOS / CHoCH / MSS",               group = grpM)
structDisp = input.float(0.5,  "Structural break body ≥ ATR × (0 = any close)", step = 0.1, minval = 0, group = grpM)

grpF = "4 · POI — FVG"
showFvg    = input.bool(true, "Draw live chart-TF FVGs",                group = grpF,
     tooltip = "v5: one registry only. These boxes are the MODULE 12C typed gaps (type, BSI/SBI, ultimate, premium/discount, mitigation state). v4 drew the plain v3 box AND the typed box over the same gap.")

grpZ = "4 · POI — Supply / Demand / Order blocks"
showZones  = input.bool(true,   "Show zones",                           group = grpZ)
dispFactor = input.float(1.2,   "Displacement body ≥ ATR ×", step = 0.1, minval = 0.5, group = grpZ)
maxZoneAtr = input.float(2.0,   "Max zone height (ATR ×)",   step = 0.5, minval = 0.5, group = grpZ)
maxZones   = input.int(6,       "Max zones per side", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = grpZ)
showOB     = input.bool(true,   "Also mark the ORDER BLOCK origin candle", group = grpZ,
     tooltip = "The opposing candle immediately before the displacement leg. Drawn as a thin companion zone when its range is distinct from the FVG imbalance.")
confirmWin = 5                  // v9 const: bars from 50 % tap to confirmation
showFlip   = input.bool(true,   "Flip violated zones into breaker / mitigation blocks", group = grpZ)
showRB     = input.bool(true,   "Rejection blocks (swept pivot wick + displacement away)", group = grpZ)
zoneMaxTests = input.int(2,     "Zone spent after N separate tests", minval = 1, maxval = 6, group = grpZ,
     tooltip = "v10 lifecycle: FRESH → 1ST TOUCH → MITIGATED (≥ 50 % traded) → WEAK (2nd test) → DEAD (3rd test = spent). Each separate visit (leave + return) consumes the zone. WEAK caps the POI at tier A; DEAD is no POI. Default 2 = the third test kills it.")
zoneMaxAge = input.int(200,     "Zone max age (bars, 0 = never)", minval = 0, group = grpZ,
     tooltip = "v7: supply / demand / OB / rejection / breaker zones had NO age. A zone from 800 bars ago that price never revisited was still the 'next demand' and a valid POI for the tier ladder, the confirmation floor and the setup machine. Typed FVGs already aged out at 120 bars. 0 restores v5.3.")

grpC = "5 · Entry — CRT / Turtle soup / CISD / IFC"
showCRT    = input.bool(true,  "CRT 3-candle trigger candidates",       group = grpC)
crtRangeAtr = input.float(1.2, "CRT min candle-1 range (ATR ×)", step = 0.1, minval = 0.5, group = grpC)
crtDispAtr  = input.float(0.5, "CRT min candle-3 body (ATR ×)",  step = 0.1, minval = 0.1, group = grpC)
showTBS    = input.bool(true,  "Turtle soup trigger candidates",        group = grpC)
tbsLen     = input.int(20,     "Turtle soup lookback (bars)", minval = 5, group = grpC)
tbsAgeMin  = input.int(4,      "Swept extreme min age (bars)", minval = 1, group = grpC)
tbsAgeMax  = input.int(60,     "Swept extreme max age (bars, 0 = off)", minval = 0, group = grpC,
     tooltip = "An extreme older than this is stale liquidity — its sweep no longer traps a fresh breakout crowd.")
showCisd   = input.bool(true,  "Label CISD (change in state of delivery)", group = grpC)
cisdAsConf = input.bool(true,  "Accept CISD as execution confirmation", group = grpC)
showIFC    = input.bool(true,  "Mark IFC candles (pool grab + displacement)", group = grpC)
sigCooldown = input.int(10,    "Engine cooldown per direction (bars)", minval = 0, group = grpC)

grpB = "5 · Entry — Inside bar / Doji (context-gated)"
showS3     = input.bool(true,  "Inside Bar Breakout trigger",           group = grpB)
ibBodyAtr  = 1.0               // v9 const: mother-candle body ≥ ATR ×
showS4     = input.bool(true,  "Doji Reversal trigger",                 group = grpB)
dojiPct    = input.float(25,   "Doji body ≤ % of range", step = 5, minval = 5, maxval = 50, group = grpB)
dojiMin    = 3                 // v9 const: dojis in the 5-bar window
minWickAtr = input.float(0.3,  "Min significant wick (ATR ×)", step = 0.1, group = grpB)

grpTL = "5 · Entry — Trendlines"
showTL     = input.bool(true, "Draw dynamic trendlines (pivot pairs)",  group = grpTL)
tlSweepEnt = input.bool(true, "Trendline sweep trigger candidates",     group = grpTL)
tlNeedConf = input.bool(true, "Require confirmation candle at the line", group = grpTL)

grpFE = "5 · Entry — Fractal entry model (HTF POI → LTF shift → LTF FVG)"
useFEM  = input.bool(true, "◎ Enable fractal entry model", group = grpFE)
femWait = 40                  // v9 const: bars from HTF POI tap to execution
showPoi = input.bool(true, "Draw live HTF FVG POI boxes", group = grpFE)

grpO = "4 · POI — Dealing range / OTE"
rangeSrc  = input.string("External", "Dealing range swings", options = ["External", "Internal"], group = grpO)

grpK = "7 · Context — Sessions (New York time)"
useKZ   = input.bool(false, "Only signal inside killzones (intraday)",  group = grpK)
paintKZ = input.bool(false, "Shade killzones",                          group = grpK)
showSesHL = input.bool(true, "Session high / low liquidity lines",      group = grpK)
asiaSes = input.session("2000-0000", "Asia",                            group = grpK)
lonSes  = input.session("0200-0500", "London",                          group = grpK)
nySes   = input.session("0700-1000", "New York AM",                     group = grpK)
sbSesLO = input.session("0300-0400", "Silver Bullet — London open",     group = grpK)
sbSesAM = input.session("1000-1100", "Silver Bullet — NY AM",           group = grpK)
sbSesPM = input.session("1400-1500", "Silver Bullet — NY PM",           group = grpK)
// v5.3 F5: a 4th TRADE window. sbSesPM used to do double duty — it is what let
// PM entries through inKZ, but p7SbSes also gates the Silver Bullet MODEL off
// the three sb* inputs, so widening the PM trade window silently widened the SB
// model with it. Default is identical to sbSesPM, so stock output is unchanged.
nyPmSes = input.session("1400-1500", "New York PM (trade window)",      group = grpK,
     tooltip = "Killzone-only window. Default matches the Silver Bullet PM session, so out of the box it adds nothing. Widen it (e.g. 1330-1600) to trade the PM session WITHOUT widening the Silver Bullet model, which reads sbSesLO / sbSesAM / sbSesPM.")
sweepMaxHrs = input.float(8, "Core-session sweep stays in play up to (hours, 0 = bars only)", step = 0.5, minval = 0, group = grpK,
     tooltip = "v7: a sweep taken in a CORE session stays in play while price is still inside a trade window and less than this many clock hours have passed — a 03:00 London raid is still the narrative at 09:30, on 1M exactly as on 15M. 'Sweep stays in play (bars)' alone made that 15 minutes on 1M and 15 hours on H1. The held test, the 3-ATR proximity rule and the anti-chase distance still apply. Needs the v7 session model.")

grpN = "7 · Context — Scheduled volatility windows (NY time) — NOT a live calendar"
useNews   = input.bool(true,  "Block entries inside the windows", group = grpN,
     tooltip = "Fixed clock windows around the usual 08:30 / 10:00 / Wednesday 14:00 US release slots. NOT an economic calendar — edit sessions to match the week. Day codes: 1=Sun … 7=Sat.")
paintNews = input.bool(true,  "Shade the windows", group = grpN)
news1Ses  = input.session("0825-0845:23456", "Window #1 — 08:30 US data slot", group = grpN)
news2Ses  = input.session("0955-1010:23456", "Window #2 — 10:00 US data slot", group = grpN)
news3Ses  = input.session("1355-1435:4",     "Window #3 — 14:00 FOMC slot (Wed)", group = grpN)
newsPostMin = input.int(15, "POST-NEWS state lasts (minutes after a window, 0 = off)", minval = 0, group = grpN,
     tooltip = "v7: three states instead of two. NORMAL · NEWS RISK (inside a window: entries blocked as before) · POST-NEWS (this many clock minutes after a window closes: the setup machine may still enter — it IS the narrative — but every engine / model / trap candidate must show the whole sequence: liquidity event + structure shift + displacement + price AT a POI). A+ is never granted in the post-news state. Clock-based, so 1M and 15M see the same length.")
newsPreMin = input.int(10, "PRE-NEWS: no new entries N minutes before a window (0 = off)", minval = 0, group = grpN,
     tooltip = "v10: a setup confirmed 3 minutes before the 08:30 print is a coin flip on the print. Clock minutes before each window's start (parsed from the session strings, same day codes).")
newsRepMin = input.int(5, "POST-NEWS REPRICE: no entries for the first N minutes after a window (0 = off)", minval = 0, group = grpN,
     tooltip = "v10: the first post-news impulse is repricing, not a setup. After this many minutes the POST-NEWS CONFIRMATION state (newsPostMin) applies: the machine may enter, engines need the whole narrative.")
// v5.3 F6: the two defaults collide and nothing said which wins. news2Ses
// 0955-1010 eats the first ten minutes of sbSesAM 1000-1100; news1Ses
// 0825-0845 eats the 08:30 drive. Precedence is now explicit, not emergent.
newsVetoSb = input.bool(true, "A volatility window vetoes a Silver Bullet window", group = grpN,
     tooltip = "ON (v5.2 behaviour, kept as the default): the scheduled-volatility block wins, so 09:55-10:10 blocks the first 10 minutes of the 10:00-11:00 Silver Bullet window and 08:25-08:45 blocks the 08:30 drive. OFF: inside a Silver Bullet window the volatility block is lifted — choose this if you trade the release itself rather than avoiding it. Neither is retuned; you pick which model owns the overlap.")

grpQ = "1 · Core engine — tiers · setup machine · regime"
tierMode = input.string("A and above", "Show signal tiers (entry level)",
     options = ["A+ only", "A and above", "B and above", "All (incl. C)"], group = grpQ,
     tooltip = "v10 ENTRY LEVELS. C = bare technical trigger · B = LEVEL 1 AGGRESSIVE (POI touch + rejection, or trigger + liquidity) · A = LEVEL 2 CONFIRMED (liquidity + POI + causal shift + displacement + retest + execution) · A+ = LEVEL 3 INSTITUTIONAL (A + HTF + core session + strong sweep + shift-leg FVG + first retest + clean target + correct premium/discount). Default A and above = Level 2+.")
minScore = input.int(60, "Min entry quality score (0 = off) — v10", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = grpQ,
     tooltip = "v10: the 0–100 ENTRY QUALITY SCORE (liquidity 15 · HTF 15 · POI 15 · shift 15 · displacement 10 · FVG 10 · retest 10 · target 5 · session 5). Below this = NO TRADE for every producer, the machine included. The score can only REMOVE a tier (A needs ≥ scoreA, A+ ≥ scoreAp); the hard gates stay hard.")
masterCd = input.int(10, "Global same-direction cooldown (bars, 0 = off)", minval = 0, group = grpQ)
useRegime = input.bool(true, "Suppress entries in CHOP regime", group = grpQ,
     tooltip = "Exception: an INSTITUTIONAL-grade sweep (quality 4) may still arm a setup inside chop — the classic liquidity-reversal case.")
v9FirstOnly = input.bool(true, "Machine: FIRST retest only (a failed first retest ends the setup)", group = grpQ,
     tooltip = "v9: the anchor (shift-leg FVG or the tapped POI zone) gets ONE retest. If price enters it and leaves again without a confirmation candle, the setup is INVALIDATED ('first retest failed') and a NEW liquidity sweep is required — it never becomes another A / A+ on the second or third touch. OFF: later retests may still enter, capped at tier B. A retest is one VISIT: price may sit inside the anchor for several bars and confirm on any of them. The candle that created the FVG never counts as its retest.")
liqWait  = input.int(20, "Machine: bars from sweep to POI tap",   minval = 3, group = grpQ)
poiWait  = input.int(15, "Machine: bars from POI tap to shift",   minval = 3, group = grpQ)
retWait  = input.int(20, "Machine: bars from shift to entry",     minval = 3, group = grpQ)
v7PdRev = input.bool(true, "Reversal setups need the correct side of the range", group = grpQ,
     tooltip = "ON: reversal-class candidates — setup machine, CRT, turtle soup, HTF CRT / TBS, doji reversal, trendline sweep, liquidity trap — are refused in PREMIUM for longs and DISCOUNT for shorts, UNLESS external structure AND the HTF bias already point the trade's way (then it is a continuation pullback and passes). Continuation-class triggers (inside-bar break, zone 50 %, FEM, the v4 models) are never blocked by this. No dealing range = no block.")

grpR = "6 · Risk — SL / TP / RR"
showTrade = input.bool(true, "Show entry / SL / TP of last signal", group = grpR)
rrMult    = input.float(2.0, "TP2 R multiple", step = 0.5, minval = 0.5, group = grpR)

grpD = "8 · Diagnostics"
showDash = input.bool(true,  "Show context dashboard", group = grpD)
v9Journal = input.bool(true, "Signal journal on the label tooltip (hover the signal)", group = grpD,
     tooltip = "v9 (§30): every signal label carries a forensic record in its tooltip — id · NY time · regime · news state · correlation · sweep age · shift grade · displacement grade · POI tier and price · FVG age · retest number · score · trap quality. The label itself still shows tier · class · liquidity · session · structure · POI · range side · HTF · exec · path · RR. No table, no extra ink.")
showDbg  = input.bool(false, "Developer debug rows (sweep · target · structure · rejection)", group = grpD,
     tooltip = "v7: four extra dashboard rows for forensic validation — sweep grade / age / session / distance from the wick per side, the liquidity target and live RR (or 'synthetic'), displacement / MSS / external CHoCH recency, and the last reason each side's raw candidate was refused, plus the breakout classifier's last verdict. Not for normal chart display.")

grpU = "9 · Display — UI"
uiSizeOpt  = input.string("Normal", "Signal label size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large"], group = grpU)
uiDashOpt  = input.string("Normal", "Dashboard / debug text size", options = ["Small", "Normal", "Large"], group = grpU)

grpV8 = "1 · Core engine — quality thresholds (soft scores can only REMOVE a tier)"
v8ExecA  = input.int(60, "Execution quality needed for tier A (0–100)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = grpV8,
     tooltip = "v8: the confirmation candle is scored — body/range (20) · close location (20) · displacement (20) · liquidity reclaim (15) · structure break / CISD (15) · FVG created (10) · volume expansion (10, capped at 100). A pin, engulfing, IFC or CISD still has to be PRESENT; this decides whether it is strong enough for A. Below this the candidate caps at B.")
v8ExecAp = input.int(75, "Execution quality needed for A+ (0–100)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = grpV8)
v8ApHtf  = input.int(3, "A+ needs HTF alignment ≥ (of 4)", minval = 1, maxval = 4, group = grpV8,
     tooltip = "v8: HTF alignment = filter-TF EMA side + HTF rolling structure (HH+HL / LH+LL on the CRT/TBS timeframe) + an HTF FVG POI on the trade's side + the Daily EMA side. A bullish EMA alone no longer makes an A+.")
v8ApLiq  = input.int(2, "A+ needs sweep type ≥ (1 swing · 2 EQ · 3 session · 4 PDH/PDL · 5 ext swing · 6 PWH/PWL)", minval = 1, maxval = 6, group = grpV8,
     tooltip = "v8 liquidity hierarchy. Every sweep remembers WHAT was taken; a bare 5-bar internal pivot poke is type 1 and cannot make an A+ at the default.")
v8CorrSym = input.symbol("", "Correlated symbol (blank = off)", group = grpV8,
     tooltip = "Optional context. The symbol's bias on the filter timeframe (close vs bias EMA, last closed bar) is read sign-adjusted; a CONFLICT with the trade withholds A+ and is printed in the label. Examples: XAUUSD ↔ TVC:DXY (inverse), BTC ↔ ETH (direct).")
v8CorrInv = input.bool(true, "Correlated symbol moves INVERSELY (XAUUSD ↔ DXY, EURUSD ↔ DXY)", group = grpV8)

// v10: CAUSALITY · RETEST · SCORE — the thresholds behind the new hard gates.
// Sensible defaults; every one of them REMOVES setups when tightened.
grpV10 = "1 · Core engine — causality · retest · score (v10)"
mssAgeA  = input.int(5, "Max structure-shift age for tier A (bars)", minval = 1, group = grpV10,
     tooltip = "v10: age of the external shift (MSS / CHoCH) at the entry bar. ≤ 1 bar strongest · ≤ A+ limit · ≤ this = A at most · older = B at most. Tier B keeps the 10-bar trigger memory.")
mssAgeAp = input.int(3, "Max structure-shift age for A+ (bars)", minval = 0, group = grpV10)
maxDispDelay = input.int(2, "Displacement must print ON the shift candle or within N bars after", minval = 0, group = grpV10,
     tooltip = "v10 causality: the displacement that qualifies a shift belongs to it. An impulse 8 bars after the shift is a different event.")
maxFvgDelay = input.int(3, "Shift-leg FVG must exist within N bars of the shift", minval = 0, group = grpV10,
     tooltip = "v10: the anchor FVG is the shift leg's OWN gap — created between the liquidity event and this many bars after the shift. The machine is invalidated ('no shift-leg FVG') when none prints and no zone was tapped.")
minDispQ = input.int(2, "Min displacement grade in the shift leg for A / A+ (1–3)", minval = 1, maxval = 3, group = grpV10,
     tooltip = "1 expansion (body ≥ 0.5 ATR) · 2 displacement (body ≥ dispFactor × ATR, ≥ 60 % body, outer-30 % close) · 3 strong (+ FVG created / 1.5 × / consecutive).")
maxRetDwell = input.int(5, "Max retest dwell — bars price may sit inside the anchor", minval = 1, group = grpV10,
     tooltip = "v10: dwell 1–2 bars = A+ quality · 3 = A · 4–5 = B · beyond this the FIRST RETEST FAILED (price is accepting the level, not rejecting it).")
retDepthLo = input.int(33, "Optimal mitigation band — from (% of anchor)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = grpV10)
retDepthHi = input.int(66, "Optimal mitigation band — to (% of anchor)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = grpV10,
     tooltip = "v10 retest depth: shallow below the band (scored 1) · optimal inside it (2) · deep above it (0) · more than 100 % by CLOSE = anchor violated. Not a hard reject for deep — it is scored.")
chasePoiAtr = input.float(1.5, "Anti-chase — entry close within (ATR ×) of the anchor edge", step = 0.25, minval = 0.25, group = grpV10,
     tooltip = "v10: halved in the EXTREME volatility regime. The sweep-origin and displacement-origin anti-chase (v5Late) still apply.")
minPathR = input.float(1.0, "Clean path — nearest opposing FRESH liquidity must be ≥ (R) away", step = 0.25, minval = 0, group = grpV10,
     tooltip = "v10 target engine: opposing resting liquidity inside this many R of the entry = the path is blocked (price reacts there before the trade is paid). 0 = off.")
scoreA  = input.int(80, "Entry score needed for tier A (0–100)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = grpV10)
scoreAp = input.int(90, "Entry score needed for A+ (0–100)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = grpV10)
volLook = input.int(200, "Volatility regime — ATR percentile lookback (bars)", minval = 20, group = grpV10,
     tooltip = "v10: LOW ≤ 20th percentile (A needs exec +10) · NORMAL · EXPANSION ≥ 80th · EXTREME ≥ the threshold below (machine entries only, anti-chase halved). Normalised, not a fixed ATR number.")
volExtPct = input.int(95, "EXTREME volatility at ATR percentile ≥", minval = 50, maxval = 100, group = grpV10)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 2
// CONSTANTS + SMALL UTILITIES
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var float NEAR_LVL_ATR   = 0.25  // "price is at the level" tolerance
var float SL_PAD_ATR     = 0.25  // stop-loss padding beyond structure
var float SWEEP_CTX_ATR  = 3.0   // sweep in play while price within this of the level
var float POI_NEAR_ATR   = 1.5   // "near the POI" distance for scoring
var float STRONG_CLOSE_PCT = 0.30 // close in outer 30% of candle = strong close
var float CISD_NEUTRAL_PCT = 0.10 // body ≤ 10% of range = neutral candle
var int   TRIG_LOOK      = 10    // bars a shift / CISD stays a live trigger
var int   IFC_LOOK       = 3     // prior bars whose extreme an IFC must take
var float BRK_BODY_ATR   = 0.5   // min body for a meaningful break close
var int   IB_WAIT_BARS   = 4     // bars allowed for the inside-bar break
var int   TRAP_WIN       = 6     // v10: bars an ACCEPTED break must fail inside to be a BREAKOUT TRAP
var int   TRADE_BARS     = 15    // length of entry/SL/TP lines
var int   DOJI_WINDOW    = 5     // lookback window for counting dojis
var int   MAX_EQ_POOLS   = 8     // max EQH/EQL pools per side
var float OTE_1          = 0.62
var float OTE_2          = 0.79
var int   REGIME_LOOK    = 30    // bars of external-event memory for the regime
var float CHOP_RANGE_ATR = 6.0   // external range narrower than this (ATR ×) = chop candidate
var int   V8_PATH_AP     = 75    // v8: A+ clean-path floor — 100 clean, −35 per opposing OB / FVG / HTF POI in the path
// ◇ P8 (v4): the two engine colours become style inputs — defaults are the
// original v3 constants, so default output is pixel-identical
grpP8s = "9 · Display — style"
COL_BULL = input.color(#089981, "Bull colour (all bullish drawings)", group = grpP8s)
COL_BEAR = input.color(#f23645, "Bear colour (all bearish drawings)", group = grpP8s)
// READABILITY: box captions used a TINTED bull/bear colour (color.new(c, 10..35))
// at size.tiny — dark red text on a dark red box is unreadable on a dark chart.
// Every box / mark caption now uses one bright colour. v4 had a switch to go
// back to the tinted rendering; it was removed in v5.1a because its OFF
// position is the unreadable one this note is about.
p8TxtCol = input.color(#e8eaed, "Box / caption text colour", group = grpP8s)
p8Gap    = input.float(2.5, "Caption row pitch (% of local range)", step = 0.1, minval = 0.3, maxval = 10, group = grpP8s,
     tooltip = "Vertical distance between the packer's caption rows (MODULE 3D), as a percentage of the recent high-low span — which tracks the price axis, so the pitch stays the same number of PIXELS whether the market is quiet or in free-fall. Earlier versions measured it in ATR and captions drifted far off their candle during a volatile session. LOWER it to pull captions tighter to price (they start to overlap below ~1.5); raise it only if rows visibly touch.")
p8TxtOpt = input.string("Normal", "Box caption size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large"], group = grpP8s,
     tooltip = "v9: ONE size for every box caption, glyph mark, session / trade-line label and POI box. Raise to Large if the text is still hard to read; drop to Small on a busy chart.")

// ◈ DECLUTTER (v5.1) — the why lives in MODULE 3D
grpDC   = "9 · Display — declutter / readability"
dcMode  = input.string("Balanced", "Chart density", options = ["Full", "Balanced", "Clean", "Minimal"], group = grpDC,
     tooltip = "Full: keep every caption. Balanced: drop a non-signal caption when no row is free. Clean: also hide the glyph marks. Minimal: signals, models and traps only.")
dcRows  = input.int(3,     "Max caption rows per side", minval = 2, maxval = 20, group = grpDC,
     tooltip = "Rows the packer may stack before it drops captions. Every extra row pushes its captions further from price, so this is deliberately low: a caption that is not visibly attached to a bar is worse than no caption. Raise it only if too much text is being dropped.")
dcChW   = input.float(2.0, "Room per text character (bars)", step = 0.05, minval = 0.2, maxval = 12.0, group = grpDC,
     tooltip = "A caption reserves length × this many bars of horizontal room. Match it to how far out you trade: ~0.9 at a 200-bar zoom, 2.0 at 430, ~4 at 900. Too low and captions touch; too high and text is dropped.")
dcPillC = input.color(color.new(#0b0f14, 12), "Pill colour", group = grpDC)

mkSize   = size.small
sigSize  = uiSizeOpt == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : uiSizeOpt == "Normal" ? size.normal : uiSizeOpt == "Large" ? size.large : size.small
dashSize = uiDashOpt == "Large" ? size.large : uiDashOpt == "Normal" ? size.normal : size.small
p8TxtSz  = p8TxtOpt == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : p8TxtOpt == "Small" ? size.small : p8TxtOpt == "Large" ? size.large : size.normal
drawSize = p8TxtSz            // v9: one caption-size input for boxes, levels and trade rows
// caption colour — the arguments are the pre-v5.1a tint the call site used to
// ask for, kept so the ~13 call sites do not all have to change

f_recent(int b, int look) => not na(b) and bar_index - b <= look
f_ageTxt(int b) => na(b) ? "—" : str.tostring(bar_index - b) + "b"

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 3
// CORE SERIES + CANDLE ANATOMY
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
atr     = ta.atr(atrLen)
body    = math.abs(close - open)
rng     = high - low
upWick  = high - math.max(open, close)
dnWick  = math.min(open, close) - low
bullBar = close > open
bearBar = close < open
confirmed = barstate.isconfirmed

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 3D
// ◈ DECLUTTER / READABILITY LAYER (v5.1)
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// WHY THIS EXISTS
// v5.0's f_stkY separated only the captions that landed on the SAME bar. But a
// 22-character caption is roughly 20 bars wide at a normal zoom, while every
// engine prints on its own bar — so captions from neighbouring bars drew
// straight through each other and the chart became the unreadable pile in the
// user's screenshot. Per-bar stacking cannot fix a horizontal collision.
//
// This layer is a real 2-D occupancy packer. Each row above (and below) the
// candles holds ONE number: the bar index up to which that row is already
// taken. A caption measures the room it actually needs (longest line length
// × dcChW bars, floored at dcMinW) and claims the first row whose
// reservation has expired; a multi-line caption claims that many consecutive
// rows. When no row is free the caption is DROPPED — except a priority-0
// caption, which is forced onto the least-crowded row so a real signal is
// never silently lost.
//
// PRIORITY  0 = signals, v4 models, liquidity traps, MSS / CHoCH / BOS
//           1 = swing chips, CLS classifier, CISD / IFC / FLIP / BPR / hCHoCH
//           2 = micro glyph marks (◆ ◈ ◇ ✓ ✗ ✕ ▿ ▵ ⇡ ⇣ ◦)
//
// The grid cannot be a plain global: Pine forbids reassigning a global from
// inside a function, but an array's CONTENTS may be mutated. Slots 0..23 are
// the rows above price, slots 24..47 the rows below.
int DC_CAP = 24
int dcMinW = 4                                     // floor for a caption's room
var dcOcc  = array.new<int>(48, -1000000)
dcRowsEff  = math.min(dcRows, DC_CAP)
dcStrict   = dcMode != "Full"                      // drop on collision?
dcMaxPri   = dcMode == "Minimal" ? 0 : dcMode == "Clean" ? 1 : 2

// ZOOM AWARENESS — REMOVED IN v5.2, AND THIS IS THE POINT OF THE REMOVAL.
// v5.1b shipped the viewport auto-scale switched OFF because reading
// chart.left/right_visible_bar_time makes TradingView re-run the WHOLE script
// on every pan and zoom, and this script is already near the 20s runtime cap.
// That defence did not work: Pine evaluates every variable DECLARATION on every
// bar, so dcVisBars read the viewport whether dcAuto was on or not — the
// ternary only gated the USE. The dependency, not the switch, is what triggers
// the re-run, and Pine offers no way to make a dependency conditional. The only
// real fix is to not reference the viewport at all. Caption room is now the
// dcChW input alone (its tooltip carries the per-zoom numbers).

// VERTICAL UNIT: the row pitch is a fraction of the price range on SCREEN, not
// of ATR. ATR is the wrong unit for a screen distance — in the reported 5m gold
// selloff ATR was ~13 points against a ~135-point visible range, so one ATR was
// a tenth of the chart height and a row-3 caption sat ~95 px from its candle;
// in a quiet market the identical code puts it 15 px away. Pine has no
// chart.top_visible_price, so the recent high-low span stands in for the axis —
// it stretches and compresses for exactly the same reason the axis does, which
// is what keeps a row at a constant PIXEL pitch in any volatility regime.
// The window is SHORT (60 bars) on purpose. v5.1c used 250 and the unit came
// out roughly double the axis whenever the chart was zoomed in — 250 bars of
// history reach prices the viewer cannot see — which is what put chips ~86 px
// off their candle. The ATR floor stops a dead-flat stretch collapsing it.
float dcSpan = ta.highest(high, 60) - ta.lowest(low, 60)
float dcUnit = math.max(nz(dcSpan, 0), atr * 8)

// grant a row (or -1 = drop). Reserves the room it hands out.
// The width is str.length of the WHOLE caption — for a two-line caption that
// over-estimates the horizontal room, and that surplus is exactly the padding
// the second line needs vertically, so one number covers both axes.
f_dcRow(int x, bool above, string txt, int pri) =>
    int row = -1
    if pri <= dcMaxPri
        int base = above ? 0 : DC_CAP
        int need = int(math.max(dcMinW, math.round(str.length(txt) * dcChW)))
        if pri == 2
            // TWO BANDS. A priority-2 caption is a single glyph (◆ ◈ ✓ ✗ …)
            // with no text of its own, so it is only meaningful pressed
            // against its candle — distance does not just crowd it, it makes
            // it unreadable. It gets row-0 geometry and its OWN reservation
            // slot (the last one), so a long text caption holding row 0 can
            // never push it off its bar. Slot taken ⇒ dropped, deliberately.
            int g = base + DC_CAP - 1
            if x >= array.get(dcOcc, g)
                row := 0
                array.set(dcOcc, g, x + need)
        else
            // text captions live in rows 1..cap, above the glyph band.
            // Priority 1 gets ROW 1 AND NOTHING ELSE. A swing chip, a CLS
            // verdict or a CISD mark means nothing unless the eye can tie it to
            // one bar, so it is either one pitch off that bar or it is dropped.
            // Only priority 0 — the signals, models and traps — may stack.
            int cap = pri == 1 ? 1 : dcRowsEff
            for r = 1 to cap
                if x >= array.get(dcOcc, base + r)
                    row := r
                    break
            if row < 0 and (pri == 0 or not dcStrict)
                row := cap              // full grid: a signal still prints
            if row >= 0
                array.set(dcOcc, base + row, x + need)
    row

// y for a granted row, measured from the caller's own anchor price.
// Row 0 is the glyph band, pressed against the bar at 0.4 of a pitch; a text
// caption on row N sits exactly N pitches out.
f_dcY(float anchor, bool above, int row) =>
    float off = (row == 0 ? 0.4 : row) * p8Gap / 100 * dcUnit
    above ? anchor + off : anchor - off

// plain-text caption — on a dark pill when dcPill is on, so it stops being
// painted straight onto a candle body
f_bare(int x, float y, string txt, color tc, string sz) =>
    label.new(x, y, txt, yloc = yloc.price,
         style = label.style_label_center, color = dcPillC,
         textcolor = tc, size = sz)


// OVERLAP: handled by the MODULE 3D packer. Every caption asks it for a row,
// turns the granted row into a y with f_dcY against this bar's own high / low,
// and treats -1 as "no room left, drop it" (priority table in MODULE 3D). The
// old per-bar counter could not fix collisions between captions on
// NEIGHBOURING bars, which is what actually piled up on the chart.

// chip = text on a solid pill — readable on any candle background
// pri: 0 signal (never dropped) · 1 structure / classifier · 2 micro mark
f_chipP(bool below, string txt, color bg, color tc, string sz, int pri) =>
    bool above = not below
    int  row   = f_dcRow(bar_index, above, txt, pri)
    if row >= 0
        label.new(bar_index, f_dcY(above ? high : low, above, row), txt, yloc = yloc.price,
             style = below ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down,
             color = bg, textcolor = tc, size = sz)
    row >= 0

f_chip(bool below, string txt, color bg, color tc, string sz) =>
    f_chipP(below, txt, bg, tc, sz, 1)

// OUTPUT-LIMIT FIX (RE10140 "The script creates too many plots (82). The limit
// is 64"): every plotchar consumes one of Pine's 64 output slots — plot,
// plotchar, bgcolor and alertcondition all share that one budget, and the
// script was 18 over. Labels consume none, so all 14 micro-marks moved here.
// Same glyph, same side of the bar, same colour, same closed-bar timing; what
// is lost is the Data Window entry and the status-line row for each mark.
// v5.1: micro-marks are priority 2 — first to be sacrificed when the chart
// runs out of room, and hidden outright at Clean / Minimal density.
f_mark(bool cond, bool above, string ch, color c) =>
    if cond
        int row = f_dcRow(bar_index, above, ch, 2)
        if row >= 0
            f_bare(bar_index, f_dcY(above ? high : low, above, row), ch, c, p8TxtSz)
    cond

// confirmation candles (pin / engulfing)
bullPin    = rng > 0 and dnWick >= 2 * body and upWick <= body and dnWick >= minWickAtr * atr
bearPin    = rng > 0 and upWick >= 2 * body and dnWick <= body and upWick >= minWickAtr * atr
bullEngulf = bullBar and bearBar[1] and close >= open[1] and open <= close[1] and body > body[1]
bearEngulf = bearBar and bullBar[1] and close <= open[1] and open >= close[1] and body > body[1]
bullConfirm = bullPin or bullEngulf
bearConfirm = bearPin or bearEngulf
doji        = rng > 0 and body <= dojiPct / 100 * rng

// ---- CISD engine (V2 FIX-16 preserved) ----------------------------------------
// Strict consecutive delivery: neutral candle (≤10% body) voids both series;
// CISD = displacement-grade close through the origin open of a ≥2-candle
// opposite run. Latched once per run.
cisdNeutral = rng == 0 or body <= CISD_NEUTRAL_PCT * rng
cisdBull    = bullBar and not cisdNeutral
cisdBear    = bearBar and not cisdNeutral
var float bullRunOpen = na
var float bearRunOpen = na
var int   bullRunLen  = 0
var int   bearRunLen  = 0
var bool  cisdDnDone  = false
var bool  cisdUpDone  = false
if confirmed
    if cisdNeutral
        bullRunOpen := na
        bearRunOpen := na
        bullRunLen  := 0
        bearRunLen  := 0
    if cisdBull and not cisdBull[1]
        bullRunOpen := open
        bullRunLen  := 1
        cisdDnDone  := false
    else if cisdBull
        bullRunLen += 1
    if cisdBear and not cisdBear[1]
        bearRunOpen := open
        bearRunLen  := 1
        cisdUpDone  := false
    else if cisdBear
        bearRunLen += 1
cisdDn = confirmed and not na(bullRunOpen) and not cisdDnDone and cisdBear and close < bullRunOpen and bullRunLen >= 2 and body >= BRK_BODY_ATR * atr and close <= low + STRONG_CLOSE_PCT * rng
cisdUp = confirmed and not na(bearRunOpen) and not cisdUpDone and cisdBull and close > bearRunOpen and bearRunLen >= 2 and body >= BRK_BODY_ATR * atr and close >= high - STRONG_CLOSE_PCT * rng
if cisdDn
    cisdDnDone := true
if cisdUp
    cisdUpDone := true
if showCisd and cisdDn
    f_chip(false, "CISD", color.new(COL_BEAR, 55), color.white, mkSize)
if showCisd and cisdUp
    f_chip(true, "CISD", color.new(COL_BULL, 55), color.white, mkSize)

// ---- IFC engine (V2 FIX-17 preserved) -------------------------------------------
// Institutional funding candle: takes a REAL pool (prior IFC_LOOK-bar extreme)
// with meaningful penetration, then closes past the prior midpoint with a
// displacement body and an outer-30% close.
prevMid  = (high[1] + low[1]) / 2
ifcPoolL = ta.lowest(low, IFC_LOOK)[1]
ifcPoolH = ta.highest(high, IFC_LOOK)[1]
ifcBull = low < ifcPoolL and ifcPoolL - low >= NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr and bullBar and close > prevMid and close >= high - STRONG_CLOSE_PCT * rng and body >= BRK_BODY_ATR * atr
ifcBear = high > ifcPoolH and high - ifcPoolH >= NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr and bearBar and close < prevMid and close <= low + STRONG_CLOSE_PCT * rng and body >= BRK_BODY_ATR * atr
if showIFC and ifcBull and confirmed
    f_chip(true, "IFC", color.new(color.gray, 55), color.new(COL_BULL, 0), mkSize)
if showIFC and ifcBear and confirmed
    f_chip(false, "IFC", color.new(color.gray, 55), color.new(COL_BEAR, 0), mkSize)

// execution confirmation used by zones / trendlines / machine
zoneBullConf = bullConfirm or ifcBull or (cisdAsConf and cisdUp)
zoneBearConf = bearConfirm or ifcBear or (cisdAsConf and cisdDn)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 4
// PIVOT ENGINE + EQ POOLS + TRENDLINE ANCHORS
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
ph = ta.pivothigh(high, pivLen, pivLen)
pl = ta.pivotlow(low, pivLen, pivLen)

var float lastRes    = na   // last confirmed swing high → buy-side liquidity
var float lastSup    = na   // last confirmed swing low  → sell-side liquidity
var int   lastResBar = na
var int   lastSupBar = na
var float prevPH     = na
var float prevPL     = na
var bool  resBroken  = false  // once-per-level POKE latch (V2 FIX-2)
var bool  supBroken  = false
var bool  resAccept  = false  // v5 F1: separate once-per-level ACCEPTANCE latch
var bool  supAccept  = false

var int   prevPHBar = na
var int   prevPLBar = na
var bool  tlUpAway  = true   // v5 J1: price is clear of the line, so the next
var bool  tlDnAway  = true   //        approach is a NEW touch, not a continuation
var float tlUpSlope = na
var float tlUpPrice = na
var int   tlUpBar   = na
var int   tlUpTouch = 0
var line  tlUpLn    = na
var float tlDnSlope = na
var float tlDnPrice = na
var int   tlDnBar   = na
var int   tlDnTouch = 0
var line  tlDnLn    = na

var eqhLvls = array.new<float>()
var eqhLns  = array.new<line>()
var eqlLvls = array.new<float>()
var eqlLns  = array.new<line>()

// CE10117 compression: the EQH and EQL pool blocks were mirror copies.
// Same tolerance, same level choice, same cap, same line style.
f_eqPool(bool isHigh, float piv, float prev) =>
    if not na(prev) and math.abs(piv - prev) <= eqTol * atr
        float lvl = isHigh ? math.max(piv, prev) : math.min(piv, prev)
        arrL = isHigh ? eqhLvls : eqlLvls
        arrN = isHigh ? eqhLns  : eqlLns
        array.push(arrL, lvl)
        array.push(arrN, line.new(bar_index - pivLen, lvl, bar_index + 1, lvl,
             color = color.new(isHigh ? COL_BEAR : COL_BULL, showEq ? 25 : 100), style = line.style_dotted, width = 2))
        if array.size(arrL) > MAX_EQ_POOLS
            line.delete(array.get(arrN, 0))
            array.remove(arrN, 0)
            array.remove(arrL, 0)

if not na(ph) and confirmed
    f_eqPool(true, ph, prevPH)
    // trendline: lower high → candidate line off the last two pivot highs.
    // A validated line (≥1 touch) is NOT re-anchored (V2 FIX-19).
    if not na(prevPH) and not na(prevPHBar) and ph < prevPH and (na(tlDnSlope) or tlDnTouch == 0)
        line.delete(tlDnLn)
        tlDnLn    := na
        tlDnSlope := (ph - prevPH) / (bar_index - pivLen - prevPHBar)
        tlDnPrice := ph
        tlDnBar   := bar_index - pivLen
        tlDnTouch := 0
        tlDnAway  := true
        if showTL
            tlDnLn := line.new(prevPHBar, prevPH, bar_index - pivLen, ph,
                 color = color.new(COL_BEAR, 30), width = 2, extend = extend.right,
                 style = line.style_dotted)
    prevPH     := ph
    prevPHBar  := bar_index - pivLen
    lastRes    := ph
    lastResBar := bar_index - pivLen
    resBroken  := false
    resAccept  := false
if not na(pl) and confirmed
    f_eqPool(false, pl, prevPL)
    if not na(prevPL) and not na(prevPLBar) and pl > prevPL and (na(tlUpSlope) or tlUpTouch == 0)
        line.delete(tlUpLn)
        tlUpLn    := na
        tlUpSlope := (pl - prevPL) / (bar_index - pivLen - prevPLBar)
        tlUpPrice := pl
        tlUpBar   := bar_index - pivLen
        tlUpTouch := 0
        tlUpAway  := true
        if showTL
            tlUpLn := line.new(prevPLBar, prevPL, bar_index - pivLen, pl,
                 color = color.new(COL_BULL, 30), width = 2, extend = extend.right,
                 style = line.style_dotted)
    prevPL     := pl
    prevPLBar  := bar_index - pivLen
    lastSup    := pl
    lastSupBar := bar_index - pivLen
    supBroken  := false
    supAccept  := false

// v8: the external pivot state moved up from MODULE 6 — the liquidity engine
// (M5) now treats a sweep of the external swing as an event, not only a target.
// EXTERNAL engine (major swings)
eph = ta.pivothigh(high, extPiv, extPiv)
epl = ta.pivotlow(low, extPiv, extPiv)
var float extRes    = na
var float extSup    = na
var int   extResBar = na
var int   extSupBar = na
var bool  extResBrk = false
var bool  extSupBrk = false
var bool  extResAcc = false   // v5 F1: external acceptance latch
var bool  extSupAcc = false
if not na(eph) and confirmed
    extRes    := eph
    extResBar := bar_index - extPiv
    extResBrk := false
    extResAcc := false
if not na(epl) and confirmed
    extSup    := epl
    extSupBar := bar_index - extPiv
    extSupBrk := false
    extSupAcc := false

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 4B
// SESSION CLOCK (v7) — hoisted above the liquidity engine so a sweep can be
// stamped with the session it happened in and given a session-aware life.
// ONE ladder feeds eligibility (inKZTrd), the score (sesPts), the tier tests,
// the dashboard and the signal metadata. v5.3 kept two models and they
// disagreed: NY PM was a trade window worth 0 session points.
//   4 CORE  London · NY AM · London SB · NY-AM SB   → A+ eligible
//   3 PM    NY PM window · PM SB                     → A eligible, never A+
//   2 ASIA  liquidity build — tracked and scored, never a trade window
//   0       off-hours
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
f_inSes(simple string ses) =>
    not na(time(timeframe.period, ses, "America/New_York"))

inAsia = f_inSes(asiaSes)
inLon  = f_inSes(lonSes)
inNY   = f_inSes(nySes)
inNYpm = f_inSes(nyPmSes)
inSbLO = f_inSes(sbSesLO)
inSbAM = f_inSes(sbSesAM)
inSbPM = f_inSes(sbSesPM)
inSB   = inSbLO or inSbAM or inSbPM
sesQ    = not timeframe.isintraday ? 4 : inLon or inNY or inSbLO or inSbAM ? 4 : inNYpm or inSbPM ? 3 : inAsia ? 2 : 0
sesName = not timeframe.isintraday ? "—" : inSbLO ? "London SB" : inSbAM ? "NY-AM SB" : inSbPM ? "NY-PM SB" : inLon ? "London" : inNY ? "NY AM" : inNYpm ? "NY PM" : inAsia ? "Asia" : "off-hours"
f_sesQTxt(int q) => q == 4 ? "core" : q == 3 ? "PM" : q == 2 ? "Asia" : "off"

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 5
// LIQUIDITY ENGINE — sweeps, quality grades, event classification
// Events per level: FORMING (pivot printed) · SWEPT/RAID (wick through, close
// back inside) · BREAKOUT (confirmed close beyond) · RECLAIMED (close back
// through after a breakout — handled by the once-per-level latch reset).
// Quality: 1 weak · 2 valid · 3 strong · 4 institutional (upgraded later by
// the structure engine when a shift lands while the raid is in play).
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
sslSweep = not na(lastSup) and low < lastSup and close > lastSup
bslSweep = not na(lastRes) and high > lastRes and close < lastRes

f_sweepQual(bool isLow, float lvl) =>
    // graded on the sweeping candle itself; institutional upgrade comes later.
    // v7: takes the LEVEL, so the EQ-pool / PDH-PDL / session writers can grade
    // penetration exactly like a swing sweep (they used to start at 2).
    float pen  = isLow ? lvl - low : high - lvl
    bool  firm = isLow ? close >= lvl + NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr * 0.5 : close <= lvl - NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr * 0.5
    bool  outr = isLow ? close >= low + (1 - STRONG_CLOSE_PCT) * rng : close <= high - (1 - STRONG_CLOSE_PCT) * rng
    bool  disp = body >= BRK_BODY_ATR * atr
    int q = 1
    // v10 (§P4): grade 2 needs BOTH — a firm close back beyond the level AND real
    // penetration. v9 accepted either, so a 0.3-ATR wick closing one tick back
    // inside armed the machine with no rejection evidence at all.
    if firm and pen >= NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr * 0.5
        q := 2
    if q == 2 and outr and disp
        q := 3
    q

var int   lastSslBar  = na
var int   lastBslBar  = na
var float lastSslLvl  = na
var float lastBslLvl  = na
var float lastSslExt  = na   // sweep wick extreme — machine invalidation + SL anchor
var float lastBslExt  = na
var int   lastSslQual = 0
var int   lastBslQual = 0
// v5.3 F3: which bar the quality slot was last written on. The slot is a single
// var per side, so without this the non-swing writers (EQ pool, PDH/PDL, session
// raid) math.max()'d a brand-new poke against a grade an unrelated level earned
// possibly hundreds of bars ago — including the institutional 4 the MSS upgrade
// writes. Same bar = several levels taken by ONE candle, so best-of is right;
// different bar = a new level, so the grade must be recomputed from scratch.
var int   lastSslQBar = na
var int   lastBslQBar = na
// v7: the session the sweep happened in and its clock time. A London raid and a
// 22:00 raid used to be indistinguishable downstream. Stamped once, at the end
// of MODULE 8 after every writer (swing · EQ · PDH/PDL · session) has had its say.
var int   lastSslSes = 0
var int   lastBslSes = 0
var int   lastSslT   = na
var int   lastBslT   = na
// v8 (V8-10): WHAT was taken. 1 internal swing · 2 EQ pool · 3 session H/L ·
// 4 PDH/PDL · 5 external swing · 6 PWH/PWL — best-of when one candle takes several.
var int lastSslType = 0
var int lastBslType = 0
f_liqT(int cur, int qb, int t) => qb == bar_index ? math.max(cur, t) : t
f_liqTxt(int t) => t == 7 ? "brk-trap" : t == 6 ? "PW" : t == 5 ? "ext swing" : t == 4 ? "PD" : t == 3 ? "session" : t == 2 ? "EQ pool" : t == 1 ? "swing" : "—"
// the secondary writers' grade. v7Quality: penetration-graded like a swing sweep
// (f_sweepQual), so a one-tick poke through PDH is WEAK (1) and cannot arm.
// OFF restores v5.3, where these writers started at 2 = minArmQual.
f_qSsl(float lvl) =>
    int q = f_sweepQual(true, lvl)
    lastSslQBar != bar_index ? q : math.max(lastSslQual, q)
f_qBsl(float lvl) =>
    int q = f_sweepQual(false, lvl)
    lastBslQBar != bar_index ? q : math.max(lastBslQual, q)
if sslSweep and confirmed
    lastSslBar  := bar_index
    lastSslLvl  := lastSup
    lastSslExt  := low
    lastSslQual := f_sweepQual(true, lastSup)
    lastSslType := f_liqT(lastSslType, lastSslQBar, 1)
    lastSslQBar := bar_index
if bslSweep and confirmed
    lastBslBar  := bar_index
    lastBslLvl  := lastRes
    lastBslExt  := high
    lastBslQual := f_sweepQual(false, lastRes)
    lastBslType := f_liqT(lastBslType, lastBslQBar, 1)
    lastBslQBar := bar_index

// v10 (§P4): LIQUIDITY EVENT CLASSIFIER. Three outcomes of a raid on a level:
//   SWEEP        wick through + close back on ONE candle — sslSweep / bslSweep,
//                graded by f_sweepQual (rejection evidence required).
//   BREAKOUT     a CLOSE beyond the level = acceptance. The stops are gone, the
//                level is consumed as a target (f_taken) — not a sweep.
//   BREAKOUT TRAP the accepted break FAILS: a close back inside within TRAP_WIN
//                bars. The crowd that traded the break is trapped — the
//                highest-quality liquidity event there is. Written into the
//                sweep memory as type 7 grade 3, so trap → MSS → displacement →
//                shift-leg FVG → first retest arms and grades like any sweep.
// A wick alone is none of these; a break that holds TRAP_WIN bars is genuine.
f_brkTrap(bool isLow, float lvl) =>
    var float bLvl = na      // the level whose break is being judged (held even if the pivot engine moves lastSup meanwhile)
    var int   bBar = na
    var float bExt = na
    var float dLvl = na      // a level whose break was judged GENUINE — never re-armed until the pivot engine replaces it
    bool  trap = false
    float tLvl = na
    float tExt = na
    if confirmed
        if not na(bLvl)
            bExt := isLow ? math.min(bExt, low) : math.max(bExt, high)
            if (isLow ? close > bLvl + NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr * 0.5 : close < bLvl - NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr * 0.5) and bar_index - bBar <= TRAP_WIN
                trap := true                              // v11 (V11-03): the reclaim must be FIRM — the same close-back evidence f_sweepQual demands of a swing sweep, not a one-tick close back inside
                tLvl := bLvl
                tExt := bExt
                bLvl := na
            else if bar_index - bBar > TRAP_WIN
                dLvl := bLvl                              // genuine breakout — held; the level is spent
                bLvl := na
        // v11 (V11-03): only a REAL break can become a trap. v10 armed on any
        // close beyond the level with any body, so a one-tick close through a
        // swing low that closed back the next bar was written into the sweep
        // memory as grade 3 / type 7 — a weaker back door than the swing-sweep
        // grading V10-09 had just tightened. Displacement body OR real penetration.
        else if not na(lvl) and lvl != dLvl and (isLow ? close < lvl : close > lvl) and (body >= BRK_BODY_ATR * atr or (isLow ? lvl - low : high - lvl) >= NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr)
            bLvl := lvl
            bBar := bar_index
            bExt := isLow ? low : high
    [trap, tLvl, tExt]
[trapUpEvt, trapUpLvl, trapUpExt] = f_brkTrap(true,  lastSup)
[trapDnEvt, trapDnLvl, trapDnExt] = f_brkTrap(false, lastRes)
if trapUpEvt
    lastSslBar  := bar_index
    lastSslLvl  := trapUpLvl
    lastSslExt  := trapUpExt
    lastSslQual := lastSslQBar != bar_index ? 3 : math.max(lastSslQual, 3)
    lastSslType := f_liqT(lastSslType, lastSslQBar, 7)
    lastSslQBar := bar_index
if trapDnEvt
    lastBslBar  := bar_index
    lastBslLvl  := trapDnLvl
    lastBslExt  := trapDnExt
    lastBslQual := lastBslQBar != bar_index ? 3 : math.max(lastBslQual, 3)
    lastBslType := f_liqT(lastBslType, lastBslQBar, 7)
    lastBslQBar := bar_index

// EQ pools: Judas sweep (close back inside) vs real break (pool consumed)
eqhSwept = false
eqlSwept = false
if array.size(eqhLvls) > 0
    for i = array.size(eqhLvls) - 1 to 0
        lvl = array.get(eqhLvls, i)
        if high > lvl and confirmed
            if close < lvl
                eqhSwept    := true
                lastBslBar  := bar_index
                lastBslLvl  := lvl
                lastBslExt  := high
                lastBslQual := f_qBsl(lvl)                            // v5.3 F3 · v7 graded
                lastBslType := f_liqT(lastBslType, lastBslQBar, 2)
                lastBslQBar := bar_index
            line.delete(array.get(eqhLns, i))
            array.remove(eqhLns, i)
            array.remove(eqhLvls, i)
if array.size(eqlLvls) > 0
    for i = array.size(eqlLvls) - 1 to 0
        lvl = array.get(eqlLvls, i)
        if low < lvl and confirmed
            if close > lvl
                eqlSwept    := true
                lastSslBar  := bar_index
                lastSslLvl  := lvl
                lastSslExt  := low
                lastSslQual := f_qSsl(lvl)                            // v5.3 F3 · v7 graded
                lastSslType := f_liqT(lastSslType, lastSslQBar, 2)
                lastSslQBar := bar_index
            line.delete(array.get(eqlLns, i))
            array.remove(eqlLns, i)
            array.remove(eqlLvls, i)

// v8 (V8-00): EVERY sweep writer runs above this line. In v7 the PDH/PDL and
// session-raid writers sat BELOW the sslInPlay snapshot (and the session ones in
// MODULE 8), so on a pure PDL / session-low raid bar sslInPlay was still false
// and the machine's arm test `sslInPlay and lastSslBar == bar_index` could
// never be true — the v7 A2 fix was dead on arrival. Blocks relocated verbatim.
// ---- previous day / week high–low (external liquidity map) ---------------------
[pdh, pdl] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", [high[1], low[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[pwh, pwl] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "W", [high[1], low[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
// v9 (§7): LIQUIDITY LIFECYCLE for the target map. FRESH → SWEPT / BROKEN →
// CONSUMED: once price has traded through a level (wick or close) the stops
// that rested there are gone, so it is no longer a valid TAKE-PROFIT target —
// the RR gate, the clean-path test and the TP ladder skip it. A level is
// fresh again only when it is REPLACED (new pivot · new day · new week).
f_taken(float lvl, bool isHi) =>
    var bool t = false
    if lvl != lvl[1]
        t := false
    if confirmed and not na(lvl) and (isHi ? high > lvl : low < lvl)
        t := true
    t
resTaken    = f_taken(lastRes, true)
supTaken    = f_taken(lastSup, false)
extResTaken = f_taken(extRes, true)
extSupTaken = f_taken(extSup, false)
pdhTaken    = f_taken(pdh, true)
pdlTaken    = f_taken(pdl, false)
pwhTaken    = f_taken(pwh, true)
pwlTaken    = f_taken(pwl, false)
pdhSweep = confirmed and not na(pdh) and high > pdh and close < pdh
pdlSweep = confirmed and not na(pdl) and low  < pdl and close > pdl
// v8 (V8-10): PDH/PDL, the external swing and the previous-week levels share one
// writer per side — same penetration grade, same held / failed rule; the highest
// level type names the level when one candle takes several.
extLoSweep = confirmed and not na(extSup) and low < extSup and close > extSup
extHiSweep = confirmed and not na(extRes) and high > extRes and close < extRes
pwlSweep   = confirmed and not na(pwl) and low < pwl and close > pwl
pwhSweep   = confirmed and not na(pwh) and high > pwh and close < pwh
if pdlSweep or extLoSweep or pwlSweep
    lastSslBar  := bar_index
    lastSslLvl  := pwlSweep ? pwl : extLoSweep ? extSup : pdl
    lastSslExt  := low
    lastSslQual := f_qSsl(lastSslLvl)
    lastSslType := f_liqT(lastSslType, lastSslQBar, pwlSweep ? 6 : extLoSweep ? 5 : 4)
    lastSslQBar := bar_index
if pdhSweep or extHiSweep or pwhSweep
    lastBslBar  := bar_index
    lastBslLvl  := pwhSweep ? pwh : extHiSweep ? extRes : pdh
    lastBslExt  := high
    lastBslQual := f_qBsl(lastBslLvl)
    lastBslType := f_liqT(lastBslType, lastBslQBar, pwhSweep ? 6 : extHiSweep ? 5 : 4)
    lastBslQBar := bar_index

// per-session H/L tracking (V2 FIX-18 RAID/BREAK split preserved), returned
// separately per session so Asia ≠ London ≠ NY in the machine and the score
f_sesTrack(bool active, string tag, color col) =>
    var float hi   = na
    var float lo   = na
    var line  hiLn = na
    var line  loLn = na
    var label hiLb = na
    var label loLb = na
    var bool  hiSwept = false
    var bool  loSwept = false
    if active
        if not active[1]
            hi := high
            lo := low
        else
            hi := math.max(hi, high)
            lo := math.min(lo, low)
    // v5.2 V4: the frozen levels are now STATE, not geometry read back out of a
    // drawing. hiLvl used to be line.get_y1(hiLn), so with "Session high / low
    // liquidity lines" switched OFF no line existed, no raid was ever detected,
    // and the London / NY raid feed into the sweep memory (ARCH-8) plus the
    // engineered-pool memory went silent — a DISPLAY toggle was disabling an
    // ENGINE. Levels are captured unconditionally; only the drawing is gated.
    // Side benefit: six line.get_y1 reads per bar removed from the hot path.
    var float hiLvl = na
    var float loLvl = na
    if not active and active[1] and confirmed and not na(hi)
        hiLvl   := hi
        loLvl   := lo
        hiSwept := false
        loSwept := false
        if showSesHL
            line.delete(hiLn)
            line.delete(loLn)
            label.delete(hiLb)
            label.delete(loLb)
            hiLn := line.new(bar_index, hi, bar_index + 1, hi, color = color.new(col, 35), extend = extend.right)
            loLn := line.new(bar_index, lo, bar_index + 1, lo, color = color.new(col, 35), extend = extend.right)
            hiLb := label.new(bar_index, hi, tag + " H", style = label.style_label_left,
                 color = color.new(col, 20), textcolor = color.white, size = drawSize)
            loLb := label.new(bar_index, lo, tag + " L", style = label.style_label_left,
                 color = color.new(col, 20), textcolor = color.white, size = drawSize)
    bool hiRaid = false
    bool loRaid = false
    bool hiBrk  = false
    bool loBrk  = false
    if not active and confirmed
        if not na(hiLvl) and not hiSwept and high > hiLvl
            hiSwept := true
            hiBrk   := close > hiLvl
            hiRaid  := not hiBrk
            if not na(hiLn)
                line.set_extend(hiLn, extend.none)
                line.set_x2(hiLn, bar_index)
                line.set_style(hiLn, hiRaid ? line.style_dashed : line.style_dotted)
                label.set_text(hiLb, tag + (hiRaid ? " H raided" : " H broken"))
        if not na(loLvl) and not loSwept and low < loLvl
            loSwept := true
            loBrk   := close < loLvl
            loRaid  := not loBrk
            if not na(loLn)
                line.set_extend(loLn, extend.none)
                line.set_x2(loLn, bar_index)
                line.set_style(loLn, loRaid ? line.style_dashed : line.style_dotted)
                label.set_text(loLb, tag + (loRaid ? " L raided" : " L broken"))
    [hiRaid, loRaid, hiBrk, loBrk, hiLvl, loLvl]

[asiaHiSw, asiaLoSw, asiaHiBk, asiaLoBk, asiaHiLvl, asiaLoLvl] = f_sesTrack(inAsia and timeframe.isintraday, "Asia", color.purple)
[lonHiSw,  lonLoSw,  lonHiBk,  lonLoBk,  lonHiLvl,  lonLoLvl]  = f_sesTrack(inLon and timeframe.isintraday,  "Lon",  color.blue)
[nyHiSw,   nyLoSw,   nyHiBk,   nyLoBk,   nyHiLvl,   nyLoLvl]   = f_sesTrack(inNY and timeframe.isintraday,   "NY",   color.orange)
sesHiSwept = asiaHiSw or lonHiSw or nyHiSw
sesLoSwept = asiaLoSw or lonLoSw or nyLoSw
sesHiBroke = asiaHiBk or lonHiBk or nyHiBk
sesLoBroke = asiaLoBk or lonLoBk or nyLoBk

// ARCH-8 as REWIRED in v7 (S2): WHICH raid arms is decided by WHEN it happens,
// not whose level it is. v5.3 armed on lonLoSw / nyLoSw — but f_sesTrack only
// reports a raid once its session is OVER, so "London low raided" meant raided
// during NY and "NY low raided" meant raided in the PM or in Asia. The Asia-
// range raid — the event London and NY are supposed to trade — reached only the
// score-only pool memory below. Now any tracked session level taken INSIDE a
// trade window (sesQ ≥ 3) arms with a penetration grade; a raid outside one
// (Asia hours) stays score-only. v7SesModel OFF restores the v5.3 wiring.
sesArmLo = (asiaLoSw or lonLoSw or nyLoSw) and sesQ >= 3
sesArmHi = (asiaHiSw or lonHiSw or nyHiSw) and sesQ >= 3
if confirmed
    if sesArmLo
        lastSslBar  := bar_index
        lastSslLvl  := asiaLoSw ? asiaLoLvl : lonLoSw ? lonLoLvl : nyLoLvl
        lastSslExt  := low
        lastSslQual := f_qSsl(lastSslLvl)                             // v5.3 F3 · v7 graded
        lastSslType := f_liqT(lastSslType, lastSslQBar, 3)
        lastSslQBar := bar_index
    if sesArmHi
        lastBslBar  := bar_index
        lastBslLvl  := asiaHiSw ? asiaHiLvl : lonHiSw ? lonHiLvl : nyHiLvl
        lastBslExt  := high
        lastBslQual := f_qBsl(lastBslLvl)                             // v5.3 F3 · v7 graded
        lastBslType := f_liqT(lastBslType, lastBslQBar, 3)
        lastBslQBar := bar_index
// v7: stamp the sweep memory with the session and clock time of whichever writer
// (swing · EQ · PDH/PDL · session raid) owns the slot on this bar.
if confirmed and lastSslBar == bar_index
    lastSslSes := sesQ
    lastSslT   := time
if confirmed and lastBslBar == bar_index
    lastBslSes := sesQ
    lastBslT   := time

// v7SesModel: a sweep from a CORE session (London / NY AM) stays in play while
// price is still inside a trade window and less than sweepMaxHrs of clock time
// has passed — a 03:00 London raid is still the narrative at 09:30, on 1M as on
// 15M. The bar count alone made that 15 minutes on 1M and 15 hours on H1. The
// held test, the 3-ATR proximity and the anti-chase distance still apply.
sslSesLife = sweepMaxHrs > 0 and lastSslSes >= 4 and sesQ >= 3 and not na(lastSslT) and time - lastSslT <= sweepMaxHrs * 3600000
bslSesLife = sweepMaxHrs > 0 and lastBslSes >= 4 and sesQ >= 3 and not na(lastBslT) and time - lastBslT <= sweepMaxHrs * 3600000
recentSsl = f_recent(lastSslBar, sweepLook) or sslSesLife
recentBsl = f_recent(lastBslBar, sweepLook) or bslSesLife
// v5 I1: "in play" also requires the raid to still be intact. A close beyond
// the sweep wick means price ACCEPTED through the level - the raid failed and
// the context is now the opposite one. Without this the proximity test alone
// (close - level <= 3 ATR) stayed true while price traded far BELOW the swept
// low, and a failed raid kept scoring as bullish liquidity for sweepLook bars.
sslHeld   = na(lastSslExt) or close > lastSslExt
bslHeld   = na(lastBslExt) or close < lastBslExt
sslInPlay = recentSsl and not na(lastSslLvl) and close - lastSslLvl <= SWEEP_CTX_ATR * atr and sslHeld
bslInPlay = recentBsl and not na(lastBslLvl) and lastBslLvl - close <= SWEEP_CTX_ATR * atr and bslHeld


// once-per-level latches — v5 F1 splits POKE from ACCEPTANCE.
//   brokeUp / brokeDn  = FIRST close beyond the level, any body. Drives the
//     breakout classifier, the weak-poke trap patterns, the CPC memory and
//     key-level condition 3 — all of which are ABOUT weak breaks.
//   accBrokeUp / accBrokeDn = first DISPLACEMENT-grade close beyond it. Only
//     this feeds the structure engine. In v4 both shared one latch, so a weak
//     nudge through a level consumed it and the genuine break that came two
//     bars later could never register a BOS / CHoCH / MSS.
brokeUp = not na(lastRes) and not resBroken and close > lastRes
brokeDn = not na(lastSup) and not supBroken and close < lastSup
accBrokeUp = not na(lastRes) and not resAccept and close > lastRes and body >= structDisp * atr
accBrokeDn = not na(lastSup) and not supAccept and close < lastSup and body >= structDisp * atr
if brokeUp and confirmed
    resBroken := true
if brokeDn and confirmed
    supBroken := true
if accBrokeUp and confirmed
    resAccept := true
if accBrokeDn and confirmed
    supAccept := true

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 6
// STRUCTURE — protected-swing engine (internal + external) + MSS grading
// BOS   = displaced continuation close through the latest trend pivot.
// CHoCH = displaced close through the PROTECTED swing (origin of the leg
//         that produced the last BOS). Minor pullback runs = inducement.
// MSS   = CHoCH landing while a quality (≥2) sweep is in play — liquidity
//         event + displacement + meaningful shift. Stronger than CHoCH alone.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// v9 (§4): the protected swing is the LAST CONFIRMED PIVOT of the leg — the
// last HL before a bullish BOS, the last LH before a bearish one — not the
// leg's cumulative lowest low / highest high. v8 used the leg extreme: with
// two pullbacks in one leg the deeper, EARLIER low stayed protected and the
// CHoCH fired late. Fallback = the leg extreme when no pivot has confirmed
// inside the leg, or when the extreme printed AFTER the last pivot (a fresh
// unconfirmed dip is the true origin of the breaking leg). Pivots are the
// engine's own length (5 internal · 12 external), so noise is filtered.
f_structure(bool upBrk, bool dnBrk, float pivL, float pivH, int pLen) =>
    var int   dir    = 0
    var float protLo = na
    var float protHi = na
    var float legLo  = na
    var float legHi  = na
    var int   legLoB = na
    var int   legHiB = na
    var int   legSt  = 0
    var float legPl  = na
    var float legPh  = na
    var int   legPlB = na
    var int   legPhB = na
    bool bosU = false
    bool bosD = false
    bool chU  = false
    bool chD  = false
    if na(legLo) or low < legLo
        legLo  := low
        legLoB := bar_index
    if na(legHi) or high > legHi
        legHi  := high
        legHiB := bar_index
    if not na(pivL) and bar_index - pLen >= legSt
        legPl  := pivL
        legPlB := bar_index - pLen
    if not na(pivH) and bar_index - pLen >= legSt
        legPh  := pivH
        legPhB := bar_index - pLen
    float swLo = not na(legPl) and legPlB > legLoB ? legPl : legLo
    float swHi = not na(legPh) and legPhB > legHiB ? legPh : legHi
    if confirmed and body >= structDisp * atr
        if dir == 1
            if upBrk
                bosU   := true
                protLo := swLo
            else if not na(protLo) and close < protLo
                chD    := true
                dir    := -1
                protHi := swHi
                protLo := na
        else if dir == -1
            if dnBrk
                bosD   := true
                protHi := swHi
            else if not na(protHi) and close > protHi
                chU    := true
                dir    := 1
                protLo := swLo
                protHi := na
        else if upBrk
            bosU   := true
            dir    := 1
            protLo := swLo
        else if dnBrk
            bosD   := true
            dir    := -1
            protHi := swHi
        if bosU or bosD or chU or chD
            legLo  := low
            legHi  := high
            legLoB := bar_index
            legHiB := bar_index
            legSt  := bar_index
            legPl  := na
            legPh  := na
    [dir, bosU, bosD, chU, chD, protLo, protHi]

[msDir, bosUp, bosDn, chochUp, chochDn, protLowI, protHighI] = f_structure(accBrokeUp, accBrokeDn, pl, ph, pivLen)

// EXTERNAL engine (major swings) — pivots and levels live in MODULE 4 since v8
eBrokeUp = not na(extRes) and not extResBrk and close > extRes
eBrokeDn = not na(extSup) and not extSupBrk and close < extSup
eAccUp = not na(extRes) and not extResAcc and close > extRes and body >= structDisp * atr
eAccDn = not na(extSup) and not extSupAcc and close < extSup and body >= structDisp * atr
if eBrokeUp and confirmed
    extResBrk := true
if eBrokeDn and confirmed
    extSupBrk := true
if eAccUp and confirmed
    extResAcc := true
if eAccDn and confirmed
    extSupAcc := true
[extDir, eBosUp, eBosDn, eChochUp, eChochDn, protLowE, protHighE] = f_structure(eAccUp, eAccDn, epl, eph, extPiv)

// v9 (§12): DISPLACEMENT GRADE of this candle in direction isL —
//   0 normal · 1 expansion (body ≥ 0.5 ATR) · 2 displacement (body ≥ dispFactor
//   × ATR, body ≥ 60 % of range, outer-30 % close) · 3 strong institutional
//   (2 + it created an FVG, or body ≥ 1.5 × the displacement threshold, or a
//   second expansion candle in a row). One candle-size test is no longer the
//   whole definition. Feeds the MSS grade, the machine memory and the journal.
f_dispQ(bool isL) =>
    int q = (isL ? bullBar : bearBar) and body >= BRK_BODY_ATR * atr ? 1 : 0
    if q == 1 and body >= dispFactor * atr and rng > 0 and body / rng >= 0.6 and (isL ? close >= high - STRONG_CLOSE_PCT * rng : close <= low + STRONG_CLOSE_PCT * rng)
        q := 2
    if q == 2 and ((isL ? low > high[2] : high < low[2]) or body >= 1.5 * dispFactor * atr or ((isL ? bullBar[1] : bearBar[1]) and body[1] >= BRK_BODY_ATR * atr))
        q := 3
    q
dispQUp = f_dispQ(true)
dispQDn = f_dispQ(false)

// MSS classification (ARCH-4): CHoCH + a quality sweep still in play.
// The same event also upgrades that sweep to INSTITUTIONAL grade (quality 4).
mssUp = eChochUp and sslInPlay and lastSslQual >= 2
mssDn = eChochDn and bslInPlay and lastBslQual >= 2
// v5.3 F3: the institutional grade is earned on THIS candle, so it claims the
// slot for this bar — a same-bar session raid keeps it, a new level later does not.
// v9 (§11): MSS GRADE — 1 external CHoCH with no quality sweep in play ·
// 2 MSS (external CHoCH + quality sweep) · 3 HIGH-QUALITY MSS (2 + the shift
// candle itself is displacement-grade). An internal CHoCH is never an MSS.
// The machine needs ≥ 2 for tier A and 3 for A+.
mssQUp = mssUp ? (dispQUp >= 2 ? 3 : 2) : eChochUp ? 1 : 0
mssQDn = mssDn ? (dispQDn >= 2 ? 3 : 2) : eChochDn ? 1 : 0
if mssUp and confirmed
    lastSslQual := 4
    lastSslQBar := bar_index
if mssDn and confirmed
    lastBslQual := 4
    lastBslQBar := bar_index

// live trigger memory
var int lastChUpBar   = na
var int lastChDnBar   = na
var int lastBosUpBar  = na
var int lastBosDnBar  = na
var int lastMssUpBar  = na
var int lastMssDnBar  = na
var int lastCisdUpBar = na
var int lastCisdDnBar = na
var int lastDispUpBar = na
var int lastDispDnBar = na
var float lastDispUpLo = na   // v8: origin of the last displacement candle — anti-chase
var float lastDispDnHi = na
if confirmed
    if chochUp or eChochUp
        lastChUpBar := bar_index
    if chochDn or eChochDn
        lastChDnBar := bar_index
    if bosUp or eBosUp
        lastBosUpBar := bar_index
    if bosDn or eBosDn
        lastBosDnBar := bar_index
    if mssUp
        lastMssUpBar := bar_index
    if mssDn
        lastMssDnBar := bar_index
    if cisdUp
        lastCisdUpBar := bar_index
    if cisdDn
        lastCisdDnBar := bar_index
    if bullBar and body >= dispFactor * atr
        lastDispUpBar := bar_index
        lastDispUpLo  := low
    if bearBar and body >= dispFactor * atr
        lastDispDnBar := bar_index
        lastDispDnHi  := high
recentChUp   = f_recent(lastChUpBar, TRIG_LOOK)
recentChDn   = f_recent(lastChDnBar, TRIG_LOOK)
recentBosUp  = f_recent(lastBosUpBar, TRIG_LOOK)
recentBosDn  = f_recent(lastBosDnBar, TRIG_LOOK)
recentMssUp  = f_recent(lastMssUpBar, TRIG_LOOK)
recentMssDn  = f_recent(lastMssDnBar, TRIG_LOOK)
recentCisdUp = f_recent(lastCisdUpBar, TRIG_LOOK)
recentCisdDn = f_recent(lastCisdDnBar, TRIG_LOOK)
recentDispUp = f_recent(lastDispUpBar, 3)
recentDispDn = f_recent(lastDispDnBar, 3)
// v7: a displacement body (dispFactor, not the 0.5-ATR structural minimum)
// inside the same window a shift stays a live trigger — the tier-A test
dispUpLive   = f_recent(lastDispUpBar, TRIG_LOOK)
dispDnLive   = f_recent(lastDispDnBar, TRIG_LOOK)
recentStructUp = recentChUp or recentBosUp
recentStructDn = recentChDn or recentBosDn

// structure marks: MSS > CHoCH > BOS; internal marks muted
if showStruct and confirmed
    // v5.1: external structure is priority 0 (a real event — never dropped);
    // the 5-bar internal ibos / iCHoCH noise is priority 2 (dropped first)
    if mssUp
        f_chipP(true, "MSS", color.new(COL_BULL, 0), color.white, sigSize, 0)
    else if eChochUp
        f_chipP(true, "CHoCH", color.new(COL_BULL, 15), color.white, sigSize, 0)
    else if eBosUp
        f_chipP(true, "BOS", color.new(COL_BULL, 15), color.white, sigSize, 0)
    else if chochUp or bosUp
        f_chipP(true, chochUp ? "iCHoCH" : "ibos", color.new(color.gray, 60), color.new(COL_BULL, 0), size.tiny, 2)
    if mssDn
        f_chipP(false, "MSS", color.new(COL_BEAR, 0), color.white, sigSize, 0)
    else if eChochDn
        f_chipP(false, "CHoCH", color.new(COL_BEAR, 15), color.white, sigSize, 0)
    else if eBosDn
        f_chipP(false, "BOS", color.new(COL_BEAR, 15), color.white, sigSize, 0)
    else if chochDn or bosDn
        f_chipP(false, chochDn ? "iCHoCH" : "ibos", color.new(color.gray, 60), color.new(COL_BEAR, 0), size.tiny, 2)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 7
// HTF DATA — MTF bias (last CLOSED candle only)
// v8 (V8-03): every request.security site now uses lookahead_on WITH the [1]
// offset — the Pine docs' non-repainting idiom. lookahead_off + [1] was stable
// in realtime but on HISTORICAL bars returned the value of the bar BEFORE the
// last confirmed HTF bar (N−2), so PDH/PDL, the HTF CRT/TBS, the HTF POI and
// the bias were one full HTF bar staler on the chart you validate on than in
// the live behaviour. Nothing unoffset is returned, so no future value leaks.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
f_bias(simple string tf) =>
    request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf, nz((close > ta.ema(close, biasLen) ? 1 : -1)[1], 0),
         lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

// v7: three datasets instead of five. b5 / b15 / b240 were read only by the
// dashboard row and the biasFilter switch; the filter TF is fetched directly
// and the row shows filter · 1H · D. request.security series share the 64-slot
// output budget with plots and alerts (OUTPUT NOTE) — every dataset counts.
bFilt = f_bias(biasFilter == "Off" ? "60" : biasFilter)
b60   = f_bias("60")
bD    = f_bias("D")
filtBias = biasFilter == "Off" ? 0 : bFilt
htfB = filtBias != 0 ? filtBias : b60
// v8 (V8-17): optional correlated symbol — its filter-TF bias, sign-adjusted so
// +1 supports longs and −1 supports shorts. Blank symbol = off (own ticker fetched, ignored).
corrRaw = request.security(v8CorrSym == "" ? syminfo.tickerid : v8CorrSym, biasFilter == "Off" ? "60" : biasFilter,
     nz((close > ta.ema(close, biasLen) ? 1 : -1)[1], 0), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
corrB = v8CorrSym == "" ? 0 : v8CorrInv ? -corrRaw : corrRaw

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 8
// SESSION ENGINE — killzones, volatility windows, per-session liquidity
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// v7: f_inSes and the session booleans moved UP to MODULE 4B — the liquidity
// engine (M5) needs sesQ to stamp a sweep with its session and to give a
// core-session sweep a clock-based life.
// v5.3 F5: TRACKING windows and TRADE windows are not the same set. Asia is
// where the range that London and NY raid is BUILT — it has to keep its session
// H/L tracking, its raid feed into the sweep memory and its dashboard row — but
// the script's own sesPts model rates it 2/5 against 5/5 for London / NY / SB,
// and inKZ let entries through it anyway. inKZ stays the tracking union;
// inKZTrd is what a killzone-filtered entry now has to satisfy.
inKZTrd = inLon or inNY or inNYpm or inSB
kzOK    = not useKZ or not timeframe.isintraday or inKZTrd

inNews  = f_inSes(news1Ses) or f_inSes(news2Ses) or f_inSes(news3Ses)
// v10 (V10-14): PRE-NEWS — the clock minutes before a window's START, parsed
// from the session string ("0825-0845:23456" → 08:25, days 2–6), NY clock.
f_preNews(simple string s) =>
    bool ok = false
    if newsPreMin > 0 and str.length(s) >= 9
        int    st   = int(str.tonumber(str.substring(s, 0, 2))) * 60 + int(str.tonumber(str.substring(s, 2, 4)))
        string days = str.contains(s, ":") ? str.substring(s, str.pos(s, ":") + 1) : "1234567"
        int    nowM = hour(time, "America/New_York") * 60 + minute(time, "America/New_York")
        ok := str.contains(days, str.tostring(dayofweek(time, "America/New_York"))) and nowM >= st - newsPreMin and nowM < st
    ok
inPreNews = timeframe.isintraday and (f_preNews(news1Ses) or f_preNews(news2Ses) or f_preNews(news3Ses))
var int newsEndT = na
if timeframe.isintraday and not inNews and inNews[1]
    newsEndT := time
float sinceNews = na(newsEndT) ? na : time - newsEndT
// v10 five states — 0 NORMAL · 1 NEWS RISK (inside a window) · 3 PRE-NEWS
// (newsPreMin before) · 4 POST-NEWS REPRICE (first newsRepMin after: the first
// impulse is repricing, nothing enters) · 2 POST-NEWS CONFIRMATION (then until
// newsPostMin: the machine may enter, engines need the whole narrative, no A+).
// 1 / 3 / 4 block entries; the Silver-Bullet exception (v5.3 F6) lifts all three.
newsRep   = newsRepMin > 0 and timeframe.isintraday and not inNews and not na(sinceNews) and sinceNews <= newsRepMin * 60000
newsPost  = newsPostMin > 0 and timeframe.isintraday and not inNews and not newsRep and not na(sinceNews) and sinceNews <= newsPostMin * 60000
newsState = not useNews or not timeframe.isintraday ? 0 : inNews ? 1 : newsRep ? 4 : inPreNews ? 3 : newsPost ? 2 : 0
newsOK    = not useNews or not timeframe.isintraday or (not inNews and not inPreNews and not newsRep) or (not newsVetoSb and inSB)


// v8: the per-session H/L tracker, the raid writers and the session/time stamp
// moved UP into MODULE 5 (V8-00) — they must precede the in-play snapshot.
// engineered-liquidity memory (EQ pools + ANY session raid) — score only
var int   lastEngLoBar = na
var int   lastEngHiBar = na
var float lastEngLoExt = na      // v5 I2: origin wick, for the held / failed test
var float lastEngHiExt = na
if confirmed
    if eqlSwept or sesLoSwept or pdlSweep or extLoSweep or pwlSweep
        lastEngLoBar := bar_index
        lastEngLoExt := low
    if eqhSwept or sesHiSwept or pdhSweep or extHiSweep or pwhSweep
        lastEngHiBar := bar_index
        lastEngHiExt := high
recentEngLo = f_recent(lastEngLoBar, sweepLook) and (na(lastEngLoExt) or close > lastEngLoExt)
recentEngHi = f_recent(lastEngHiBar, sweepLook) and (na(lastEngHiExt) or close < lastEngHiExt)

// ---- opening prices (00:00 / 08:30 lines): removed in v7 — display only,
// ~130 raw tokens, paid for the arbiter. The 08:30 slot is still a scheduled
// volatility window (news1Ses) and midnight still closes the Asia session.

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 9
// HTF ENGINES — CRT + Turtle soup + FVG POI (closed HTF candles only)
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
f_autoHtf() =>
    switch timeframe.period
        "1"   => "15"
        "2"   => "30"
        "3"   => "30"
        "5"   => "60"
        "10"  => "120"
        "15"  => "240"
        "30"  => "240"
        "60"  => "D"
        "120" => "D"
        "240" => "D"
        "D"   => "W"
        "W"   => "M"
        => "D"
htfTf   = htfSel == "Auto" ? f_autoHtf() : htfSel
// v9 (§6): the HTF must be HIGHER than the chart. "Chart 1H, HTF 15m" is a
// configuration error, not a context: every signal is blocked (longCtx /
// shortCtx) and the dashboard title + Verdict row say why. Same test for the
// bias-filter timeframe. Nothing is silently treated as "HTF".
htfOK   = timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf) > timeframe.in_seconds()
biasOK  = biasFilter == "Off" or timeframe.in_seconds(biasFilter == "Off" ? "60" : biasFilter) > timeframe.in_seconds()
cfgOK   = htfOK and biasOK
htfLive = htfOK

// turtle-soup age note (audited, V2 logic KEPT): ta.lowestbars/highestbars
// return a NON-POSITIVE offset (0 = this bar, -k = k bars back). Taking the
// value on the [1] series and negating: -offset[1] + 1 = positive age of the
// extreme in bars as seen from the CURRENT bar (≥ 1). No sign bug. v3 adds
// the MAX age gate: fading a months-old level is not a turtle soup.
f_tbsAgeOk(int age) => age >= tbsAgeMin and (tbsAgeMax == 0 or age <= tbsAgeMax)

f_crtTbsHtf() =>
    _atr  = ta.atr(atrLen)
    _rng  = high - low
    _body = math.abs(close - open)
    _bull = close > open
    _bear = close < open
    _c1big = _rng[2] >= crtRangeAtr * _atr
    _crtB  = _c1big and low[1] < low[2] and close[1] > low[2] and close[1] < high[2] and low[2] - low[1] >= minWickAtr * _atr and _bull and close > high[1] and _body >= crtDispAtr * _atr
    _crtS  = _c1big and high[1] > high[2] and close[1] < high[2] and close[1] > low[2] and high[1] - high[2] >= minWickAtr * _atr and _bear and close < low[1] and _body >= crtDispAtr * _atr
    _tl    = ta.lowest(low, tbsLen)[1]
    _th    = ta.highest(high, tbsLen)[1]
    _loAge = -ta.lowestbars(low, tbsLen)[1] + 1
    _hiAge = -ta.highestbars(high, tbsLen)[1] + 1
    _tbsB  = low < _tl and close > _tl and _bull and f_tbsAgeOk(_loAge) and close >= low + 0.5 * _rng
    _tbsS  = high > _th and close < _th and _bear and f_tbsAgeOk(_hiAge) and close <= high - 0.5 * _rng
    // v8: HTF rolling structure — HH+HL over the last 10 HTF bars = 1, LH+LL = −1
    bool _hh = ta.highest(high, 10) > ta.highest(high, 10)[10]
    bool _hl = ta.lowest(low, 10)   > ta.lowest(low, 10)[10]
    bool _lh = ta.highest(high, 10) < ta.highest(high, 10)[10]
    bool _ll = ta.lowest(low, 10)   < ta.lowest(low, 10)[10]
    int  _sd = _hh and _hl ? 1 : _lh and _ll ? -1 : 0
    // v10 (V10-16): the structural stop of the pattern — the raid candle's
    // extreme (CRT candle 2 / the turtle-soup candle) — instead of a 2-bar
    // chart-TF fallback that made the RR look excellent.
    float _slL = math.min(low, low[1])
    float _slS = math.max(high, high[1])
    [_crtB[1], _crtS[1], _tbsB[1], _tbsS[1], time[1], _sd[1], _slL[1], _slS[1]]

[hCrtB, hCrtS, hTbsB, hTbsS, hT, hStruct, hSlL, hSlS] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTf, f_crtTbsHtf(),
     lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

newHtfBar    = htfLive and not na(hT) and hT != nz(hT[1])
sigHCrtLong  = useHtfCrt and confirmed and newHtfBar and hCrtB
sigHCrtShort = useHtfCrt and confirmed and newHtfBar and hCrtS
sigHTbsLong  = useHtfCrt and confirmed and newHtfBar and hTbsB
sigHTbsShort = useHtfCrt and confirmed and newHtfBar and hTbsS

// HTF FVG POI with freshness (V2 FIX-15 preserved)
f_htfPoi() =>
    var float bTop = na
    var float bBot = na
    var int   bBar = na
    var int   bIn  = 0
    var float sTop = na
    var float sBot = na
    var int   sBar = na
    var int   sIn  = 0
    if low > high[2]
        bTop := low
        bBot := high[2]
        bBar := bar_index
        bIn  := 0
    if high < low[2]
        sBot := high
        sTop := low[2]
        sBar := bar_index
        sIn  := 0
    if not na(bTop) and bar_index > bBar and low <= bTop
        bIn += 1
    if not na(sTop) and bar_index > sBar and high >= sBot
        sIn += 1
    if not na(bBot) and (close < bBot or bar_index - bBar > hPoiMaxAge or bIn > hPoiMaxTouch)
        bTop := na
        bBot := na
    if not na(sTop) and (close > sTop or bar_index - sBar > hPoiMaxAge or sIn > hPoiMaxTouch)
        sTop := na
        sBot := na
    [bTop[1], bBot[1], sTop[1], sBot[1]]

[hPoiBTop, hPoiBBot, hPoiSTop, hPoiSBot] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTf, f_htfPoi(),
     lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
// v8 (V8-09): HTF STRUCTURAL ALIGNMENT 0–4 — filter-TF EMA · HTF structure ·
// an HTF FVG POI on the trade's side · Daily EMA. One EMA side is 1 of 4.
// v9 (§19): HTF LOCATION — the entry candle is INSIDE an HTF FVG POI on the
// trade's side. Read by the machine (POI tap), the POI tier and — v9HtfLoc —
// the bias filter: a lower-timeframe reversal AT an HTF POI is not counter-trend.
htfLocL = htfLive and not na(hPoiBTop) and low <= hPoiBTop and close > hPoiBBot
htfLocS = htfLive and not na(hPoiSTop) and high >= hPoiSBot and close < hPoiSTop
htfAlnL = (htfB > 0 ? 1 : 0) + (nz(hStruct) > 0 ? 1 : 0) + (htfLive and not na(hPoiBTop) and close >= hPoiBBot ? 1 : 0) + (bD > 0 ? 1 : 0)
htfAlnS = (htfB < 0 ? 1 : 0) + (nz(hStruct) < 0 ? 1 : 0) + (htfLive and not na(hPoiSTop) and close <= hPoiSTop ? 1 : 0) + (bD < 0 ? 1 : 0)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 10
// DEALING RANGE — premium / discount + OTE (external swings by default)
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
useExtRng = rangeSrc == "External" and not na(extRes) and not na(extSup)
rngHi     = useExtRng ? extRes    : lastRes
rngLo     = useExtRng ? extSup    : lastSup
rngHiBar  = useExtRng ? extResBar : lastResBar
rngLoBar  = useExtRng ? extSupBar : lastSupBar
rangeOK   = not na(rngHi) and not na(rngLo) and rngHi > rngLo
bullRange = rangeOK and not na(rngHiBar) and not na(rngLoBar) and rngHiBar > rngLoBar
bearRange = rangeOK and not na(rngHiBar) and not na(rngLoBar) and rngLoBar > rngHiBar
rngW    = rangeOK ? rngHi - rngLo : na
eqLvl   = rangeOK ? rngLo + rngW / 2 : na
pdPos   = rangeOK ? (close - rngLo) / rngW : na
oteBuyTop  = rangeOK ? rngHi - OTE_1 * rngW : na
oteBuyBot  = rangeOK ? rngHi - OTE_2 * rngW : na
oteSellBot = rangeOK ? rngLo + OTE_1 * rngW : na
oteSellTop = rangeOK ? rngLo + OTE_2 * rngW : na
inOTEbuy   = bullRange and close <= oteBuyTop  and close >= oteBuyBot
inOTEsell  = bearRange and close >= oteSellBot and close <= oteSellTop

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 11
// MARKET REGIME — TRENDING / TRANSITION / RANGING / CHOP (ARCH-5)
// Deterministic, closed-bar only:
//   TRENDING   = external dir set + external BOS within REGIME_LOOK bars and
//                no fresh opposing external CHoCH
//   TRANSITION = external CHoCH within REGIME_LOOK bars (structure flipping)
//   CHOP       = no recent external event AND external range < CHOP_RANGE_ATR
//   RANGING    = everything else (wide range, no directional events)
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var int lastEBosUpBar = na
var int lastEBosDnBar = na
var int lastEChUpBar  = na
var int lastEChDnBar  = na
if confirmed
    if eBosUp
        lastEBosUpBar := bar_index
    if eBosDn
        lastEBosDnBar := bar_index
    if eChochUp
        lastEChUpBar := bar_index
    if eChochDn
        lastEChDnBar := bar_index
regEBosUp = f_recent(lastEBosUpBar, REGIME_LOOK)
regEBosDn = f_recent(lastEBosDnBar, REGIME_LOOK)
regEChUp  = f_recent(lastEChUpBar,  REGIME_LOOK)
regEChDn  = f_recent(lastEChDnBar,  REGIME_LOOK)
// v7: the same event in the 10-bar TRIGGER window — tier A's structure leg.
// lastChUpBar (M6) is written by the internal 5-bar CHoCH too, so it cannot
// serve; this one is external-only.
extChUpRec = f_recent(lastEChUpBar, TRIG_LOOK)
extChDnRec = f_recent(lastEChDnBar, TRIG_LOOK)
extRngAtr = rangeOK and atr > 0 ? rngW / atr : na

regTrending = (extDir == 1 and regEBosUp and not regEChDn) or (extDir == -1 and regEBosDn and not regEChUp)
regTransition = not regTrending and (regEChUp or regEChDn)
regChop = not regTrending and not regTransition and (na(extRngAtr) or extRngAtr < CHOP_RANGE_ATR)
regime = regTrending ? "TRENDING" : regTransition ? "TRANSITION" : regChop ? "CHOP" : "RANGING"
// v10 (V10-13): VOLATILITY REGIME — where today's ATR sits in its own history
// (percentile over volLook bars), so 1M gold and D1 EURUSD read the same scale.
//   0 LOW (≤ 20 %)  A needs exec quality +10 (thin tape: demand a stronger candle)
//   1 NORMAL        normal rules
//   2 EXPANSION (≥ 80 %)  normal rules — strong-displacement setups are welcome
//   3 EXTREME (≥ volExtPct)  machine (full narrative) only; anti-chase halved
volPct = ta.percentrank(atr, volLook)
volReg = na(volPct) ? 1 : volPct >= volExtPct ? 3 : volPct >= 80 ? 2 : volPct <= 20 ? 0 : 1
volTxt = volReg == 3 ? "EXTREME" : volReg == 2 ? "EXPANSION" : volReg == 0 ? "LOW" : "NORMAL"
lateM  = volReg == 3 ? 0.5 : 1.0          // every anti-chase distance is halved in EXTREME

// structure filter direction: external first, internal fallback
structDir = extDir != 0 ? extDir : msDir

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 12
// FVG DETECTION + LOCKED "LATEST GAP" ANCHORS
// v5: the v3 BOX registry that lived here was deleted — it only drew boxes,
// and MODULE 12C draws the same gaps typed and classified, so every gap was
// boxed twice. What stays is the raw 3-candle test plus the latest-respected
// gap per side, which FEM (M15), the setup machine (M17) and the score (M16)
// consume as scalars. "Draw live chart-TF FVGs" now drives the M12C boxes.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
bullFVG = low > high[2]
bearFVG = high < low[2]

// latest respected FVG per side (FEM execution + machine retest anchor)
var float cFvgBTop = na
var float cFvgBBot = na
var int   cFvgBBar = na
var float cFvgSTop = na
var float cFvgSBot = na
var int   cFvgSBar = na
if confirmed
    if bullFVG
        cFvgBTop := low
        cFvgBBot := high[2]
        cFvgBBar := bar_index
    if not na(cFvgBBot) and close < cFvgBBot
        cFvgBTop := na
        cFvgBBot := na
        cFvgBBar := na
    if bearFVG
        cFvgSBot := high
        cFvgSTop := low[2]
        cFvgSBar := bar_index
    if not na(cFvgSTop) and close > cFvgSTop
        cFvgSTop := na
        cFvgSBot := na
        cFvgSBar := na

// v10 (V10-02 / V10-03): SHIFT LINEAGE — what belongs to the last EXTERNAL shift.
// The displacement that qualifies a shift is the one ON the shift candle or
// within maxDispDelay bars after it; the shift-leg FVG is the gap created
// between the liquidity event and maxFvgDelay bars after the shift. Both are
// remembered WITH the shift and die with it (a new shift or the opposite one
// resets the lineage; a close through the gap's far edge consumes it). v9 asked
// "was there an MSS in 10 bars AND a big candle in 10 bars" — two unrelated
// facts. Consumers: tier A / A+ (M16), the score and the no-trade engine (M18).
f_shift(bool isL, bool shift, bool opp, int mssQ, int dispQ, int liqBar, float fvgT, float fvgB, int fvgBar) =>
    var int   sBar = na       // bar of the last external shift (MSS or CHoCH)
    var int   sQ   = 0        // 1 CHoCH · 2 MSS · 3 high-quality MSS
    var int   dBar = na       // displacement bar tied to it
    var int   dQ   = 0        // its grade (best inside the window)
    var int   gBar = na       // shift-leg FVG creation bar
    var float gT   = na
    var float gB   = na
    if confirmed
        if opp
            sBar := na
            gBar := na
        if shift
            sBar := bar_index
            sQ   := mssQ
            dBar := dispQ >= 1 ? bar_index : na
            dQ   := dispQ
            // the leg's own gap may have printed on the way INTO the break
            bool legGap = not na(fvgBar) and bar_index - fvgBar <= maxFvgDelay and (na(liqBar) or fvgBar >= liqBar)
            gBar := legGap ? fvgBar : na
            gT   := legGap ? fvgT : na
            gB   := legGap ? fvgB : na
        else if not na(sBar)
            if bar_index - sBar <= maxDispDelay and dispQ > dQ
                dBar := bar_index
                dQ   := dispQ
            if na(gBar) and fvgBar == bar_index and bar_index - sBar <= maxFvgDelay
                gBar := bar_index
                gT   := fvgT
                gB   := fvgB
        if not na(gBar) and (isL ? close < gB : close > gT)
            gBar := na                                  // gap consumed
    [sBar, sQ, dBar, dQ, gBar, gT, gB]
[shUpBar, shUpQ, shUpDispBar, shUpDispQ, shUpFvgBar, shUpFvgT, shUpFvgB] = f_shift(true,  eChochUp, eChochDn, mssQUp, dispQUp, lastSslBar, cFvgBTop, cFvgBBot, cFvgBBar)
[shDnBar, shDnQ, shDnDispBar, shDnDispQ, shDnFvgBar, shDnFvgT, shDnFvgB] = f_shift(false, eChochDn, eChochUp, mssQDn, dispQDn, lastBslBar, cFvgSTop, cFvgSBot, cFvgSBar)
// STRUCTURE AGE grade: 3 ≤ 1 bar (strongest) · 2 ≤ mssAgeAp (A+) · 1 ≤ mssAgeA (A) · 0 stale (B at most)
f_ageQ(int b) => na(b) ? 0 : bar_index - b <= 1 ? 3 : bar_index - b <= mssAgeAp ? 2 : bar_index - b <= mssAgeA ? 1 : 0
shAgeQL = f_ageQ(shUpBar)
shAgeQS = f_ageQ(shDnBar)
// CAUSAL CHAIN: an external shift with ITS OWN displacement of grade ≥ minDispQ
chainL = not na(shUpBar) and not na(shUpDispBar) and shUpDispQ >= minDispQ
chainS = not na(shDnBar) and not na(shDnDispBar) and shDnDispQ >= minDispQ
// … and ITS OWN unconsumed FVG; price retesting that gap (creation bar excluded)
chainFvgL = chainL and not na(shUpFvgBar)
chainFvgS = chainS and not na(shDnFvgBar)
inShFvgL  = chainFvgL and bar_index > shUpFvgBar and low  <= shUpFvgT and close >= shUpFvgB
inShFvgS  = chainFvgS and bar_index > shDnFvgBar and high >= shDnFvgB and close <= shDnFvgT

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 12B
// ◇ PHASE 1 (v4) HH / HL / LH / LL ENGINE — REMOVED in v10 (V10-18, CE10117).
// At default settings it fed only the Strict-mode "V4STR" floor layer, a rare
// strong-level flip invalidation of the machine and the Quasimodo zones; the
// PRIMARY structure engine (protected swings · BOS · CHoCH · MSS, MODULE 6)
// is untouched. It was the heaviest module for its default-path contribution
// (~5,200 compiled tokens + ~1,300 for QM). Full text in Demand + Price
// Action-9.pine (MODULE 12B / 13C) for a companion indicator.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 12C
// ◇ PHASE 3 (v4) — IMBALANCE / FVG FAMILY
// Parallel TYPED FVG registry on top of the untouched v3 registry (M12):
//   · mitigation states per box: fresh → touched → 50% filled → full filled;
//     the "mitigated" cut-off is configurable (touch / 50% / full) — only
//     unmitigated boxes stay entry-grade
//   · third-candle typing (lesson's 7 types): 1 bull pin / 2 bear pin /
//     3 breakaway momentum / 5 candle-4 sweep-engulf = SKIP · 4 strong
//     opposite candle = expect FULL FILL · 6 candle-4 inside bar / 7 doji =
//     conditional, entry only after the candle-5 (resp. candle-4) sweep-and-
//     reverse trigger
//   · BSI / SBI — all three candles the same colour as the move
//   · ULTIMATE FVG — earliest gap of the current impulse leg (primary target)
//   · per-FVG premium/discount flag (·PD) — bull gaps under the range 50%,
//     bear gaps above it
//   · BOS-overlap flag (·BOS) — the gap intersects the BOS candle's range
//   · BPR — bull/bear FVG overlap zones; a CHoCH landing while the BPR lives
//     arms it (lesson type a); trend-internal overlaps stay type b
//   · RDRB — redelivered-rebalanced 3-candle zones (candle1/candle3 wicks DO
//     overlap — the anti-FVG): bullish zone [candle3.low … candle2.close],
//     bearish zone [candle2.close … candle3.high]
//   · HIDDEN CHoCH — the first counter-trend imbalance inside a pullback
//     becomes the early shift level; a displaced close through it fires
//     hCHoCH before the classic CHoCH
// FULLY ADDITIVE: p3Enable OFF ⇒ output identical to v3+P1+P2. Labels /
// lines / boxes only (64-output budget stays 63). The v3 FVG boxes (M12)
// still draw — disable "Draw live chart-TF FVGs" to avoid double boxes.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
grpP3 = "4 · POI — typed FVG family"
p3Enable   = input.bool(true,  "Enable v4 FVG family", group = grpP3,
     tooltip = "Typed FVG registry (7 types, BSI/SBI, ultimate, PD/BOS flags, mitigation states) + BPR + RDRB + hidden CHoCH. Fully additive — OFF restores v3+P1+P2 output.")
p3MaxKeep  = 6                 // v9 const
p3MaxAge   = input.int(120,    "Typed FVG / zone max age (bars)", minval = 20, group = grpP3)
p3MitMode  = input.string("50% fill", "Mitigated when", options = ["Touch", "50% fill", "Full fill"], group = grpP3,
     tooltip = "Cut-off after which a gap stops being entry-grade (lesson: unmitigated FVGs only for entries; touch vs 50% vs full is style-dependent).")
p3BreakAtr = 1.2               // v9 const: breakaway / opposite candle-3 body ≥ ATR ×
p3HpOnly   = input.bool(false, "Entry-grade needs premium/discount alignment", group = grpP3,
     tooltip = "ON: only bull FVGs below the dealing-range 50% (and bear above) stay entry-grade (lesson: FVG premium/discount filter).")
p3ReqBos   = input.bool(false, "Entry-grade needs BOS-candle overlap", group = grpP3,
     tooltip = "ON: the gap must intersect the range of the candle that broke structure (lesson: FVG must overlap the BOS candle).")
p3BosLook  = 10                // v9 const
p3ShowBpr  = input.bool(true,  "Show BPR (balanced price range) zones", group = grpP3,
     tooltip = "v8: ink only. BPR detection always runs (a BPR retest is a POI layer of the confirmation floor); OFF hides the boxes and chips.")
p3ShowHch  = input.bool(true,  "Show hidden-CHoCH chips", group = grpP3,
     tooltip = "v8: ink only. Hidden-CHoCH detection always runs (it is a STRUCT layer of the Strict floor); OFF hides the chips.")
p3HchExp   = 40                // v9 const: hidden-CHoCH level expiry

// typed FVG — one gap + its full lesson classification and lifecycle
type P3Fvg
    box   bx
    float top
    float bot
    int   barC        // creation bar (candle 3)
    bool  isBull
    int   typ         // 0 plain · 1..7 lesson type
    bool  entryOk     // type 6/7 sweep-and-reverse trigger satisfied
    bool  bsi         // BSI/SBI: all three candles the colour of the move
    bool  ultimate    // earliest gap of its impulse leg
    bool  hp          // premium/discount aligned
    bool  bosOverlap  // intersects the BOS candle range
    int   mit         // 0 fresh · 1 touched · 2 half filled · 3 full filled
    bool  frozen      // box stopped extending (mitigated per mode)
    int   legId       // impulse-leg anchor (swing bar) for the ultimate flag
    float c3Hi        // candle-3 range (types 5/6/7)
    float c3Lo
    float c4Hi        // candle-4 range (type 6 trigger)
    float c4Lo
    int   vis         // v10 (V10-06): separate visits (leave + return); entry-grade needs ≤ 1
    bool  wasIn       // v10: price overlapped the gap on the previous bar

// BPR / RDRB zone
type P3Zone
    box    bx
    bool   isBull
    int    barC
    bool   armed      // BPR type a: a CHoCH landed while the zone lived
    bool   tapped
    float  top        // v10 (V10-17): geometry held as data, never read back from the box
    float  bot

var p3Bull  = array.new<P3Fvg>()
var p3Bear  = array.new<P3Fvg>()
var p3Zones = array.new<P3Zone>()

p3MitTh = p3MitMode == "Touch" ? 1 : p3MitMode == "50% fill" ? 2 : 3

// ---- BOS-candle range memory (for the ·BOS overlap flag) -------------------------
var float p3BosUpHi  = na
var float p3BosUpLo  = na
var int   p3BosUpBar = na
var float p3BosDnHi  = na
var float p3BosDnLo  = na
var int   p3BosDnBar = na
if p3Enable and confirmed
    if accBrokeUp or eAccUp
        p3BosUpHi  := high                 // v5 F1: the ACCEPTED break candle
        p3BosUpLo  := low
        p3BosUpBar := bar_index
    if accBrokeDn or eAccDn
        p3BosDnHi  := high
        p3BosDnLo  := low
        p3BosDnBar := bar_index

// third-candle typing at creation (candle3 = current bar). Lesson types:
// 1/2 pin bar → skip · 3 breakaway momentum → skip · 4 strong opposite →
// expect full fill · 7 doji → conditional. Types 5/6 resolve on candle 4.
f_p3Type(bool isBull) =>
    int t = 0
    if bullPin
        t := 1
    else if bearPin
        t := 2
    else if body >= p3BreakAtr * atr and (isBull ? bullBar : bearBar)
        t := 3
    else if body >= p3BreakAtr * atr and (isBull ? bearBar : bullBar)
        t := 4
    else if doji
        t := 7
    t

// v5.1a: type + tier + mitigation state only. The v4 caption also carried
// ·U ·PD ·BOS and skip / wait / full-fill — ~30 characters on a 3-bar-wide
// box, so it spilled over the candles either side of the gap and collided
// with the next gap's caption. The ·U / entry-grade detail is on the
// dashboard's "◇ v4 FVG" row, and the short form keeps this function cheap
// (it is on the caption hot path).
f_p3Txt(P3Fvg f) =>
    string t = f.isBull ? "+FVG" : "−FVG"
    if f.bsi
        t += f.isBull ? " BSI" : " SBI"
    if f.typ > 0
        t += " T" + str.tostring(f.typ)
    t += f.mit >= 3 ? " ·filled" : f.mit == 2 ? " ·50%" : f.mit == 1 ? " ·touched" : ""
    t

f_p3NewFvg(bool isBull, float top_, float bot_) =>
    color c = isBull ? COL_BULL : COL_BEAR
    // ultimate = earliest live gap of this impulse leg (anchored at the swing)
    int leg = isBull ? nz(lastSupBar, -1) : nz(lastResBar, -1)
    bool ult = true
    arr = isBull ? p3Bull : p3Bear
    if array.size(arr) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(arr) - 1
            if array.get(arr, i).legId == leg
                ult := false
                break
    bool hp_ = rangeOK and (isBull ? top_ <= eqLvl : bot_ >= eqLvl)
    bool bosOv = isBull ?
         (not na(p3BosUpBar) and bar_index - p3BosUpBar <= p3BosLook and bot_ <= p3BosUpHi and top_ >= p3BosUpLo) :
         (not na(p3BosDnBar) and bar_index - p3BosDnBar <= p3BosLook and bot_ <= p3BosDnHi and top_ >= p3BosDnLo)
    bool bsi_ = isBull ? bullBar[2] and bullBar[1] and bullBar : bearBar[2] and bearBar[1] and bearBar
    box   bxNa = na
    float c4h  = na
    float c4l  = na
    P3Fvg f = P3Fvg.new(bxNa, top_, bot_, bar_index, isBull, f_p3Type(isBull), false, bsi_, ult, hp_, bosOv, 0, false, leg, high, low, c4h, c4l, 0, false)
    if showFvg
        f.bx := box.new(bar_index - 2, top_, bar_index + 1, bot_,
             border_color = color.new(c, f.bsi ? 35 : 60), bgcolor = color.new(c, f.bsi ? 92 : 95),
             text = f_p3Txt(f), text_color = p8TxtCol, text_size = p8TxtSz,
             text_halign = text.align_right, text_valign = isBull ? text.align_bottom : text.align_top)
    f

// ---- creation + BPR overlap scan ---------------------------------------------------
f_p3NewZone(bool isBull, float top_, float bot_) =>
    color c = color.purple
    bx = box.new(bar_index - 2, top_, bar_index + 1, bot_,
         border_color = color.new(c, p3ShowBpr ? 40 : 100), bgcolor = color.new(c, p3ShowBpr ? 93 : 100),
         text = p3ShowBpr ? "BPR" + (isBull ? " ▲" : " ▼") : "", text_color = p8TxtCol, text_size = p8TxtSz,
         text_halign = text.align_right, text_valign = isBull ? text.align_bottom : text.align_top)
    array.push(p3Zones, P3Zone.new(bx, isBull, bar_index, false, false, top_, bot_))
    if array.size(p3Zones) > 10
        z0 = array.get(p3Zones, 0)
        box.delete(z0.bx)
        array.remove(p3Zones, 0)

// wrapped in a function (CE10295 fix) — verbatim logic, mutates registries only
f_p3Create() =>
    if p3Enable and confirmed and bullFVG
        array.push(p3Bull, f_p3NewFvg(true, low, high[2]))
        if array.size(p3Bull) > p3MaxKeep
            f0 = array.get(p3Bull, 0)
            box.delete(f0.bx)
            array.remove(p3Bull, 0)
        // bullish BPR: this buy-side gap overlaps a live sell-side gap
        if array.size(p3Bear) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(p3Bear) - 1
                fb = array.get(p3Bear, i)
                float iTop = math.min(low, fb.top)
                float iBot = math.max(high[2], fb.bot)
                if iTop > iBot
                    f_p3NewZone(true, iTop, iBot)
                    break
    if p3Enable and confirmed and bearFVG
        array.push(p3Bear, f_p3NewFvg(false, low[2], high))
        if array.size(p3Bear) > p3MaxKeep
            f0 = array.get(p3Bear, 0)
            box.delete(f0.bx)
            array.remove(p3Bear, 0)
        if array.size(p3Bull) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(p3Bull) - 1
                fb = array.get(p3Bull, i)
                float iTop = math.min(low[2], fb.top)
                float iBot = math.max(high, fb.bot)
                if iTop > iBot
                    f_p3NewZone(false, iTop, iBot)
                    break
f_p3Create()

// ---- typed-FVG lifecycle: candle-4/5 typing · mitigation states · aging -----------
// wrapped in a function (CE10295 fix) — verbatim logic, trigger events returned
// CE10117 compression: the bull and bear lifecycles were mirror copies — one
// direction-parameterized pass now serves both. Rules are unchanged.
f_p3Life(array<P3Fvg> arr, bool isBull) =>
    if p3Enable and confirmed and array.size(arr) > 0
        for i = array.size(arr) - 1 to 0
            f = array.get(arr, i)
            float pen = isBull ? low : high          // the side that fills this gap
            if bar_index == f.barC + 1 and f.typ == 0
                if (isBull ? high > f.c3Hi and bearEngulf : low < f.c3Lo and bullEngulf)
                    f.typ := 5                        // candle4 sweeps candle3 + engulfs → trap
                else if high <= f.c3Hi and low >= f.c3Lo
                    f.typ := 6                        // candle4 inside bar
                    f.c4Hi := high
                    f.c4Lo := low
            // types 7 (doji, candle4) and 6 (inside bar, candle5): sweep the
            // reference extreme, tap the gap, close back = entry trigger
            bool t7 = bar_index == f.barC + 1 and f.typ == 7
            bool t6 = bar_index == f.barC + 2 and f.typ == 6
            if (t7 or t6) and not f.entryOk
                float ref = t7 ? (isBull ? f.c3Lo : f.c3Hi) : (isBull ? f.c4Lo : f.c4Hi)
                bool swept = isBull ? pen < ref : pen > ref
                bool tapped = isBull ? low <= f.top : high >= f.bot
                bool back = isBull ? close > ref and bullBar : close < ref and bearBar
                if swept and tapped and back
                    f.entryOk := true
            if bar_index > f.barC
                // v10 (V10-06): a VISIT is leave + return; the 2nd visit ends entry grade
                bool inF = low <= f.top and high >= f.bot
                if inF and not f.wasIn
                    f.vis += 1
                f.wasIn := inF
                float mid = (f.top + f.bot) / 2
                int m0 = f.mit
                f.mit := (isBull ? pen <= f.bot : pen >= f.top) ? 3 :
                     (isBull ? pen <= mid : pen >= mid) ? math.max(f.mit, 2) :
                     (isBull ? pen <= f.top : pen >= f.bot) ? math.max(f.mit, 1) : f.mit
                if not f.frozen and f.mit >= p3MitTh   // mitigated per mode → freeze + flag
                    f.frozen := true
                    if not na(f.bx)
                        box.set_right(f.bx, bar_index)
                        box.set_bgcolor(f.bx, color.new(isBull ? COL_BULL : COL_BEAR, 97))
                // RUNTIME: this rebuilt the caption for every live gap on every
                // bar — ~12 ternary/concat string builds plus 12 drawing writes
                // per bar, for text that only changes when the mitigation state
                // moves or while the candle-4/5 typing is still resolving.
                if not na(f.bx) and (f.mit != m0 or bar_index <= f.barC + 2)
                    box.set_text(f.bx, f_p3Txt(f))
            if (isBull ? close < f.bot : close > f.top) or bar_index - f.barC > p3MaxAge
                box.delete(f.bx)                       // inverted or stale → drop
                array.remove(arr, i)
f_p3Life(p3Bull, true)                                     // v11 (V11-09): the return value was documented unread in v10 — removed
f_p3Life(p3Bear, false)

// ---- BPR / RDRB lifecycle: CHoCH arming (type a) · retest events · aging ----------
// wrapped in a function (CE10295 fix) — verbatim logic, retest events returned
f_p3ZoneLife() =>
    bool tapUp = false
    bool tapDn = false
    if p3Enable and confirmed and array.size(p3Zones) > 0
        for i = array.size(p3Zones) - 1 to 0
            z = array.get(p3Zones, i)
            float zt = z.top                                        // v10 (V10-17)
            float zb = z.bot
            if not z.armed and (z.isBull ? chochUp or eChochUp : chochDn or eChochDn)
                z.armed := true                                     // lesson type a: pre-CHoCH BPR, traded after the CHoCH
                if p3ShowBpr
                    box.set_text(z.bx, "BPR " + (z.isBull ? "▲" : "▼") + " ·CHoCH armed")
            if bar_index > z.barC and not z.tapped
                if z.isBull and low <= zt and close >= zb and zoneBullConf
                    z.tapped := true
                    tapUp    := true
                    if p3ShowBpr
                        f_chip(true, "BPR ▲ retest ✓", color.new(COL_BULL, 30), color.white, mkSize)
                if not z.isBull and high >= zb and close <= zt and zoneBearConf
                    z.tapped := true
                    tapDn    := true
                    if p3ShowBpr
                        f_chip(false, "BPR ▼ retest ✓", color.new(COL_BEAR, 30), color.white, mkSize)
            if (z.isBull and close < zb) or (not z.isBull and close > zt) or bar_index - z.barC > p3MaxAge
                box.delete(z.bx)
                array.remove(p3Zones, i)
    [tapUp, tapDn]
[p3BprTapUp, p3BprTapDn] = f_p3ZoneLife()

// ---- HIDDEN CHoCH: first counter-trend imbalance inside the pullback --------------
// downtrend + pullback-up prints its FIRST bull FVG → candle-1 high = the
// early shift level; a displaced close above it = hCHoCH ▲ (fires before the
// classic CHoCH). Mirror for the uptrend pullback.
// wrapped in a function (CE10295 fix) — verbatim logic, events + levels returned
f_p3Hidden() =>
    var float p3HchUpLvl = na
    var int   p3HchUpBar = na
    var float p3HchDnLvl = na
    var int   p3HchDnBar = na
    bool hUp = false
    bool hDn = false
    if p3Enable and confirmed
        if na(p3HchUpLvl) and bullFVG and (msDir == -1 or extDir == -1)
            p3HchUpLvl := high[2]
            p3HchUpBar := bar_index
        if na(p3HchDnLvl) and bearFVG and (msDir == 1 or extDir == 1)
            p3HchDnLvl := low[2]
            p3HchDnBar := bar_index
        if not na(p3HchUpLvl) and (bar_index - p3HchUpBar > p3HchExp or chochUp or eChochUp)
            p3HchUpLvl := na                                        // stale, or the classic CHoCH beat it
        if not na(p3HchDnLvl) and (bar_index - p3HchDnBar > p3HchExp or chochDn or eChochDn)
            p3HchDnLvl := na
        if not na(p3HchUpLvl) and close > p3HchUpLvl and body >= structDisp * atr
            p3HchUpLvl := na
            hUp := true
            if p3ShowHch
                f_chip(true, "hCHoCH", color.new(COL_BULL, 25), color.white, mkSize)
        if not na(p3HchDnLvl) and close < p3HchDnLvl and body >= structDisp * atr
            p3HchDnLvl := na
            hDn := true
            if p3ShowHch
                f_chip(false, "hCHoCH", color.new(COL_BEAR, 25), color.white, mkSize)
    [hUp, hDn]                                              // v11 (V11-09): the two level slots were never read outside
[p3HchUp, p3HchDn] = f_p3Hidden()
// v5: remember the hidden shift for TRIG_LOOK bars — it is an EARLY structure
// signal, so the engine that consumes it needs a window, not a single bar.
var int p3HchUpBarM = na
var int p3HchDnBarM = na
if p3HchUp
    p3HchUpBarM := bar_index
if p3HchDn
    p3HchDnBarM := bar_index
p3HchUpRec = f_recent(p3HchUpBarM, TRIG_LOOK)
p3HchDnRec = f_recent(p3HchDnBarM, TRIG_LOOK)

// ---- nearest ENTRY-GRADE typed FVG per side (for Phases 6/7) -----------------------
// entry-grade = type 0 plain, or type 6/7 with the trigger done; unmitigated
// per the configured mode; optional PD / BOS-overlap gates. Ultimate preferred.
// wrapped in a function (CE10295 fix) — verbatim logic, results returned
// CE10117 compression: one parameterized scan for both sides (same rules)
f_p3Nearest(array<P3Fvg> arr, bool isBull) =>
    float top_ = na
    float bot_ = na
    bool  ult  = false        // v11 (V11-09): still the PREFERENCE key below, no longer returned (never read)
    bool  in2  = false
    if p3Enable and array.size(arr) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(arr) - 1
            f = array.get(arr, i)
            // v10: f.vis ≤ 1 — the FIRST visit is the retest; a second visit of the same gap is not entry-grade
            bool ok = bar_index > f.barC and f.mit < p3MitTh and f.vis <= 1 and (f.typ == 0 or ((f.typ == 6 or f.typ == 7) and f.entryOk)) and (not p3HpOnly or f.hp) and (not p3ReqBos or f.bosOverlap) and (isBull ? f.top <= close : f.bot >= close)
            bool nearer = isBull ? (na(top_) or f.top > top_) : (na(bot_) or f.bot < bot_)
            if ok and ((f.ultimate and not ult) or (f.ultimate == ult and nearer) or na(top_))
                top_ := f.top
                bot_ := f.bot
                ult  := f.ultimate
            // v10 (no-trade reason): price is INSIDE a live gap that is on its 2nd+ visit
            if bar_index > f.barC and f.vis >= 2 and f.mit < p3MitTh and low <= f.top and high >= f.bot
                in2 := true
    [top_, bot_, in2]
[p3BullTop, p3BullBot, p3BullIn2] = f_p3Nearest(p3Bull, true)
[p3BearTop, p3BearBot, p3BearIn2] = f_p3Nearest(p3Bear, false)

// keep live (unfrozen) typed boxes and zones extending on the last bar
f_p3Ext(array<P3Fvg> arr) =>
    if array.size(arr) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(arr) - 1
            f = array.get(arr, i)
            if not na(f.bx) and not f.frozen
                box.set_right(f.bx, bar_index + 1)
if barstate.islast and p3Enable
    f_p3Ext(p3Bull)
    f_p3Ext(p3Bear)
    if array.size(p3Zones) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(p3Zones) - 1
            box.set_right(array.get(p3Zones, i).bx, bar_index + 1)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 13
// ZONE ENGINE — S/D (imbalance geometry) · OB (origin candle) · RB (wick) ·
// BREAKER / MITIGATION flips. Each zone carries its KIND (ARCH-6) and a
// freshness test-counter (spec §20/§24: heavily mitigated zone = low quality).
// Lifecycle: fresh → tested (×N) → 50% tapped → signaled / spent → violated
// (flip once → breaker/mitigation, second violation deletes).
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
type Zone
    box    bx
    line   mid
    bool   isSupply
    bool   touched
    bool   tapped50
    bool   signaled
    int    score
    int    tap50Bar
    bool   flipped
    int    touchBar
    string kind      // "SD" | "OB" | "RB" | "BRK" | "MIT"
    int    tests     // separate visits (leave + return) consumed
    bool   wasIn     // price overlapped the zone on the previous bar
    // v5.3 F2: the zone PRICE, held as data, not read back out of the drawing.
    // Two reasons. (a) max_boxes_count is 500 and every box family on this chart
    // shares it; when the cap is exceeded TradingView deletes the OLDEST box and
    // box.get_top/get_bottom on that id then silently return na — the zone stays
    // in the array with no geometry, so nbTop/nbBot, the flip test, the dedup
    // scans and the P7 breaker model all go quietly wrong instead of loudly.
    // (b) it removes ten drawing reads per bar, three of them inside per-bar
    // array walks, from a script already near the 20s cap. The box is now
    // render-only. `mid` never had its y read back, so it needs no companion.
    float  zTop
    float  zBot
    int    barC      // v7: creation bar — zones age out (zoneMaxAge)
    float  mit       // v10 (V10-06): deepest penetration so far, 0..1+ of the zone height

var zones = array.new<Zone>()
// v10 (V10-06): POI LIFE from the visit count and the mitigation depth —
// 0 FRESH · 1 1ST TOUCH · 2 MITIGATED (≥ 50 % traded on the first visit) ·
// 3 WEAK (2nd separate test) · 4 DEAD (3rd). WEAK caps a POI at tier A, DEAD is
// no POI (and the zone is spent at zoneMaxTests anyway).
f_life(int tests, float mit) => tests <= 0 ? 0 : tests == 1 ? (mit >= 0.5 ? 2 : 1) : tests == 2 ? 3 : 4
f_lifeTxt(int l) => l == 0 ? "fresh" : l == 1 ? "1st touch" : l == 2 ? "mitigated" : l == 3 ? "weak" : "dead"

// v5.3 F1: which zone families are INKED. Detection no longer depends on any of
// these; each one only decides whether its family is painted. showZones is the
// group master, showOB / showRB / showFlip the per-family switches — so a zone
// hidden here is still a live POI for nbTop/nbBot, the tier ladder, the v5 POI
// floor, the trap engine's obNear test and the Phase-7 BRK model.
f_zVis(string kind) =>
    showZones and (kind == "OB" ? showOB : kind == "RB" ? showRB : (kind == "BRK" or kind == "MIT") ? showFlip : true)

f_newZone(bool isSupply, float top, float bot, bool star, string kind, string txt, int lft) =>
    c  = isSupply ? COL_BEAR : COL_BULL
    x1 = lft != 0 ? lft : bar_index - 2
    thin = kind == "OB"
    // v5.3 F1: the display switches are INK switches now. The zone is always
    // built (it is the input to nbTop/nbBot → inDemand/inSupply → poiLong →
    // tier → machine); when its family is hidden the box is drawn fully
    // transparent with no caption, so the chart looks exactly as before.
    bool vis = f_zVis(kind)
    bx = box.new(x1, top, bar_index + 1, bot,
         border_color = color.new(c, vis ? (thin ? 75 : 55) : 100),
         bgcolor = color.new(c, vis ? (thin ? 96 : 93) : 100),
         text = vis ? txt : "", text_color = p8TxtCol, text_size = drawSize,
         // LEFT, not right: every box family used to write its caption at the
         // right edge, so at bar_index "DEMAND ★HP" landed on top of "+FVG T7"
         // and "REJECTION ▲" on top of the HTF POI caption. The left edge is
         // this zone's formation bar, so the move also says where it was born.
         text_halign = text.align_left,
         text_valign = isSupply ? text.align_top : text.align_bottom)
    md = line.new(x1, (top + bot) / 2, bar_index + 1, (top + bot) / 2,
         color = color.new(c, vis ? 72 : 100), style = line.style_dotted)
    Zone.new(bx, md, isSupply, false, false, false, star ? 3 : 2, -1, false, -1, kind, 0, false, top, bot, bar_index, 0.0)

// ---- update zones, 50% tap engine (edge-triggered, V2 FIX-10), flips ----------
// CE10117 compression: the supply and demand halves of this loop were mirror
// copies (~100 lines). One direction-generic pass now serves both: every
// asymmetry is resolved through `sup` at the top of the body. Same lifecycle,
// same edge-triggering, same flip rules, same signal and stop geometry.
f_zoneLoop() =>
    bool sdL = false
    bool sdS = false
    float slL = na
    float slS = na
    bool invU = false
    bool invD = false
    if array.size(zones) > 0
        for i = array.size(zones) - 1 to 0
            z    = array.get(zones, i)
            bool sup = z.isSupply
            top  = z.zTop                       // v5.3 F2 (was box.get_top)
            bot  = z.zBot                       // v5.3 F2 (was box.get_bottom)
            midP = (top + bot) / 2
            // ---- v7: stale zone — never a POI again (ages from creation, flips included)
            if zoneMaxAge > 0 and bar_index - z.barC > zoneMaxAge and confirmed
                box.delete(z.bx)
                line.delete(z.mid)
                array.remove(zones, i)
                continue
            // ---- violation: flip once into a breaker / mitigation block, else drop
            if (sup ? close > top : close < bot) and confirmed
                if sup
                    invD := true
                else
                    invU := true
                if not z.flipped
                    // BREAKER needs sweep + structure break before failure (FIX-14)
                    bool isBrk = sup ? recentSsl and recentStructUp : recentBsl and recentStructDn
                    color cf   = sup ? COL_BULL : COL_BEAR
                    z.isSupply := not sup
                    z.flipped  := true
                    z.touched  := false
                    z.touchBar := -1
                    z.tapped50 := false
                    z.signaled := false
                    z.tap50Bar := -1
                    z.tests    := 0
                    z.wasIn    := false
                    z.mit      := 0
                    z.kind     := isBrk ? "BRK" : "MIT"
                    z.score    := isBrk ? 3 : 2
                    // v5.3 F1: ink only. showFlip OFF no longer DELETES the zone
                    // (the Phase-7 BRK model trades these), so the box has to be
                    // actively blanked instead — otherwise a flipped zone would
                    // keep displaying its old DEMAND / SUPPLY paint.
                    if showZones
                        bool fv = showFlip
                        box.set_border_color(z.bx, color.new(cf, fv ? 55 : 100))
                        box.set_bgcolor(z.bx, color.new(cf, fv ? 93 : 100))
                        box.set_text(z.bx, fv ? (isBrk ? "BREAKER " : "MITIGATION ") + (sup ? "▲" : "▼") : "")
                        box.set_text_color(z.bx, p8TxtCol)
                        box.set_text_valign(z.bx, sup ? text.align_bottom : text.align_top)
                        line.set_color(z.mid, color.new(cf, fv ? 72 : 100))
                else
                    box.delete(z.bx)
                    line.delete(z.mid)
                    array.remove(zones, i)
                continue
            // ---- freshness: each separate visit (leave + return) consumes the zone
            inZ = sup ? high >= bot : low <= top
            if inZ
                if not z.touched
                    z.touchBar := bar_index
                z.touched := true
                float hz = top - bot
                if hz > 0 and confirmed
                    z.mit := math.max(z.mit, (sup ? high - bot : top - low) / hz)   // v10: mitigation depth
                if not z.wasIn and confirmed
                    z.tests := z.tests + 1
                    if z.tests > zoneMaxTests and not z.signaled
                        z.signaled := true                       // spent by repeated tests
                        if f_zVis(z.kind)                             // v5.3 F1: ink only
                            box.set_bgcolor(z.bx, color.new(sup ? COL_BEAR : COL_BULL, 96))
                            box.set_text(z.bx, z.kind + " ·spent")
            if confirmed
                z.wasIn := inZ
            // ---- edge-triggered 50% tap, then confirmation inside the window
            if (sup ? high < bot : low > top)
                z.tapped50 := false
            if (sup ? high >= midP : low <= midP) and not z.tapped50
                z.tapped50 := true
                z.tap50Bar := bar_index
            if not z.signaled and z.tapped50 and bar_index - z.tap50Bar <= confirmWin and (sup ? zoneBearConf : zoneBullConf) and inZ and confirmed
                if sup
                    sdS := true
                    slS := math.max(high, top) + SL_PAD_ATR * atr
                else
                    sdL := true
                    slL := math.min(low, bot) - SL_PAD_ATR * atr
                z.signaled := true
                if f_zVis(z.kind)                                     // v5.3 F1: ink only
                    box.set_bgcolor(z.bx, color.new(sup ? COL_BEAR : COL_BULL, 94))
    [sdL, sdS, slL, slS, invU, invD]
// declared here (not tuple-destructured) because later modules reassign them
sigSDLong  = false
sigSDShort = false
float sigSLLong  = na
float sigSLShort = na
// v8 (V8-07): per-class stop slots. sigSLLong/Short become the SELECTED stop —
// the highest-ranked RAW candidate's before the gates, the ACCEPTED producer's
// after the arbiter — instead of whichever producer happened to write last.
float slEngL = na
float slEngS = na
float slP7L  = na
float slP7S  = na
float slMcL  = na
float slMcS  = na
bool zoneInvalidatedUp = false   // demand-side POI violated this bar (machine invalidation)
bool zoneInvalidatedDn = false
[zLg, zSh, zSlL, zSlS, zInvU, zInvD] = f_zoneLoop()
sigSDLong  := zLg
sigSDShort := zSh
slEngL := zSlL
slEngS := zSlS
zoneInvalidatedUp := zInvU
zoneInvalidatedDn := zInvD

// ---- create S/D zones (FVG-imbalance geometry, V2 FIX-9) + OB companions ------
dispUp  = bullBar[1] and body[1] >= dispFactor * atr
dispDn  = bearBar[1] and body[1] >= dispFactor * atr
// v5.3 F1: DETECTION is ungated. `showZones` no longer decides whether a POI
// exists — only whether you can see it. Same for the OB companion (showOB feeds
// obNearL/obNearS in the trap engine), the rejection blocks and the breaker flip
// (showFlip is what creates the "BRK" zones the Phase-7 BRK model trades): all
// four are the identical fault inside the one `zones` array this fix is about.
newDemand = bullFVG and dispUp
newSupply = bearFVG and dispDn

f_pushZone(Zone z) =>
    array.push(zones, z)

// CE10117 compression: the "is this a duplicate of a live zone?" scan was
// written out once per direction. Same rule: an overlapping zone of the same
// side with an equal-or-better score and no signal yet blocks the new one;
// otherwise the weaker zone is deleted and the new one replaces it.
f_zoneFree(bool isSup, float zTop, float zBot, int newScore) =>
    bool dup = false
    if array.size(zones) > 0
        for i = array.size(zones) - 1 to 0
            z = array.get(zones, i)
            if z.isSupply == isSup and not (zBot > z.zTop or zTop < z.zBot)   // v5.3 F2
                if z.score >= newScore and not z.signaled
                    dup := true
                else
                    box.delete(z.bx)
                    line.delete(z.mid)
                    array.remove(zones, i)
    not dup

if newDemand and confirmed
    float zTop = low
    float zBot = math.max(high[2], low - maxZoneAtr * atr)
    bs = not na(lastRes) and close[1] > lastRes
    if f_zoneFree(false, zTop, zBot, bs ? 3 : 2)
        f_pushZone(f_newZone(false, zTop, zBot, bs, "SD", "DEMAND" + (bs ? " ★HP" : ""), 0))
        // ORDER BLOCK companion: the opposing (bearish) origin candle before
        // the displacement leg — its own geometry, below the imbalance
        if bearBar[2]
            float obTop = high[2]
            float obBot = math.max(low[2], high[2] - maxZoneAtr * atr)
            if obTop > obBot and obTop <= zBot + atr * 0.01
                f_pushZone(f_newZone(false, obTop, obBot, false, "OB", "OB ▲", bar_index - 2))

if newSupply and confirmed
    float zBot = high
    float zTop = math.min(low[2], high + maxZoneAtr * atr)
    bs = not na(lastSup) and close[1] < lastSup
    if f_zoneFree(true, zTop, zBot, bs ? 3 : 2)
        f_pushZone(f_newZone(true, zTop, zBot, bs, "SD", "SUPPLY" + (bs ? " ★HP" : ""), 0))
        if bullBar[2]
            float obBot = low[2]
            float obTop = math.min(high[2], low[2] + maxZoneAtr * atr)
            if obTop > obBot and obBot >= zTop - atr * 0.01
                f_pushZone(f_newZone(true, obTop, obBot, false, "OB", "OB ▼", bar_index - 2))


// ---- rejection blocks (swept pivot wick + displacement away, V2 FIX-24) -------
// CE10117 compression: the two halves were mirror copies — one helper now.
rbSwpH = high[pivLen] > ta.highest(high, pivLen * 2)[pivLen + 1]
rbDspH = ta.lowest(low, pivLen) <= high[pivLen] - dispFactor * atr
rbSwpL = low[pivLen] < ta.lowest(low, pivLen * 2)[pivLen + 1]
rbDspL = ta.highest(high, pivLen) >= low[pivLen] + dispFactor * atr

f_rbNew(bool isSup, float rbTop, float rbBot, bool ok) =>
    bool made = false
    if ok and rbTop - rbBot >= minWickAtr * atr
        bool dup = false
        if array.size(zones) > 0
            for i = array.size(zones) - 1 to 0
                z = array.get(zones, i)
                if z.isSupply == isSup and not (rbBot > z.zTop or rbTop < z.zBot)  // v5.3 F2
                    dup := true
                    break
        if not dup
            f_pushZone(f_newZone(isSup, rbTop, rbBot, false, "RB", "REJECTION " + (isSup ? "▼" : "▲"), bar_index - pivLen))
            made := true
    made

rbNew = false
if confirmed
    if f_rbNew(true, high[pivLen], math.max(open[pivLen], close[pivLen]), not na(ph) and rbSwpH and rbDspH)
        rbNew := true
    if f_rbNew(false, math.min(open[pivLen], close[pivLen]), low[pivLen], not na(pl) and rbSwpL and rbDspL)
        rbNew := true


// ---- v11 (V11-07): QUASIMODO / QML ZONE ----------------------------------------
// The classic bullish Quasimodo is L1 → H1 → L2 < L1 (the HEAD takes L1's
// sell-side liquidity) → a displaced close back above H1 (the right-shoulder
// break). The level a trader waits for — the QML — is the LEFT SHOULDER L1, the
// level that was raided; the invalidation is the head. Both are already in the
// sweep memory the instant an MSS lands: lastSslLvl IS the raided level and
// lastSslExt IS the head, and mssUp IS "external CHoCH while that raid is in
// play". So the whole pattern is available without a swing registry — v9 built
// QM out of the MODULE 12B HH/HL array and V10-18 deleted both for the token cap.
// Pushed into the v3 zone registry so it inherits the ENTIRE v10 lifecycle the
// v9 version never had: visits, mitigation %, life state, age-out, spent,
// violation/flip, the nearest-POI walk, the target map and the POI-used memory.
// f_zoneFree(.., 1) is a pure "does a live same-side zone already cover this?"
// test — it deletes nothing except an already-spent overlap, so the QM never
// evicts a legitimate FVG or order block; star = true scores it 3 so a later
// plain zone cannot evict IT.
qmNew = false
if mssUp and confirmed and not na(lastSslExt) and not na(lastSslLvl) and lastSslLvl > lastSslExt
    float qT = lastSslLvl
    float qB = math.max(lastSslExt, qT - maxZoneAtr * atr)
    if f_zoneFree(false, qT, qB, 1)
        f_pushZone(f_newZone(false, qT, qB, true, "QM", "QM ▲ QML", nz(lastSslBar, bar_index - 2)))
        qmNew := true
if mssDn and confirmed and not na(lastBslExt) and not na(lastBslLvl) and lastBslExt > lastBslLvl
    float qB = lastBslLvl
    float qT = math.min(lastBslExt, qB + maxZoneAtr * atr)
    if f_zoneFree(true, qT, qB, 1)
        f_pushZone(f_newZone(true, qT, qB, true, "QM", "QM ▼ QML", nz(lastBslBar, bar_index - 2)))
        qmNew := true

// ---- cap zone count per side (drop oldest) -------------------------------------
if newDemand or newSupply or rbNew or qmNew
    dCnt = 0
    sCnt = 0
    if array.size(zones) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(zones) - 1
            z = array.get(zones, i)
            if z.isSupply
                sCnt += 1
            else
                dCnt += 1
    if dCnt > maxZones
        for i = 0 to array.size(zones) - 1
            z = array.get(zones, i)
            if not z.isSupply
                box.delete(z.bx)
                line.delete(z.mid)
                array.remove(zones, i)
                break
    if sCnt > maxZones
        for i = 0 to array.size(zones) - 1
            z = array.get(zones, i)
            if z.isSupply
                box.delete(z.bx)
                line.delete(z.mid)
                array.remove(zones, i)
                break

// ---- NEXT buy / sell zone (nearest un-spent POI per side) ----------------------
float nbTop = na
float nbBot = na
float nsTop = na
float nsBot = na
bool  nbFresh = false
bool  nsFresh = false
int   nbLife = 0                 // v10: life state of the nearest zone (f_life)
int   nsLife = 0
bool  nbQm   = false             // v11 (V11-07): the nearest zone is a QUASIMODO QML → POI tier 3, not 4
bool  nsQm   = false
// v10 (V10-17): the Phase-7 BRK model's scan folded into this walk — nothing
// mutates `zones` between here and MODULE 16D, and its inputs (candle anatomy,
// zoneBullConf / bullPin) are settled in MODULE 3. One less per-bar array walk.
bool  brkTapL = false
bool  brkTapS = false
float brkSlL  = na
float brkSlS  = na
if array.size(zones) > 0
    for i = 0 to array.size(zones) - 1
        z = array.get(zones, i)
        t = z.zTop                              // v5.3 F2 (was box.get_top)
        b = z.zBot                              // v5.3 F2 (was box.get_bottom)
        if not z.isSupply and not z.signaled and b <= close and (na(nbTop) or t > nbTop)
            nbTop := t
            nbBot := b
            nbFresh := not z.touched or z.touchBar == bar_index
            nbLife  := f_life(z.tests, z.mit)
            nbQm    := z.kind == "QM"
        if z.isSupply and not z.signaled and t >= close and (na(nsBot) or b < nsBot)
            nsTop := t
            nsBot := b
            nsFresh := not z.touched or z.touchBar == bar_index
            nsLife  := f_life(z.tests, z.mit)
            nsQm    := z.kind == "QM"
        if z.kind == "BRK" and confirmed
            if not z.isSupply and low <= t and close >= b and (zoneBullConf or bullPin) and upWick <= body
                brkTapL := true
                brkSlL  := na(brkSlL) ? b - SL_PAD_ATR * atr : math.min(brkSlL, b - SL_PAD_ATR * atr)
            if z.isSupply and high >= b and close <= t and (zoneBearConf or bearPin) and dnWick <= body
                brkTapS := true
                brkSlS  := na(brkSlS) ? t + SL_PAD_ATR * atr : math.max(brkSlS, t + SL_PAD_ATR * atr)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 13B
// ◇ PHASE 2 (v4) — LIQUIDITY DISTANCE MAP (reduced scope)
// The full Phase-2 engine (Sydney session + pre-Asia swings, previous-week
// sweeps, touch counters, multi-tap watcher, inducement marks, internal/
// external tags, liquidity cycle) was REMOVED to fit Pine's 100,256-token
// compile budget — v3 alone consumes 69,570 of it. What survives is the
// nearest-resting-liquidity map, because the Phase-7 models measure their
// reward against it. Everything removed lives in v3's own sweep engines.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
grpP2 = "6 · Risk — liquidity target map"
p2Enable = input.bool(true, "Enable the v4 liquidity distance map", group = grpP2,
     tooltip = "Nearest resting liquidity above/below (swing, external swing, PDH/PDL, PWH/PWL, EQ pools, the next S/D zone). The target engine and the RR gate use it. v10 (V10-01): OFF now REALLY falls back to the last fresh swing + the external map (ext swing · PDH/PDL · PWH/PWL) — in v9 OFF returned na for every target and the RR gate refused every signal.")
p2MinAtr = input.float(0.5, "Ignore targets closer than (ATR ×)", step = 0.1, minval = 0, group = grpP2,
     tooltip = "v5: a level inside the entry's own noise band is not a target. Without this the nearest swing could sit a few ticks away, the measured reward was ~0, and the minimum-RR gates refused otherwise valid setups.")

// ---- distance filter: nearest resting liquidity above / below --------------------
// CE10117 compression: the same "closest level on this side" test repeated ten
// times is now one helper + one pooled loop per side. Same level set, same result.
f_p2Closer(float cur, float lvl, bool above, bool ok) =>
    float pad = p2MinAtr * atr
    ok and not na(lvl) and (above ? lvl > close + pad : lvl < close - pad) and (na(cur) or (above ? lvl < cur : lvl > cur)) ? lvl : cur

// v9 (§26): the map returns the nearest fresh level (TP1 / RR gate) AND the
// nearest fresh EXTERNAL level (ext swing · PDH/PDL · PWH/PWL) for TP2.
f_p2Dist() =>
    float eu = na
    float ed = na
    // v10 (V10-01): the external map and the last fresh swing are ALWAYS built —
    // p2Enable only adds the zone edges and the EQ pools. v9 returned na for
    // every target with the switch OFF and the RR gate then refused everything.
    eu := f_p2Closer(f_p2Closer(f_p2Closer(eu, extRes, true, not extResTaken), pdh, true, not pdhTaken), pwh, true, not pwhTaken)
    ed := f_p2Closer(f_p2Closer(f_p2Closer(ed, extSup, false, not extSupTaken), pdl, false, not pdlTaken), pwl, false, not pwlTaken)
    // v9 (§7): only FRESH levels are targets; EQ pools are deleted on touch, so they are fresh by construction
    float up = f_p2Closer(eu, lastRes, true, not resTaken)
    float dn = f_p2Closer(ed, lastSup, false, not supTaken)
    if p2Enable
        up := f_p2Closer(up, nsBot, true, true)
        dn := f_p2Closer(dn, nbTop, false, true)
        if array.size(eqhLvls) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(eqhLvls) - 1
                up := f_p2Closer(up, array.get(eqhLvls, i), true, true)
        if array.size(eqlLvls) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(eqlLvls) - 1
                dn := f_p2Closer(dn, array.get(eqlLvls, i), false, true)
    [up, dn, eu, ed]
[p2NearUp, p2NearDn, p2ExtUp, p2ExtDn] = f_p2Dist()

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 13C
// ◇ PHASE 4 (v4) — ZONES: corrected order blocks · base zones · key levels ·
// Quasimodo. One P4Zone registry, states fresh → touched → mitigated →
// broken/flipped. The v3 zone engine (M13: SD/OB/RB/BRK/MIT) is untouched.
//   ORDER BLOCK (lesson's 5 selection corrections, applied in this order):
//     5. preferred: the candle that made the ACTUAL swing extreme in the
//        lookback before the impulse, any colour (FVG attached by trigger)
//     1. impulse candle hunting the naive OB's liquidity is covered by (5) —
//        the hunted candle's extreme wins the lookback scan
//     3. if that candle is an inside bar → the mother candle is the OB
//     4. if the next candle engulfs it AND set the swing extreme → (5)
//        already selected the engulfing candle
//     2. if the OB candle fully engulfs a small-body neighbour → merge both
//   OB VALIDITY: imbalance attached (by construction) · BOS/CHoCH after
//   formation (✓shift tag, optional entry gate) · unmitigated (state).
//   INVALID OB: the OB candle's own wick already fills the attached FVG.
//   HIGH-PROBABILITY OB: formed right after a liquidity sweep (★ tag).
//   BASE ZONES: run of ≥N small-body candles then a displacement breakout →
//   DBR / RBR (demand) · RBD / DBD (supply). ★HP when trend-aligned +
//   doji-heavy base + ≥2 FVGs in the breakout leg. Opposite break FLIPS the
//   role once (demand ↔ supply — counts as a structure shift), second
//   break deletes.
//   KEY LEVELS — REMOVED in v7. The v5.3 note at the old f_p4Key already
//   proved they fed nothing (the only reads of kind == "KEY" were the creation
//   site, the colour helper and the role flip — all drawing). ~450 raw tokens
//   of display paid for the v7 arbiter and debug rows.
//   QUASIMODO: close through the last LH (needs the P1 engine) → demand zone
//   between the two lows flanking that LH; mirror for HL → supply.
// FULLY ADDITIVE: p4Enable OFF ⇒ output identical to v3+P1+P2+P3.
// Labels/lines/boxes only — the 64-output budget stays at 63.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
grpP4 = "4 · POI — corrected order blocks / Quasimodo"
p4Enable   = input.bool(true,  "Enable v4 zone engine", group = grpP4,
     tooltip = "Corrected order blocks and Quasimodo zones (the P4 families that feed the confirmation floor and the models). Base zones went in v4's size pass; KEY levels went in v7 — they fed no engine and paid for the arbiter.")
p4ShowOb   = input.bool(true,  "Corrected order blocks", group = grpP4)
p4ObLook   = 10                // v9 const: OB swing lookback
p4ReqShift = input.bool(false, "OB entry-grade needs the ✓shift (BOS/CHoCH after it)", group = grpP4)
p4Max      = 12                // v9 const

// one v4 zone: corrected OB / base / key level / Quasimodo
// v11 (V11-09): ORDER BLOCKS are the only kind this registry ever creates — KEY
// went in v7, BASE in v4's size pass, and QM moved into the MODULE 13 registry
// in v11 — so `kind`, the role-flip flag and the volume tag are gone with the
// two dispatch helpers that read them.
type P4Zone
    box    bx
    bool   isBull
    int    barC
    int    state      // 0 fresh · 1 touched · 2 mitigated (50% traded)
    bool   validated  // OB: BOS/CHoCH landed after formation
    bool   hp         // OB: formed right after a liquidity sweep (★)
    float  top        // v10 (V10-17): geometry held as data (box.get_* is na once the box cap evicts the drawing)
    float  bot

var p4Zones = array.new<P4Zone>()

// top-level series (ta.* must run every bar)
p4LowOff  = -ta.lowestbars(low, p4ObLook)[1] + 1     // offset of the swing-low candle before this bar
p4HighOff = -ta.highestbars(high, p4ObLook)[1] + 1

// v5.1a: kind + direction + ★ + a one-glyph state. ✓shift and ·vol are still
// tracked on the zone (the OB entry gate reads z.validated) — they are just
// no longer spelled out on a box that is only a few bars wide.
f_p4Txt(P4Zone z) =>
    string t = "OB" + (z.isBull ? " ▲" : " ▼")
    if z.hp
        t += " ★"
    t += z.state >= 2 ? " ·mit" : z.state == 1 ? " ·t" : ""
    t

// v5.3 F1: p4ShowOb is an INK switch, never a detection switch — p6InObL is the
// POI layer of the confirmation floor and a leg of the tier ladder, so hiding
// the family used to disable it. v11 (V11-09): the kind / visibility dispatch
// helpers are gone with the kinds they dispatched on.
f_p4New(bool isBull, float top_, float bot_, int x1, bool hp_) =>
    color c  = isBull ? COL_BULL : COL_BEAR
    bool vis = p4ShowOb
    box bxNa = na
    P4Zone z = P4Zone.new(bxNa, isBull, bar_index, 0, false, hp_, top_, bot_)
    z.bx := box.new(x1, top_, bar_index + 1, bot_,
         border_color = color.new(c, vis ? 45 : 100), border_style = line.style_dashed,
         bgcolor = color.new(c, vis ? 94 : 100), text = vis ? f_p4Txt(z) : "", text_color = p8TxtCol,
         text_size = p8TxtSz, text_halign = text.align_left,
         text_valign = isBull ? text.align_bottom : text.align_top)
    array.push(p4Zones, z)
    if array.size(p4Zones) > p4Max
        z0 = array.get(p4Zones, 0)
        box.delete(z0.bx)
        array.remove(p4Zones, 0)

// ---- corrected ORDER BLOCKS --------------------------------------------------------
// same trigger as the v3 S/D engine (FVG + displacement leg) so condition 1
// of OB validity (attached imbalance) holds by construction
p4DemTrig = p4Enable and confirmed and bullFVG and bullBar[1] and body[1] >= dispFactor * atr   // v5.3 F1
p4SupTrig = p4Enable and confirmed and bearFVG and bearBar[1] and body[1] >= dispFactor * atr   // v5.3 F1
// CE10117 compression: demand and supply scans were mirror copies — one
// direction-parameterized pass now serves both. Corrections are unchanged.
f_p4ObScan(bool trig, bool isBull) =>
    // RE10140 fix: p4LowOff / p4HighOff come from ta.lowestbars()[1], which is
    // na until p4ObLook+1 bars exist — and j is used as a HISTORY OFFSET
    // (high[j]). An na or out-of-range offset is a runtime error, so the scan
    // is skipped until the offset is real and j is clamped into [1, p4ObLook].
    int off = isBull ? p4LowOff : p4HighOff
    if trig and not na(off)
        int j = math.max(1, math.min(off, p4ObLook))               // correction 5/1/4: the swing-extreme candle wins
        if high[j] <= high[j + 1] and low[j] >= low[j + 1]         // correction 3: inside bar → mother candle
            j := math.min(j + 1, p4ObLook)
        float obTop = high[j]
        float obBot = low[j]
        if high[j] >= high[j + 1] and low[j] <= low[j + 1] and body[j + 1] <= 0.5 * body[j]
            obTop := math.max(obTop, high[j + 1])                  // correction 2: engulfed small body → merge
            obBot := math.min(obBot, low[j + 1])
        if isBull
            obTop := math.min(obTop, obBot + maxZoneAtr * atr)
        else
            obBot := math.max(obBot, obTop - maxZoneAtr * atr)
        // invalid OB: the OB candle's own wick already fills the attached FVG.
        // v5 F6: the gap runs high[2]..low (bull) / high..low[2] (bear), so the
        // edge a pre-fill would eat is high[2] / low[2] — v4 tested against the
        // far side (low / high) and accepted OBs that had already filled the gap.
        if isBull ? high[j] <= high[2] : low[j] >= low[2]
            bool dup = false
            if array.size(p4Zones) > 0
                for i = 0 to array.size(p4Zones) - 1
                    z = array.get(p4Zones, i)
                    if z.isBull == isBull and not (obBot > z.top or obTop < z.bot)   // v10 (V10-17)
                        dup := true
                        break
            if not dup
                f_p4New(isBull, obTop, obBot, bar_index - j, f_recent(isBull ? lastSslBar : lastBslBar, 5))
f_p4ObScan(p4DemTrig, true)
f_p4ObScan(p4SupTrig, false)

// ---- KEY LEVELS: removed in v7 (display-only; see the module header) --------------

// ---- QUASIMODO: removed in v10 with the P1 engine it depended on (V10-18) ----

// ---- P4 zone lifecycle: states · OB ✓shift · BASE ★HP + role flip · deletion --------
// wrapped in a function (CE10295 fix) — verbatim logic; flip events returned
// DEAD-CODE PASS (CE10117): base zones (DBR/RBR/RBD/DBD/BASE) were removed in
// the size pass, so only OB / KEY / QM are ever created and every isBase branch
// here was unreachable. The role flip survives for KEY, which does use it.
f_p4Life() =>
    if p4Enable and confirmed and array.size(p4Zones) > 0
        for i = array.size(p4Zones) - 1 to 0
            z = array.get(p4Zones, i)
            float zt = z.top                                        // v10 (V10-17)
            float zb = z.bot
            if z.isBull ? close < zb : close > zt
                box.delete(z.bx)          // v7: KEY (the only flipping kind) is gone → violated = deleted
                array.remove(p4Zones, i)
                continue
            int st0 = z.state
            bool vd0 = z.validated
            if bar_index > z.barC
                if z.isBull ? low <= zt : high >= zb
                    z.state := math.max(z.state, 1)
                if z.isBull ? low <= (zt + zb) / 2 : high >= (zt + zb) / 2
                    z.state := math.max(z.state, 2)
            if not z.validated and (z.isBull ? brokeUp or eBosUp or chochUp or eChochUp or mssUp : brokeDn or eBosDn or chochDn or eChochDn or mssDn)
                z.validated := true                                  // OB validity condition 2
            // RUNTIME: same as MODULE 12C — the caption was rebuilt for every
            // live zone on every bar. It can only change when the state moves
            // or the order block earns its ✓shift.
            if (z.state != st0 or z.validated != vd0) and p4ShowOb            // v5.3 F1
                box.set_text(z.bx, f_p4Txt(z))
f_p4Life()

// ---- nearest entry-grade corrected OB / QM per side (for Phases 6/7) ----------------
// wrapped in a function (CE10295 fix) — verbatim logic, results returned
f_p4Nearest() =>
    float p4ObBullTop = na
    float p4ObBullBot = na
    float p4ObBearTop = na
    float p4ObBearBot = na
    if p4Enable and array.size(p4Zones) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(p4Zones) - 1
            z = array.get(p4Zones, i)
            float zt = z.top                                        // v10 (V10-17)
            float zb = z.bot
            bool okOb = z.state < 2 and (not p4ReqShift or z.validated)
            if okOb and z.isBull and zt <= close and (na(p4ObBullTop) or zt > p4ObBullTop)
                p4ObBullTop := zt
                p4ObBullBot := zb
            if okOb and not z.isBull and zb >= close and (na(p4ObBearBot) or zb < p4ObBearBot)
                p4ObBearTop := zt
                p4ObBearBot := zb
    [p4ObBullTop, p4ObBullBot, p4ObBearTop, p4ObBearBot]
[p4ObBullTop, p4ObBullBot, p4ObBearTop, p4ObBearBot] = f_p4Nearest()

// keep v4 zone boxes extending on the last bar
if barstate.islast and p4Enable and array.size(p4Zones) > 0
    for i = 0 to array.size(p4Zones) - 1
        box.set_right(array.get(p4Zones, i).bx, bar_index + 1)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 14
// TRIGGER-CANDIDATE ENGINES — CRT · Turtle soup · Trendline sweep ·
// Inside bar · Doji. All context-gated, cooldown-limited, closed-bar only.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var int lastCrtLongBar  = na
var int lastCrtShortBar = na
var int lastTbsLongBar  = na
var int lastTbsShortBar = na
crtLongCd  = na(lastCrtLongBar)  or bar_index - lastCrtLongBar  > sigCooldown
crtShortCd = na(lastCrtShortBar) or bar_index - lastCrtShortBar > sigCooldown
tbsLongCd  = na(lastTbsLongBar)  or bar_index - lastTbsLongBar  > sigCooldown
tbsShortCd = na(lastTbsShortBar) or bar_index - lastTbsShortBar > sigCooldown

// CRT: Range → Raid → Reclaim → Directional delivery (all four required)
crtC1Big     = rng[2] >= crtRangeAtr * atr
crtBullSetup = crtC1Big and low[1] < low[2] and close[1] > low[2] and close[1] < high[2] and low[2] - low[1] >= minWickAtr * atr
crtBearSetup = crtC1Big and high[1] > high[2] and close[1] < high[2] and close[1] > low[2] and high[1] - high[2] >= minWickAtr * atr
sigCRTLong  = showCRT and confirmed and crtBullSetup and bullBar and close > high[1] and body >= crtDispAtr * atr and crtLongCd
sigCRTShort = showCRT and confirmed and crtBearSetup and bearBar and close < low[1] and body >= crtDispAtr * atr and crtShortCd
if sigCRTLong
    slEngL := low[1] - SL_PAD_ATR * atr
if sigCRTShort
    slEngS := high[1] + SL_PAD_ATR * atr

// Turtle soup: OLD (min AND max age) extreme + raid + decisive reclaim.
// Age math audited — see MODULE 9 note. No sign bug.
tbsLow  = ta.lowest(low, tbsLen)[1]
tbsHigh = ta.highest(high, tbsLen)[1]
tbsLowAge  = -ta.lowestbars(low, tbsLen)[1] + 1
tbsHighAge = -ta.highestbars(high, tbsLen)[1] + 1
sigTBSLong  = showTBS and confirmed and low < tbsLow and close > tbsLow and bullBar and f_tbsAgeOk(tbsLowAge) and close >= low + 0.5 * rng and tbsLongCd
sigTBSShort = showTBS and confirmed and high > tbsHigh and close < tbsHigh and bearBar and f_tbsAgeOk(tbsHighAge) and close <= high - 0.5 * rng and tbsShortCd
if sigTBSLong
    slEngL := low - SL_PAD_ATR * atr
if sigTBSShort
    slEngS := high + SL_PAD_ATR * atr
// v10 (V10-16): the HTF CRT / turtle-soup candidates propose the HTF raid
// candle's extreme, not the 2-bar chart-TF fallback (which made RR look superb)
if sigHCrtLong or sigHTbsLong
    slEngL := math.min(nz(hSlL, low), low) - SL_PAD_ATR * atr
if sigHCrtShort or sigHTbsShort
    slEngS := math.max(nz(hSlS, high), high) + SL_PAD_ATR * atr

// Trendline liquidity: candidate → validated → sweep entry / break (FIX-19)
float tlUpVal = not na(tlUpSlope) ? tlUpPrice + tlUpSlope * (bar_index - tlUpBar) : na
float tlDnVal = not na(tlDnSlope) ? tlDnPrice + tlDnSlope * (bar_index - tlDnBar) : na
sigTLLong  = false
sigTLShort = false
tlUpBreak  = false
tlDnBreak  = false
if not na(tlUpVal) and confirmed
    if close < tlUpVal
        tlUpBreak := true
        if not na(tlUpLn)
            line.set_extend(tlUpLn, extend.none)
            line.set_x2(tlUpLn, bar_index)
            line.set_style(tlUpLn, line.style_dashed)
        tlUpLn    := na
        tlUpSlope := na
    else if low < tlUpVal
        tlUpTouch += tlUpAway ? 1 : 0
        if tlSweepEnt and tlUpAway and tlUpTouch >= 2 and (not tlNeedConf or zoneBullConf)
            sigTLLong := true
            slEngL := low - SL_PAD_ATR * atr
        tlUpAway := false
    else if low <= tlUpVal + NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr
        tlUpTouch += tlUpAway ? 1 : 0
        tlUpAway := false
    else
        tlUpAway := true
if not na(tlDnVal) and confirmed
    if close > tlDnVal
        tlDnBreak := true
        if not na(tlDnLn)
            line.set_extend(tlDnLn, extend.none)
            line.set_x2(tlDnLn, bar_index)
            line.set_style(tlDnLn, line.style_dashed)
        tlDnLn    := na
        tlDnSlope := na
    else if high > tlDnVal
        tlDnTouch += tlDnAway ? 1 : 0
        if tlSweepEnt and tlDnAway and tlDnTouch >= 2 and (not tlNeedConf or zoneBearConf)
            sigTLShort := true
            slEngS := high + SL_PAD_ATR * atr
        tlDnAway := false
    else if high >= tlDnVal - NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr
        tlDnTouch += tlDnAway ? 1 : 0
        tlDnAway := false
    else
        tlDnAway := true
if not na(tlUpLn) and tlUpTouch >= 1
    line.set_style(tlUpLn, line.style_solid)
if not na(tlDnLn) and tlDnTouch >= 1
    line.set_style(tlDnLn, line.style_solid)

// Inside bar breakout (context-gated: structure + HTF + strong close, FIX-22)
var int   ibStage = 0
var float mHigh   = na
var float mLow    = na
var float ibHigh  = na
var float ibLow   = na
var int   ibStart = na
sig3Long  = false
sig3Short = false
mMid = (mHigh + mLow) / 2
if confirmed
    if ibStage == 1
        if high < mHigh and low > mLow and low >= mMid
            ibHigh := high
            ibLow  := low
            ibStage := 2
        else
            ibStage := 0
    else if ibStage == 2
        if close > ibHigh
            if bullBar and body >= BRK_BODY_ATR * atr and close >= high - STRONG_CLOSE_PCT * rng and structDir >= 0 and htfB >= 0
                sig3Long := showS3
                if showS3
                    slEngL := math.min(ibLow, low) - SL_PAD_ATR * atr     // v10 (V10-16): inside-bar low
            ibStage := 0
        else if close < ibLow or bar_index - ibStart > IB_WAIT_BARS
            ibStage := 0
    else if ibStage == -1
        if high < mHigh and low > mLow and high <= mMid
            ibHigh := high
            ibLow  := low
            ibStage := -2
        else
            ibStage := 0
    else if ibStage == -2
        if close < ibLow
            if bearBar and body >= BRK_BODY_ATR * atr and close <= low + STRONG_CLOSE_PCT * rng and structDir <= 0 and htfB <= 0
                sig3Short := showS3
                if showS3
                    slEngS := math.max(ibHigh, high) + SL_PAD_ATR * atr   // v10 (V10-16)
            ibStage := 0
        else if close > ibHigh or bar_index - ibStart > IB_WAIT_BARS
            ibStage := 0
    if showS3 and ibStage == 0 and brokeUp and body >= ibBodyAtr * atr
        ibStage := 1
        mHigh := high
        mLow  := low
        ibStart := bar_index
    else if showS3 and ibStage == 0 and brokeDn and body >= ibBodyAtr * atr
        ibStage := -1
        mHigh := high
        mLow  := low
        ibStart := bar_index

// Doji reversal (compression + level raid + displacement confirm, FIX-23)
dojiRecent = math.sum(doji ? 1 : 0, DOJI_WINDOW)
ctxBias = structDir != 0 ? structDir : htfB
dojiCompressed = ta.sma(rng, DOJI_WINDOW)[1] <= atr
dojiHi = ta.highest(high, DOJI_WINDOW)
dojiLo = ta.lowest(low, DOJI_WINDOW)
dojiRaidRes    = not na(lastRes) and dojiHi > lastRes and close < lastRes
dojiRaidSup    = not na(lastSup) and dojiLo < lastSup and close > lastSup
sig4Short = false
sig4Long  = false
if showS4 and confirmed
    atRes   = not na(lastRes) and high >= lastRes - NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr and close <= lastRes + NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr
    atSup   = not na(lastSup) and low <= lastSup + NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr and close >= lastSup - NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr
    driftUp = close[1] > close[DOJI_WINDOW + 1]
    driftDn = close[1] < close[DOJI_WINDOW + 1]
    dispConf = body >= BRK_BODY_ATR * atr
    if ctxBias == -1 and dojiRecent[1] >= dojiMin and atRes and driftUp and dojiCompressed and dojiRaidRes and bearConfirm and dispConf
        sig4Short := true
        slEngS := math.max(dojiHi, high) + SL_PAD_ATR * atr      // v10 (V10-16): the raid extreme
    if ctxBias == 1 and dojiRecent[1] >= dojiMin and atSup and driftDn and dojiCompressed and dojiRaidSup and bullConfirm and dispConf
        sig4Long := true
        slEngL := math.min(dojiLo, low) - SL_PAD_ATR * atr

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 14B
// ◇ PHASE 5 (v4) — PATTERN HELPERS (reduced scope)
// The full 12-pattern library (spec-IFC + double IFC, piercing, stars,
// manipulative candle, fakey, dual trap, long-wick rejection, CISD
// reliability score, verify chips) was REMOVED for the token budget.
// The four booleans the surviving engines consume are kept: a configurable-
// ratio pin bar (breaker entries + breakout classifier), the inside-bar
// flag, and the CPC continuation pin bar.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// name accumulator shared by the Phase-7 model labels
f_p5Add(string acc, bool c, string nm) => c ? (acc == "" ? nm : acc + "+" + nm) : acc



// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 15
// FRACTAL ENTRY MODEL (FEM) — HTF POI → tap → LTF shift → LOCKED LTF FVG →
// retest execution. V2 FIX-11 preserved: the first valid FVG is locked, later
// FVGs never overwrite it, a close through it kills the chain.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var int   femL    = 0
var int   femLBar = na
var float femLTop = na
var float femLBot = na
var int   femLFvg = na
var int   femS    = 0
var int   femSBar = na
var float femSTop = na
var float femSBot = na
var int   femSFvg = na
sigFEMLong  = false
sigFEMShort = false
if useFEM and confirmed
    if femL >= 1 and (na(hPoiBTop) or bar_index - femLBar > femWait)
        femL := 0
    if femL == 0 and htfLive and not na(hPoiBTop) and low <= hPoiBTop and close > hPoiBBot
        femL    := 1
        femLBar := bar_index
        femLTop := na
        femLBot := na
        femLFvg := na
    // v5.2 W3: bosUp is CONTINUATION, not a shift — the fractal model wants a
    // change of state after the HTF POI tap. Swapped for the external CHoCH.
    // The 5-bar internal chochUp stays: FEM is explicitly an LTF-confirmation
    // model, which is why mcShiftExt does not reach in here.
    if femL == 1 and (cisdUp or chochUp or eChochUp or mssUp)
        femL := 2
        if not na(cFvgBTop) and cFvgBBar > femLBar
            femLTop := cFvgBTop
            femLBot := cFvgBBot
            femLFvg := cFvgBBar
            femL    := 3
    if femL == 2 and bullFVG
        femLTop := low
        femLBot := high[2]
        femLFvg := bar_index
        femL    := 3
    if femL == 3
        if close < femLBot
            femL := 0
        else if bar_index > femLFvg and low <= femLTop and close > femLBot and zoneBullConf
            sigFEMLong := true
            slEngL := math.min(low, femLBot) - SL_PAD_ATR * atr
            femL := 0
    if femS >= 1 and (na(hPoiSTop) or bar_index - femSBar > femWait)
        femS := 0
    if femS == 0 and htfLive and not na(hPoiSTop) and high >= hPoiSBot and close < hPoiSTop
        femS    := 1
        femSBar := bar_index
        femSTop := na
        femSBot := na
        femSFvg := na
    if femS == 1 and (cisdDn or chochDn or eChochDn or mssDn)
        femS := 2
        if not na(cFvgSTop) and cFvgSBar > femSBar
            femSTop := cFvgSTop
            femSBot := cFvgSBot
            femSFvg := cFvgSBar
            femS    := 3
    if femS == 2 and bearFVG
        femSBot := high
        femSTop := low[2]
        femSFvg := bar_index
        femS    := 3
    if femS == 3
        if close > femSTop
            femS := 0
        else if bar_index > femSFvg and high >= femSBot and close < femSTop and zoneBearConf
            sigFEMShort := true
            slEngS := math.max(high, femSTop) + SL_PAD_ATR * atr
            femS := 0

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 16
// POI LOCATION · QUALITY ENGINES · TIER LADDER · CONTEXT GATES
// v10 (V10-10): the v3 alignment score (context 30 · liquidity 20 · POI 20 ·
// trigger 20 · execution 10) is REPLACED by the ENTRY QUALITY SCORE in
// MODULE 18 (f_score), which is computed after the machine and the target
// engine have spoken and can only REMOVE a tier. The tier ladder below keeps
// the HARD gates; the score is the soft layer over it.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// v8: the six P6 POI-location booleans moved up here from MODULE 16C — the tier
// ladder now reads them (A = AT a zone / corrected OB / entry-grade FVG).
p6InObL  = not na(p4ObBullTop) and low <= p4ObBullTop and close >= p4ObBullBot
p6InObS  = not na(p4ObBearBot) and high >= p4ObBearBot and close <= p4ObBearTop
p6InFvgL = not na(p3BullTop) and low <= p3BullTop and close >= p3BullBot
p6InFvgS = not na(p3BearBot) and high >= p3BearBot and close <= p3BearTop
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 16E
// ◈ v8 QUALITY ENGINES — soft scores. They can only REMOVE a tier (A needs
// exec ≥ v8ExecA, A+ needs exec ≥ v8ExecAp and a clean path); they never add one.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
volAvg = ta.sma(volume, 20)
volExp = not na(volume) and volume > 0 and volAvg > 0 and volume >= 1.3 * volAvg
// EXECUTION QUALITY (V8-08) of THIS candle as a confirmation in direction isL
// v10 (V10-16): body 15 · close location 15 · displacement 20 · liquidity
// reclaim 15 · structure / CISD 10 · FVG created 10 · volume 5 · WICK REJECTION
// 10 = 100. A pin bar earns its wick, an engulfing its body; a CISD close in the
// middle of nowhere scores the structure points and little else.
f_execQ(bool isL) =>
    float br = rng > 0 ? body / rng : 0
    float cl = rng > 0 ? (isL ? close - low : high - close) / rng : 0
    float wk = rng > 0 ? (isL ? dnWick : upWick) / rng : 0
    int q = br >= 0.6 ? 15 : br >= 0.4 ? 8 : 0
    q += cl >= 0.8 ? 15 : cl >= 0.65 ? 8 : 0
    q += body >= dispFactor * atr ? 20 : body >= BRK_BODY_ATR * atr ? 10 : 0
    q += (isL ? sslInPlay and low <= lastSslLvl and close > lastSslLvl : bslInPlay and high >= lastBslLvl and close < lastBslLvl) ? 15 : 0
    q += (isL ? accBrokeUp or eAccUp or cisdUp : accBrokeDn or eAccDn or cisdDn) ? 10 : 0
    q += (isL ? bullFVG : bearFVG) ? 10 : 0
    q += volExp ? 5 : 0
    q += wk >= 0.5 and (isL ? dnWick : upWick) >= minWickAtr * atr ? 10 : wk >= 0.33 ? 5 : 0
    math.min(100, q)
execQL = f_execQ(true)
execQS = f_execQ(false)
// CLEAN PATH (V8-11): opposing corrected OB · entry-grade FVG · HTF POI · fresh
// opposing S/D zone strictly between entry and the target. 100 = clean, −35 per
// obstacle. v10: takes the target — the ladder measures to the nearest opposing
// liquidity (TP1), MODULE 18 measures again to the selected TP2.
f_path(bool isL, float tgt) =>
    int n = 0
    if not na(tgt)
        float o1 = isL ? p4ObBearBot : p4ObBullTop
        float o2 = isL ? p3BearBot : p3BullTop
        float o3 = htfLive ? (isL ? hPoiSBot : hPoiBTop) : na
        float o4 = isL ? nsBot : nbTop
        n += not na(o1) and (isL ? o1 > close and o1 < tgt : o1 < close and o1 > tgt) ? 1 : 0
        n += not na(o2) and (isL ? o2 > close and o2 < tgt : o2 < close and o2 > tgt) ? 1 : 0
        n += not na(o3) and (isL ? o3 > close and o3 < tgt : o3 < close and o3 > tgt) ? 1 : 0
        n += not na(o4) and o4 != tgt and (isL ? o4 > close and o4 < tgt : o4 < close and o4 > tgt) ? 1 : 0
    na(tgt) ? 0 : math.max(0, 100 - 35 * n)
pathL = f_path(true,  p2NearUp)
pathS = f_path(false, p2NearDn)

inDemand   = not na(nbTop) and close <= nbTop
nearDemand = not na(nbTop) and not inDemand and close - nbTop <= POI_NEAR_ATR * atr
inSupply   = not na(nsBot) and close >= nsBot
nearSupply = not na(nsBot) and not inSupply and nsBot - close <= POI_NEAR_ATR * atr
// v9 (§9): POI TIER of the entry candle's location — 1 HTF FVG POI · 2 corrected
// OB / entry-grade typed FVG · 3 OTE / QM / BPR retest · 4 generic S/D zone ·
// 5 none. A+ needs ≤ 2 (the machine reads its own suLPoiT); a generic zone caps
// at A. A weak generic zone no longer competes equally with an HTF POI.
// v11 (V11-07): a QUASIMODO QML tap re-enters the ladder at tier 3, where v9 had it.
poiTL = htfLocL ? 1 : p6InObL or p6InFvgL ? 2 : inOTEbuy or p3BprTapUp or (inDemand and nbQm) ? 3 : inDemand ? 4 : 5
poiTS = htfLocS ? 1 : p6InObS or p6InFvgS ? 2 : inOTEsell or p3BprTapDn or (inSupply and nsQm) ? 3 : inSupply ? 4 : 5

retestLong  = not na(nbTop) and low <= nbTop and close >= nbBot
retestShort = not na(nsBot) and high >= nsBot and close <= nsTop

// ---- tier grading (ARCH-2) ------------------------------------------------------
// C = bare trigger · B = trigger + (liquidity OR poi) · A = liquidity + POI +
// structure trigger + execution · A+ = A + HTF + session + strong sweep + P/D.
// v8: one direction-generic ladder (the two mirrors were identical).
//   B  = trigger + (liquidity OR poi)
//   A  = liquidity in play + AT an institutional POI (zone / corrected OB /
//        entry-grade FVG — V8-04) + EXTERNAL shift with a displacement body in
//        the trigger window + trade-window session + a PRESENT confirmation
//        candle scoring ≥ v8ExecA (V8-08)
//   A+ = A + filter EMA + HTF alignment ≥ v8ApHtf + CORE session + sweep grade
//        ≥ 3 of type ≥ v8ApLiq + correct range side + exec ≥ v8ExecAp + clean
//        path + no correlated conflict. The arbiter may still demote it.
// v10 exec threshold for A: LOW volatility demands a stronger candle (V10-13)
// v11 (V11-05): f_execQ is capped at 100, so an unclamped +10 made tier A
// unreachable in a quiet tape at high v8ExecA settings.
execAEff = math.min(100, v8ExecA + (volReg == 0 ? 10 : 0))
f_tier(bool isL) =>
    bool hasLiq  = isL ? sslInPlay : bslInPlay                                       // (v9: liqLong ≥ 10 ⇔ sweep in play)
    bool hasPoi  = isL ? inDemand or nearDemand or inOTEbuy : inSupply or nearSupply or inOTEsell   // (v9: poiLong ≥ 5)
    bool hasTrig = isL ? recentMssUp or recentChUp or recentCisdUp : recentMssDn or recentChDn or recentCisdDn
    // v10 (V10-02 / V10-03): the structure leg is the CAUSAL CHAIN — an external
    // shift with ITS OWN displacement (on the shift candle or ≤ maxDispDelay
    // after), graded by age (≤ mssAgeA for A, ≤ mssAgeAp for A+), and the shift
    // bar must precede the entry bar (v9: one candle cannot be the shift AND its
    // own retest). v9 accepted any MSS in 10 bars + any big candle in 10 bars.
    int  ageQ    = isL ? shAgeQL : shAgeQS
    bool aTrig   = (isL ? chainL : chainS) and ageQ >= 1 and sesQ >= 3 and (isL ? shUpBar : shDnBar) < bar_index
    bool atPoi   = isL ? inDemand or p6InObL or p6InFvgL : inSupply or p6InObS or p6InFvgS
    // v10 (V10-06): a WEAK / DEAD zone is not an institutional POI (A needs life ≤ 2, A+ ≤ 1)
    bool lifeA   = isL ? not inDemand or nbLife <= 2 : not inSupply or nsLife <= 2
    bool lifeAp  = isL ? not inDemand or nbLife <= 1 : not inSupply or nsLife <= 1
    int  ex      = isL ? execQL : execQS
    bool hasExec = (isL ? zoneBullConf : zoneBearConf) and ex >= execAEff
    int tier = 1
    if hasTrig and (hasLiq or hasPoi)
        tier := 2
    if hasLiq and atPoi and lifeA and aTrig and hasExec
        tier := 3
    // A+ (LEVEL 3): + fresh shift (≤ mssAgeAp) · the shift-leg FVG exists · HTF bias + alignment · CORE
    // session · strong sweep of type ≥ v8ApLiq · correct range side · exec · clean path · no correlated conflict · POI tier ≤ 2 · first touch
    if tier == 3 and ageQ >= 2 and (isL ? chainFvgL : chainFvgS) and lifeAp and (isL ? htfB > 0 : htfB < 0) and (isL ? htfAlnL : htfAlnS) >= v8ApHtf and sesQ == 4 and (isL ? lastSslQual : lastBslQual) >= 3 and (isL ? lastSslType : lastBslType) >= v8ApLiq and rangeOK and (isL ? pdPos < 0.5 : pdPos >= 0.5) and ex >= v8ExecAp and (isL ? pathL : pathS) >= V8_PATH_AP and (isL ? corrB >= 0 : corrB <= 0) and (isL ? poiTL : poiTS) <= 2
        tier := 4
    tier
tierLong  = f_tier(true)
tierShort = f_tier(false)
minRank = tierMode == "A+ only" ? 4 : tierMode == "A and above" ? 3 : tierMode == "B and above" ? 2 : 1
f_tierTxt(int t) => t == 4 ? "A+" : t == 3 ? "A" : t == 2 ? "B" : "C"

// ---- master CONTEXT gates (bias · killzone · news · chop · score) --------------
// v5.2 V1: these lived in MODULE 18, four hundred lines BELOW the liquidity-trap
// engine, which is the only reason the trap engine was never gated by them.
// Nothing about them needs to be that late — every input is settled by here —
// so they move up and MODULE 16B can finally see them. MODULE 18 keeps the
// cooldown half (longOK / shortOK), which does have to stay after the signals.
// v7 F: the institutional exception needs the institutional sweep to be IN PLAY.
// lastSslQual is only rewritten by the NEXT sweep, so after any MSS it held 4
// for hours and the CHOP filter was silently off for that side.
chopOKL = not useRegime or regime != "CHOP" or (sslInPlay and lastSslQual >= 4)
chopOKS = not useRegime or regime != "CHOP" or (bslInPlay and lastBslQual >= 4)
// v10 (V10-15): HTF LOCATION passes the bias filter only with an LTF REVERSAL
// MODEL behind it — a sweep in play AND an external shift. An HTF POI on its own
// never justifies a counter-trend entry. The score gate (minScore) moved to
// MODULE 18, where the entry score exists.
htfRevL  = v9HtfLoc and htfLocL and sslInPlay and (recentMssUp or extChUpRec)
htfRevS  = v9HtfLoc and htfLocS and bslInPlay and (recentMssDn or extChDnRec)
longCtx  = cfgOK and (biasFilter == "Off" or filtBias >= 0 or htfRevL) and kzOK and newsOK and chopOKL
shortCtx = cfgOK and (biasFilter == "Off" or filtBias <= 0 or htfRevS) and kzOK and newsOK and chopOKS

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 16C
// ◇ PHASE 6 (v4) — POI LOCATION HELPERS (reduced scope)
// The full filter/confluence layer (weight-adjustable score, pullback and
// approach quality, FOMO trap, trend-only, inducement, parabolic break,
// volume layer, correlated symbol, HTF ladder, debug breakdown, master
// gate) was REMOVED for the token budget; v3's own score, tiers and gates
// still run untouched. What survives is where price sits relative to the
// v4 zones — the Phase-7 models need it to place entries.
// v8: the six booleans now live in MODULE 16 (above the tier ladder).
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 16D
// ◇ PHASE 7 (v4) — TRADE MODELS AS CANDIDATES (v7 relocation)
// In v5.3 this sat in MODULE 18B, AFTER the arbiter, with its own finalize:
// own RR gate (na target passed), own cooldown, own conflict rule, own E/SL/TP
// lines, own label, own alert() and the [v4] alertcondition — a second final
// decision-maker beside the v3 stack, and the two could disagree or double-
// print on one bar. v7 moves the model detection ABOVE the confirmation floor
// so SB · QM · BRK · FVG4 are graded like every other trigger and surface only
// as a line inside the single signal label. The CLS breakout classifier stays
// in MODULE 18B (labels only). p7MinRr / p7Cd / p7AlertRr / p7ShowTrade /
// p7Alert / p8Trail / p8TradeBars are gone with the code they served.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
grpP7 = "5 · Entry — trade models (SB · QM · BRK · FVG4)"
p7Enable  = input.bool(true,  "Enable v4 trade models", group = grpP7,
     tooltip = "Master switch. OFF ⇒ output identical to the phases before it.")
p7Win     = 15                // v9 const: model stage window
p7mSb     = input.bool(true,  "SB — Silver Bullet", group = grpP7)
p7SbSes   = input.bool(true,  "SB — the WHOLE sequence must sit inside a Silver Bullet window (v11)", group = grpP7,
     tooltip = "v11 (V11-08): ICT's Silver Bullet is a MACRO-WINDOW model — liquidity is taken, price displaces and shifts, and the entry is the FVG that displacement leg itself created, all inside the killzone hour (03:00-04:00 / 10:00-11:00 / 14:00-15:00 NY by default). v10 gated only the ENTRY on the window, so a 20:00 raid could arm a 10:15 entry through the 15-bar stage budget. ON: the raid, the shift and the entry must all print inside a window. OFF: the window is ignored entirely (the model is then just sweep → shift → shift-leg FVG).")
p7mQm     = input.bool(true,  "QM — Quasimodo (QML retest)", group = grpP7,
     tooltip = "v11 (V11-07): the QUASIMODO level (QML) is the LEFT SHOULDER — the swing low whose sell-side liquidity the head raided before the right-shoulder break (mirror for shorts). The zone is built in MODULE 13 on every MSS from the sweep memory, so it carries the full zone lifecycle (visits, mitigation, life state, age). This model enters on a confirmed rejection inside that zone, with the stop under the head.")
p7mBrk    = input.bool(true,  "BRK — breaker block model", group = grpP7)
p7mFvg4   = input.bool(true,  "FVG4 — FVG + liquidity 4-confirmation", group = grpP7)

f_p7SlL(float cur, float sl) => na(cur) ? sl : math.min(cur, sl)
f_p7SlS(float cur, float sl) => na(cur) ? sl : math.max(cur, sl)

// SB is a 3-stage narrative (sweep → shift → retrace entry); one helper keeps
// its own state per call site, so long and short run independently.
f_p7Sb(bool arm, bool shift, bool entry) =>
    var int st  = 0
    var int bar_ = na
    bool fired = false
    if st >= 1 and bar_index - bar_ > p7Win
        st := 0
    if st == 0 and arm
        st   := 1
        bar_ := bar_index
    // v11 (V11-02): every stage needs a LATER bar than the one before it. v10
    // walked 0→1→2→fire inside a single bar pass, so a sweep + MSS + FVG tap on
    // ONE candle was a complete three-stage narrative — the same event counted
    // three times. That is the double-count V9-07 closed in the tier ladder and
    // left open here.
    if st == 1 and shift and bar_index > bar_
        st   := 2
        bar_ := bar_index
    if st == 2 and entry and bar_index > bar_
        fired := true
        st    := 0
    [st, fired]

f_p7Models() =>
    bool qmL = false
    bool qmS = false
    bool bkL = false
    bool bkS = false
    bool f4L = false
    bool f4S = false
    float slL = na
    float slS = na
    // ---- SB: v11 (V11-08) SILVER BULLET, MACRO-WINDOW FIDELITY ----------------
    // ICT's rule is that the WHOLE sequence happens inside the killzone hour:
    // liquidity is taken, price displaces and shifts, and the entry is the FVG
    // that displacement leg itself created. v10 gated only the ENTRY on the
    // window (a 20:00 raid could arm a 10:15 entry through the p7Win budget),
    // armed on a PDH/PDL sweep ALONE — the two levels ICT is least specific
    // about, and a level that is often not even in the window — and entered on
    // ANY nearest entry-grade FVG, so a gap from hours earlier could be the
    // trigger. v11:
    //   arm    any quality sweep of the UNIFIED liquidity memory (swing · EQ ·
    //          session · PD · ext swing · PW · breakout trap) printed THIS bar,
    //          inside the window, graded >= minArmQual
    //   shift  external CHoCH / MSS, inside the window, on a LATER bar (V11-02)
    //   entry  the SHIFT LEG'S OWN FVG (the f_shift lineage, inShFvgL / inShFvgS
    //          — created between the raid and maxFvgDelay bars after the shift,
    //          creation bar excluded), inside the window, on the right side of
    //          the dealing range, with a confirmation candle
    // The stop goes under the FVG and the raid wick, not under the entry candle.
    bool sbWin = not p7SbSes or not timeframe.isintraday or inSB
    [sbStL, sbL] = f_p7Sb(p7Enable and p7mSb and confirmed and sbWin and sslInPlay and lastSslBar == bar_index and lastSslQual >= minArmQual,
         p7Enable and confirmed and sbWin and (mssUp or eChochUp),
         p7Enable and confirmed and p7mSb and sbWin and inShFvgL and rangeOK and pdPos < 0.5 and zoneBullConf)
    [sbStS, sbS] = f_p7Sb(p7Enable and p7mSb and confirmed and sbWin and bslInPlay and lastBslBar == bar_index and lastBslQual >= minArmQual,
         p7Enable and confirmed and sbWin and (mssDn or eChochDn),
         p7Enable and confirmed and p7mSb and sbWin and inShFvgS and rangeOK and pdPos >= 0.5 and zoneBearConf)
    if sbL
        slL := f_p7SlL(slL, math.min(math.min(low, nz(shUpFvgB, low)), nz(lastSslExt, low)) - SL_PAD_ATR * atr)
    if sbS
        slS := f_p7SlS(slS, math.max(math.max(high, nz(shDnFvgT, high)), nz(lastBslExt, high)) + SL_PAD_ATR * atr)
    if p7Enable and confirmed
        // ---- QM: v11 (V11-07) a confirmed rejection inside the QUASIMODO QML.
        // The zone is the left shoulder — the level the head raided — built in
        // MODULE 13 on the MSS, so it arrives with the full zone lifecycle: this
        // model only has to ask whether price is AT it with a rejection candle.
        // The stop sits under the zone (the head), which is the pattern's own
        // invalidation, not under the entry candle.
        if p7mQm and nbQm and inDemand and retestLong and zoneBullConf
            qmL := true
            slL := f_p7SlL(slL, math.min(low, nbBot) - SL_PAD_ATR * atr)
        if p7mQm and nsQm and inSupply and retestShort and zoneBearConf
            qmS := true
            slS := f_p7SlS(slS, math.max(high, nsTop) + SL_PAD_ATR * atr)
        // ---- BRK: reversal / pin inside a v3 BREAKER zone (scan folded into the
        // MODULE 13 nearest-POI walk in v10 — same test, same stop) -----------
        if p7mBrk and brkTapL
            bkL := true
            slL := f_p7SlL(slL, brkSlL)
        if p7mBrk and brkTapS
            bkS := true
            slS := f_p7SlS(slS, brkSlS)
        // ---- FVG4: BSI/SBI + BOS overlap + prior grab + reversal in the gap --
        if p7mFvg4 and (sslInPlay or recentEngLo) and zoneBullConf and array.size(p3Bull) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(p3Bull) - 1
                f = array.get(p3Bull, i)
                if bar_index > f.barC and f.bsi and f.bosOverlap and f.mit < p3MitTh and low <= f.top and close >= f.bot
                    f4L := true
                    slL := f_p7SlL(slL, f.bot - SL_PAD_ATR * atr)
                    break
        if p7mFvg4 and (bslInPlay or recentEngHi) and zoneBearConf and array.size(p3Bear) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(p3Bear) - 1
                f = array.get(p3Bear, i)
                if bar_index > f.barC and f.bsi and f.bosOverlap and f.mit < p3MitTh and high >= f.bot and close <= f.top
                    f4S := true
                    slS := f_p7SlS(slS, f.top + SL_PAD_ATR * atr)
                    break
    string txtL = ""
    txtL := f_p5Add(txtL, sbL, "SB")
    txtL := f_p5Add(txtL, qmL, "QM")
    txtL := f_p5Add(txtL, bkL, "BRK")
    txtL := f_p5Add(txtL, f4L, "FVG4")
    string txtS = ""
    txtS := f_p5Add(txtS, sbS, "SB")
    txtS := f_p5Add(txtS, qmS, "QM")
    txtS := f_p5Add(txtS, bkS, "BRK")
    txtS := f_p5Add(txtS, f4S, "FVG4")
    [txtL, txtS, slL, slS, sbStL, sbStS]
[p7TxtL, p7TxtS, p7SlL, p7SlS, p7SbStL, p7SbStS] = f_p7Models()
// v7 AGG: a model fire is a CANDIDATE, not a decision. Its stop joins the shared
// stop slot here (weakest → strongest order: zones → engines → FEM → models →
// machine) so the confirmation floor and the arbiter measure the same risk the
// model proposes. SB and FVG4 are narrative-class (sweep → shift → POI, or
// liquidity + BSI + BOS overlap); QM and BRK are technical-class.
sigP7Long  = p7Enable and confirmed and p7TxtL != ""
sigP7Short = p7Enable and confirmed and p7TxtS != ""
slP7L := p7SlL
slP7S := p7SlS
p7NarL = str.contains(p7TxtL, "SB") or str.contains(p7TxtL, "FVG4")
p7NarS = str.contains(p7TxtS, "SB") or str.contains(p7TxtS, "FVG4")

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 16B
// ◬ LIQUIDITY TRAP ENGINE (LT-1 … LT-7) — REMOVED in v10 (V10-18) to clear
// CE10117 (compiled 106,706 tokens against the 100,256 cap on first load).
// It was the first lever named in the v10 header and AUDIT-v10.md §9: ~280
// dense lines, a CANDIDATE producer (never a final decision since v7), and
// structurally short-biased (5 short patterns vs 2 long). The trap CONCEPT
// survives where it matters most: the MODULE 5 breakout-trap classifier
// (f_brkTrap) writes an accepted-then-failed break into the sweep memory as a
// type-7 grade-3 liquidity event, so trap → MSS → displacement → shift-leg FVG
// → first retest arms and grades through the primary setup machine. The
// full engine is preserved in Demand + Price Action-9.pine (MODULE 16B) and
// belongs in a companion indicator if it is wanted back.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 17
// MASTER SETUP STATE MACHINE (ARCH-1) — the primary signal path
//   0 IDLE → 1 SWEPT (quality ≥ minArmQual) → 2 AT POI → 3 SHIFTED
//   (MSS/CHoCH/CISD, retest anchor locked) → ENTRY → 4 ACTIVE → 0.
// Edge-triggered, stage expiry, explicit invalidation with a reason string.
// CHOP suppression with the institutional-sweep exception (ARCH-5).
// v10 (V10-07): ONE direction-generic function. The long and short machines
// were ~110-line mirror copies at global scope; every rule now lives once, the
// state is function-local `var`, and the machine RESOLVES ITSELF: a refused
// entry (M18) and a finished trade (own SL / TP2) release stage 4 through the
// accPrev / tgtPrev parameters instead of outside writes into its state.
//   near = the anchor edge price enters first (top of a demand anchor, bottom
//   of a supply anchor) · far = the edge whose violation kills the anchor.
// v10 (V10-05): a RETEST is a VISIT with a start bar, a DWELL (bars inside) and
// a DEPTH (deepest penetration as a fraction of the anchor height). Dwell
// beyond maxRetDwell = the first retest FAILED (price is accepting the level).
// v10 (V10-02 / V10-08): a displacement inside maxDispDelay bars after the shift
// upgrades the shift grade (it belongs to the shift); no shift-leg FVG inside
// maxFvgDelay bars and no tapped zone = "no shift-leg FVG" → invalidated.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var setupCtr = array.new<int>(1, 0)          // SETUP-n counter (arrays may be mutated inside functions)
var bool   mcAccL = false                    // M18's verdict on the machine's entry bar (read the bar after)
var bool   mcAccS = false
var float  mcTgtL = na                       // M19's real TP2 for an accepted machine entry
var float  mcTgtS = na
var string rejL = "—"                        // last refusal reason per side (M18 writes, dashboard + machine read)
var string rejS = "—"

f_machine(bool isL, bool inPlay, int lastBar, int lastQual, int lastType, int lastSes, float lastExt,
     bool tapZone, float zNear, float zFar, bool tapOte, bool tapHtf,
     bool shiftExt, bool shiftCisd, int dispQ, float fNear, float fFar, int fBar,
     bool zoneInv, bool oppDisp, bool conf, bool accPrev, string rejPrev, float tgtPrev) =>
    var int    st       = 0
    var int    stBar    = na
    var float  aNear    = na       // retest anchor (locked FVG or POI zone)
    var float  aFar     = na
    var int    fvgBar   = na       // anchor creation bar (na = zone anchor)
    var float  swExt    = na       // arming sweep wick — invalidation + SL anchor
    var string reason   = ""       // last invalidation / expiry / refusal reason
    var int    qual     = 0        // v7 memory: arming sweep grade · type · session
    var int    typ      = 0
    var int    ses      = 0
    var int    mQ       = 0        // shift grade — 1 CISD-only · 2 external · 3 external + displacement
    var int    poiT     = 5        // POI tier — 1 HTF POI · 2 OB / shift-leg FVG · 3 OTE / QM · 4 generic S/D · 5 none
    var int    visit    = 0        // separate retest VISITS of the anchor (1 = the FIRST retest)
    var bool   wasIn    = false    // price overlapped the anchor on the previous bar
    var int    legBar   = na       // bar the current leg began (arm / POI tap)
    var int    armBar   = na       // the arming sweep bar (journal: sweep age)
    var int    id       = 0        // v10: SETUP-n
    var int    shBar    = na       // v10: the shift bar (lineage)
    var int    dQ       = 0        // v10: displacement grade tied to the shift
    var int    retStart = na       // v10: bar the current visit began (dwell)
    var float  depth    = 0        // v10: deepest penetration of the current visit, 0..1+
    var float  mSl      = na       // own stop / TP2 for the ACTIVE state (v5.3 F4)
    var float  mTp      = na
    bool  sig = false
    float sl  = na
    if confirmed
        // ---- ACTIVE: released by M18's refusal, or when its own SL / TP2 is reached
        if st == 4 and bar_index > stBar
            if bar_index == stBar + 1
                if not accPrev
                    st     := 0
                    // v11 (V11-06): rejL / rejS are cleared to "—" on any bar the
                    // arbiter ACCEPTED another producer, so a machine entry voided
                    // by the clash rule released with "entry refused · —".
                    reason := rejPrev == "—" or rejPrev == "" ? "entry refused (arbiter)" : "entry refused · " + rejPrev
                else if not na(tgtPrev)
                    mTp := tgtPrev                              // the real TP2 (M19), not rrMult × risk
            if st == 4 and (isL ? low <= mSl or high >= mTp : high >= mSl or low <= mTp)
                st     := 0
                reason := "trade resolved"
        // ---- invalidation checks first (any armed stage)
        if st >= 1
            if not na(swExt) and (isL ? close < swExt : close > swExt)
                st     := 0
                reason := "sweep undone"
            // v9: at SHIFTED with an anchor, a strong opposing candle that HOLDS the
            // anchor is the retest the machine is waiting for — the anchor test below
            // (close through its far edge) is the invalidation there.
            else if oppDisp and (st <= 2 or na(aNear))
                st     := 0
                reason := "opposing displacement"
        if st >= 2 and zoneInv and na(fvgBar)
            st     := 0
            reason := "POI violated"
        // ---- stage expiry
        if st == 1 and bar_index - stBar > liqWait
            st     := 0
            reason := "sweep expired (no POI tap)"
        if st == 2 and bar_index - stBar > poiWait
            st     := 0
            reason := "POI tap expired (no shift)"
        if st == 3 and bar_index - stBar > retWait
            st     := 0
            reason := "retest window expired"
        if st == 3 and na(aNear) and bar_index - shBar > maxFvgDelay          // v10 (V10-08)
            st     := 0
            reason := "no shift-leg FVG within " + str.tostring(maxFvgDelay) + " bars"
        // ---- ARM on a quality sweep printed THIS bar (every writer ran above the snapshot, V8-00)
        if st == 0 and inPlay and lastBar == bar_index and lastQual >= minArmQual
            bool chopBlock = useRegime and regime == "CHOP" and lastQual < 4
            if not chopBlock
                array.set(setupCtr, 0, array.get(setupCtr, 0) + 1)
                id       := array.get(setupCtr, 0)
                st       := 1
                stBar    := bar_index
                armBar   := bar_index
                legBar   := bar_index
                swExt    := lastExt
                qual     := lastQual                                // v7 memory
                typ      := lastType
                ses      := lastSes
                poiT     := 5
                aNear    := na
                aFar     := na
                fvgBar   := na
                shBar    := na
                mQ       := 0
                dQ       := 0
                visit    := 0
                wasIn    := false
                retStart := na
                depth    := 0
        // ---- SWEPT → AT POI (fresh zone · OTE · HTF POI)
        if st == 1 and (tapZone or tapOte or tapHtf)
            st     := 2
            stBar  := bar_index
            legBar := bar_index                                    // v9: the leg that must shift starts at the POI
            // v11 (V11-04): the ternary tested the ZONE first, so a tap that was
            // both a generic S/D zone and an OTE leg graded 4 instead of 3 — the
            // worse of the two locations won. The better location decides the
            // tier; the zone still supplies the anchor below. A QUASIMODO QML
            // (V11-07) is a raided level, not a generic zone — tier 3.
            poiT   := tapHtf ? 1 : tapOte or (isL ? nbQm : nsQm) ? 3 : 4
            if tapZone
                aNear := zNear
                aFar  := zFar
        // ---- → SHIFTED. v8 (V8-02): an EXTERNAL shift straight from SWEPT; a CISD
        // only from AT POI (→ B). v9 (§3): the anchor FVG must have been CREATED on
        // or after the bar the leg began. The shift grade is remembered (§11).
        bool toShift = (st == 1 and shiftExt) or (st == 2 and (shiftExt or shiftCisd))
        if toShift
            st       := 3
            stBar    := bar_index
            shBar    := bar_index
            mQ       := shiftExt ? (dispQ >= 2 ? 3 : 2) : 1
            dQ       := dispQ
            visit    := 0
            wasIn    := false
            retStart := na
            depth    := 0
            if not na(fBar) and fBar >= legBar
                aNear  := fNear                                     // lock the shift-leg FVG as the anchor
                aFar   := fFar
                fvgBar := fBar
                poiT   := math.min(poiT, 2)
        if st == 3
            // v10 (V10-02): a displacement inside the causal window belongs to the shift
            if bar_index > shBar and bar_index - shBar <= maxDispDelay and dispQ > dQ
                dQ := dispQ
                if mQ >= 2 and dQ >= 2
                    mQ := 3
            // the FIRST FVG formed after the shift — only inside maxFvgDelay, only before any retest began
            if na(fvgBar) and visit == 0 and not na(fBar) and fBar > shBar and fBar - shBar <= maxFvgDelay
                aNear  := fNear
                aFar   := fFar
                fvgBar := fBar
                poiT   := math.min(poiT, 2)
            if not na(aNear)
                // v9 (§1 / §8): a RETEST is a VISIT — price enters the anchor on a bar
                // after the shift bar and after the FVG's creation bar. v10: the visit
                // has a start bar (dwell) and a depth; §15: the entry close must sit
                // at the anchor (chasePoiAtr, halved in EXTREME volatility).
                bool inA = bar_index > stBar and (na(fvgBar) or bar_index > fvgBar) and (isL ? low <= aNear : high >= aNear)
                if inA and not wasIn
                    visit    += 1
                    retStart := bar_index
                    depth    := 0
                float h = math.abs(aFar - aNear)
                if inA and h > 0
                    depth := math.max(depth, (isL ? aNear - low : high - aNear) / h)
                int   dwell = inA and not na(retStart) ? bar_index - retStart + 1 : 0
                float chase = chasePoiAtr * atr * (volReg == 3 ? 0.5 : 1.0)
                if (isL ? close < aFar : close > aFar)
                    st     := 0
                    reason := "anchor POI violated"
                else if inA and dwell > maxRetDwell and v9FirstOnly
                    st     := 0
                    reason := "FIRST RETEST FAILED (dwell " + str.tostring(dwell) + " > " + str.tostring(maxRetDwell) + " bars)"
                else if inA and (isL ? close > aFar : close < aFar) and conf and (visit == 1 or not v9FirstOnly) and dwell <= maxRetDwell and (isL ? close - aNear : aNear - close) <= chase
                    sig   := true
                    sl    := isL ? math.min(math.min(low, aFar), nz(swExt, low)) - SL_PAD_ATR * atr : math.max(math.max(high, aFar), nz(swExt, high)) + SL_PAD_ATR * atr
                    st    := 4
                    stBar := bar_index
                    mSl   := sl                                        // v5.3 F4: own resolution references
                    mTp   := isL ? close + rrMult * (close - sl) : close - rrMult * (sl - close)
                else if not inA and wasIn and v9FirstOnly
                    st     := 0
                    reason := "FIRST RETEST FAILED (left the POI unconfirmed)"
                wasIn := inA
    [st, stBar, aNear, aFar, fvgBar, swExt, reason, qual, typ, ses, mQ, poiT, visit, wasIn, armBar, id, shBar, dQ, retStart, depth, sig, sl]

// LONG machine — anchor near = top, far = bottom
[suL, suLBar, suLAnchorT, suLAnchorB, suLFvgBar, suLSweepExt, suLReason, suLQual, suLType, suLSes, suLMssQ, suLPoiT, suLVisit, suLIn, suLArmBar, suLId, suLShiftBar, suLDispQ, suLRetStart, suLDepth, mcSigL, mcSlL] =
     f_machine(true, sslInPlay, lastSslBar, lastSslQual, lastSslType, lastSslSes, lastSslExt,
     inDemand and retestLong and nbFresh, nbTop, nbBot, inOTEbuy, htfLocL,
     mssUp or eChochUp, cisdUp, dispQUp, cFvgBTop, cFvgBBot, cFvgBBar,
     zoneInvalidatedUp, bearBar and body >= dispFactor * atr, zoneBullConf, mcAccL, rejL, mcTgtL)
// SHORT machine — anchor near = bottom, far = top (so [.., B, T, ..] here)
[suS, suSBar, suSAnchorB, suSAnchorT, suSFvgBar, suSSweepExt, suSReason, suSQual, suSType, suSSes, suSMssQ, suSPoiT, suSVisit, suSIn, suSArmBar, suSId, suSShiftBar, suSDispQ, suSRetStart, suSDepth, mcSigS, mcSlS] =
     f_machine(false, bslInPlay, lastBslBar, lastBslQual, lastBslType, lastBslSes, lastBslExt,
     inSupply and retestShort and nsFresh, nsBot, nsTop, inOTEsell, htfLocS,
     mssDn or eChochDn, cisdDn, dispQDn, cFvgSBot, cFvgSTop, cFvgSBar,
     zoneInvalidatedDn, bullBar and body >= dispFactor * atr, zoneBearConf, mcAccS, rejS, mcTgtS)
sigMCLong  = mcSigL
sigMCShort = mcSigS
slMcL := mcSlL
slMcS := mcSlS
// v10: dwell of the current / entry visit (bars), for the score and the journal
suLDwell = na(suLRetStart) ? 0 : bar_index - suLRetStart + 1
suSDwell = na(suSRetStart) ? 0 : bar_index - suSRetStart + 1

// v8 (V8-07): the stop the RR gate measures is the highest-ranked RAW
// candidate's OWN stop — machine > narrative model > engine.
f_slPick(bool mc, bool p7, float sMc, float sP7, float sEng) =>
    mc ? sMc : p7 ? sP7 : sEng
sigSLLong  := f_slPick(sigMCLong,  sigP7Long,  slMcL, slP7L, slEngL)
sigSLShort := f_slPick(sigMCShort, sigP7Short, slMcS, slP7S, slEngS)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 17B
// ◈ v5 — CONFIRMATION ENGINE (the quality floor under the engine triggers)
// WHY: v4 finalised nine independent trigger engines with one test —
// "tier ≥ minRank", default B — and tier B needs only a trigger plus ONE core
// layer. A CRT candle with a stale sweep in play therefore shipped as a signal.
// The setup machine (M17) already walks the full narrative; these nine did not.
// This module gives them a shared, explicit floor built ONLY from series the
// script already computes — no new indicator, no new lookback:
//   LIQ    a sweep is in play, or an engineered pool was taken
//   POI    price is at a demand/supply zone, an OTE leg, a v4 OB / QM / FVG,
//          or a BPR that just retested
//   STRUCT a structure shift is live — BOS / CHoCH / MSS / CISD, or the
//          Phase-3 HIDDEN CHoCH (the early one) inside the same window
//   DISP   a displacement body printed within the last 3 bars
//   V4STR  the Phase-1 HH/HL classification is not against the trade. This is
//          what finally makes the Phase-1 engine do work — in v4 it computed a
//          full structure state and then only printed it on a table.
//   LATE   price has not already run more than N ATR from the sweep that
//          justifies the trade — the anti-chase rule
//   RR     the nearest OPPOSING liquidity still pays the minimum multiple
// MODE presets move the floor without touching the individual switches:
//   Aggressive = none of them (this is exactly v4's behaviour)
//   Balanced   = LIQ + POI
//   Strict     = LIQ + POI + STRUCT + DISP + V4STR
//   Custom     = whatever the five switches below say
// LATE and RR apply in every mode (set them to 0 to disable).
// The setup machine and the Phase-7 models keep their own stacks and are NOT
// filtered here — they are already narrative-complete.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
grpV5 = "1 · Core engine — confirmation floor · anti-chase · RR"
v5Mode = input.string("Balanced", "Confirmation mode for the engine triggers",
     options = ["Aggressive", "Balanced", "Strict", "Custom"], group = grpV5,
     tooltip = "Aggressive reproduces v4 (tier filter only). Balanced demands a liquidity event AND a point of interest. Strict adds a live structure shift and fresh displacement. Custom uses the four switches below.")
v5cLiq  = input.bool(true,  "Custom · require a liquidity event",        group = grpV5)
v5cPoi  = input.bool(true,  "Custom · require price at a POI",           group = grpV5)
v5cStr  = input.bool(false, "Custom · require a live structure shift",   group = grpV5)
v5cDisp = input.bool(false, "Custom · require fresh displacement",       group = grpV5)
v5Late  = input.float(2.5, "Anti-chase — max ATR from the sweep origin (0 = off)", step = 0.5, minval = 0, group = grpV5,
     tooltip = "Rejects a trigger that fires after price has already travelled this far from the wick of the sweep that justifies it. The move is gone; the risk is not.")
v5MinRr = input.float(1.5, "Min RR to the nearest opposing liquidity (0 = off)", step = 0.5, minval = 0, group = grpV5,
     tooltip = "Reward measured to the nearest resting level on the far side (Phase-2 map), risk to the stop of the highest-ranked candidate (v8). No known target = refused while 'Require a KNOWN liquidity target' is ON, else the gate passes.")
v8Cost = input.float(0, "Spread + slippage allowance (ticks, 0 = off)", step = 0.5, minval = 0, group = grpV5,
     tooltip = "v8: effective RR = (reward − cost) / (risk + cost), cost = this many ticks. On 1M gold the spread is a large share of a 0.5-ATR stop; a 1:2 plan can be 1:1.4 after cost. The gate, the label and the alert all use the effective figure.")
v5RegUp = input.bool(true,  "Raise the tier floor one step outside TRENDING", group = grpV5,
     tooltip = "In RANGING / TRANSITION / CHOP the same technical trigger is worth less. The engine-trigger tier floor moves up one grade; the setup machine is unaffected.")

v5Lv      = v5Mode == "Aggressive" ? 0 : v5Mode == "Balanced" ? 1 : v5Mode == "Strict" ? 2 : 3
v5ReqLiq  = v5Lv == 3 ? v5cLiq  : v5Lv >= 1
v5ReqPoi  = v5Lv == 3 ? v5cPoi  : v5Lv >= 1
v5ReqStr  = v5Lv == 3 ? v5cStr  : v5Lv >= 2
v5ReqDisp = v5Lv == 3 ? v5cDisp : v5Lv >= 2

// which layers are still missing right now — operator explainability
f_v5Why(bool liq, bool poi, bool str_, bool disp, bool late, bool rr, bool tgt, bool blk) =>
    string w = ""
    w := f_p5Add(w, v5ReqLiq  and not liq,  "liq")
    w := f_p5Add(w, v5ReqPoi  and not poi,  "poi")
    w := f_p5Add(w, v5ReqStr  and not str_, "struct")
    w := f_p5Add(w, v5ReqDisp and not disp, "disp")
    w := f_p5Add(w, not late, "chase")
    w := f_p5Add(w, blk,      "path blocked")
    w := f_p5Add(w, not rr and not blk, tgt ? "RR" : "no target")
    w := f_p5Add(w, volReg == 3, "extreme vol · machine only")
    w

// v10 (V10-04): TARGET ENGINE. Candidates come from the fresh-liquidity map:
//   n  nearest fresh opposing level of ANY type (swing · zone edge · EQ pool · external)
//   x  nearest fresh EXTERNAL level (ext swing · PDH/PDL · PWH/PWL)
//   w  the HTF objective — a fresh PWH/PWL, else PDH/PDL, beyond the entry
// Consumed (f_taken), wrong-side and inside-noise (p2MinAtr) levels never enter
// the map. Rules, in order:
//   1 PATH   n closer than minPathR × risk = BLOCKED — price reacts there before
//            the trade is paid. v9 had no such notion: it measured RR to n and
//            refused a 3 R external target because a swing sat 1.2 R away.
//   2 TP2    the best fresh level paying ≥ rrMult × risk: n itself, else x, else
//            w. None → the nearest fresh level paying ≥ v5MinRr ("short of
//            plan"). None → NO TARGET → refused (synthetic rows are ink only).
//   3 TP1    n when it pays ≥ 1 R and is not TP2 (the internal objective).
//   4 RR     effective (spread / slippage) RR to TP2 · rrN = RR to n (dashboard).
f_tgt(bool isL, float e, float sl) =>
    float risk = math.abs(e - sl)
    float cst  = v8Cost * syminfo.mintick
    float n    = isL ? p2NearUp : p2NearDn
    float x    = isL ? p2ExtUp  : p2ExtDn
    float w    = isL ? (not pwhTaken and pwh > e ? pwh : not pdhTaken and pdh > e ? pdh : na) : (not pwlTaken and pwl < e ? pwl : not pdlTaken and pdl < e ? pdl : na)
    float dn   = math.abs(n - e)
    float dx   = math.abs(x - e)
    float dw   = math.abs(w - e)
    bool  blocked = minPathR > 0 and risk > 0 and not na(n) and dn < minPathR * risk
    float t2   = not na(n) and dn >= rrMult * risk ? n : not na(x) and dx >= rrMult * risk ? x : not na(w) and dw >= rrMult * risk ? w : na
    bool  short_ = false
    if na(t2)
        t2 := not na(n) and dn >= v5MinRr * risk ? n : not na(x) and dx >= v5MinRr * risk ? x : not na(w) and dw >= v5MinRr * risk ? w : na
        short_ := not na(t2)
    float t1   = not na(n) and dn >= risk and (na(t2) or n != t2) ? n : na
    float rr   = risk > 0 and not na(t2) ? (math.abs(t2 - e) - cst) / (risk + cst) : na
    [t1, t2, w, rr, blocked, short_]                        // v11 (V11-09): the RR-to-nearest slot was a debug number; `blocked` already carries what it meant

// wrapped in a function (CE10295 — Pine caps the GLOBAL-scope compiled size;
// function bodies compile separately). Every term below is a series the script
// already computes — this module adds no new lookback and no new indicator.
f_v5Gate() =>
    bool liqL  = sslInPlay or recentEngLo
    bool liqS  = bslInPlay or recentEngHi
    // v7Quality: POI means AT the POI. nearDemand reaches 1.5 ATR above the zone
    // and let a trigger pass the floor without price ever retracing into anything.
    bool poiL  = inDemand or inOTEbuy  or p6InObL or p6InFvgL or p3BprTapUp
    bool poiS  = inSupply or inOTEsell or p6InObS or p6InFvgS or p3BprTapDn
    bool strL  = recentStructUp or recentCisdUp or recentMssUp or p3HchUpRec
    bool strS  = recentStructDn or recentCisdDn or recentMssDn or p3HchDnRec
    // anti-chase: measured from whichever liquidity origin is carrying the LIQ
    // layer on this bar. v4 only knew the swing-sweep wick, so a trigger whose
    // liquidity came from an engineered pool skipped the test entirely.
    float origL = sslInPlay ? lastSslExt : recentEngLo ? lastEngLoExt : na
    float origS = bslInPlay ? lastBslExt : recentEngHi ? lastEngHiExt : na
    // v8 (V8-16): also from the origin of the live displacement candle
    bool lateL = v5Late == 0 or ((na(origL) or close - origL <= v5Late * atr * lateM) and (not dispUpLive or na(lastDispUpLo) or close - lastDispUpLo <= v5Late * atr * lateM))
    bool lateS = v5Late == 0 or ((na(origS) or origS - close <= v5Late * atr * lateM) and (not dispDnLive or na(lastDispDnHi) or lastDispDnHi - close <= v5Late * atr * lateM))
    // risk the firing engine actually proposes (the fallback M19 also uses)
    float slL  = not na(sigSLLong)  and sigSLLong  < close ? sigSLLong  : math.min(low,  low[1])  - SL_PAD_ATR * atr
    float slS  = not na(sigSLShort) and sigSLShort > close ? sigSLShort : math.max(high, high[1]) + SL_PAD_ATR * atr
    // v10 (V10-04): reward to the SELECTED TP2 of the target engine; a blocked
    // path is a hard refusal; an unknown target still fails (V8-01) — RR = na
    // is a missing hard input, not a pass.
    [t1L, t2L, t3L, rrL, blkL, shL] = f_tgt(true,  close, slL)
    [t1S, t2S, t3S, rrS, blkS, shS] = f_tgt(false, close, slS)
    bool rrOkL = not na(rrL) and not blkL and (v5MinRr == 0 or rrL >= v5MinRr)
    bool rrOkS = not na(rrS) and not blkS and (v5MinRr == 0 or rrS >= v5MinRr)
    // v10 (V10-13): EXTREME volatility — engine / model / trap candidates are refused (the machine is not floored here)
    bool okL = (not v5ReqLiq or liqL) and (not v5ReqPoi or poiL) and (not v5ReqStr or strL) and (not v5ReqDisp or recentDispUp) and lateL and rrOkL and volReg != 3
    bool okS = (not v5ReqLiq or liqS) and (not v5ReqPoi or poiS) and (not v5ReqStr or strS) and (not v5ReqDisp or recentDispDn) and lateS and rrOkS and volReg != 3
    // v7 post-news: in the minutes after a scheduled window an engine candidate
    // needs the WHOLE narrative — liquidity, structure, displacement, at-POI —
    // whatever the mode says. The setup machine is not floored here (it is the
    // narrative), so it keeps its own path.
    bool fullL = liqL and strL and recentDispUp and poiL
    bool fullS = liqS and strS and recentDispDn and poiS
    okL := okL and (newsState != 2 or fullL)
    okS := okS and (newsState != 2 or fullS)
    string whyL = f_v5Why(liqL, poiL, strL, recentDispUp, lateL, rrOkL, not na(rrL), blkL)
    string whyS = f_v5Why(liqS, poiS, strS, recentDispDn, lateS, rrOkS, not na(rrS), blkS)
    whyL := f_p5Add(whyL, newsState == 2 and not fullL, "post-news")
    whyS := f_p5Add(whyS, newsState == 2 and not fullS, "post-news")
    // the last two are the RR verdicts the setup machine borrows (v5.2 V3).
    // It does NOT borrow lateL / lateS: those measure from whichever sweep is
    // still "in play", and the machine's own stage budget (liqWait + poiWait +
    // retWait, up to 55 bars) routinely outlives sweepLook (15), so origL would
    // be na by entry time and the test would pass for free. The machine gets
    // its anti-chase measured from its OWN held sweep wick, in MODULE 18.
    [okL, okS, whyL, whyS, rrL, rrS, rrOkL, rrOkS, t1L, t2L, t3L, t1S, t2S, t3S, blkL, blkS, shL, shS]
[v5OkL, v5OkS, v5WhyL, v5WhyS, v5RrL, v5RrS, v5RrOkL, v5RrOkS, v5T1L, v5T2L, v5T3L, v5T1S, v5T2S, v5T3S, v5BlkL, v5BlkS, v5ShL, v5ShS] = f_v5Gate()
// v10: clean-path score to the SELECTED TP2 (the ladder's pathL/pathS measure to the nearest level)
pathL2 = f_path(true,  v5T2L)
pathS2 = f_path(false, v5T2S)

// v9 (§23): regime-aware tier floor BY SETUP CLASS — engine triggers only.
// TRENDING penalises a reversal (continuation preferred) · RANGING penalises a
// continuation (sweep / reversal preferred) · TRANSITION penalises everything
// (high selectivity) · CHOP is suppressed upstream (chopOK) unless the arming
// sweep was institutional, and then also penalised. CONT = external structure
// AND the HTF bias already point the trade's way (the arbiter's class rule).
contL = extDir == 1  and htfB > 0
contS = extDir == -1 and htfB < 0
f_rank(bool cont) => minRank + (v5RegUp and minRank < 4 and (regTrending ? not cont : regTransition or regChop or cont) ? 1 : 0)
v5RankL = f_rank(contL)
v5RankS = f_rank(contS)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 18
// SIGNAL FINALIZE — context gates, tier filter, cooldowns, conflict rule
// Precedence on conflict (spec §45): the machine narrative wins; if both
// directions fire on one bar → NO TRADE (both suppressed).
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var int lastLongSigBar  = na
var int lastShortSigBar = na
// v9 (§31): ONE POI, ONE PRIMARY ENTRY. The POI that produced the last accepted
// signal on a side is remembered (machine: its anchor; engines: the zone / FVG /
// OB / QM the entry candle sits in). A new candidate at the same level (within
// 0.25 ATR) is refused until that POI has aged out (zoneMaxAge). Cooldowns
// stop same-candle duplicates; this stops the third entry from one FVG.
poiTopL = sigMCLong  ? suLAnchorT : p6InFvgL ? p3BullTop : p6InObL ? p4ObBullTop : inDemand ? nbTop : na
poiTopS = sigMCShort ? suSAnchorB : p6InFvgS ? p3BearBot : p6InObS ? p4ObBearBot : inSupply ? nsBot : na
var float usedPoiL = na
var float usedPoiS = na
var int   usedPoiBarL = na
var int   usedPoiBarS = na
poiFreeL = na(poiTopL) or na(usedPoiL) or math.abs(poiTopL - usedPoiL) > NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr or (zoneMaxAge > 0 and bar_index - usedPoiBarL > zoneMaxAge)
poiFreeS = na(poiTopS) or na(usedPoiS) or math.abs(poiTopS - usedPoiS) > NEAR_LVL_ATR * atr or (zoneMaxAge > 0 and bar_index - usedPoiBarS > zoneMaxAge)
longCdOK  = masterCd == 0 or na(lastLongSigBar)  or bar_index - lastLongSigBar  > masterCd
shortCdOK = masterCd == 0 or na(lastShortSigBar) or bar_index - lastShortSigBar > masterCd
longOK   = longCtx  and longCdOK  and poiFreeL
shortOK  = shortCtx and shortCdOK and poiFreeS
// v7 AGG: every raw candidate is remembered BEFORE the gates, so the debug table
// can say what fired and why it was refused (MODULE 21, showDbg), and so A+ can
// be withheld when the other side raised ANY candidate at all (§9: no
// directional conflict).
rawL = sigMCLong  or sigSDLong  or sig3Long  or sig4Long  or sigTLLong  or sigCRTLong  or sigTBSLong  or sigHCrtLong  or sigHTbsLong  or sigFEMLong  or sigP7Long
rawS = sigMCShort or sigSDShort or sig3Short or sig4Short or sigTLShort or sigCRTShort or sigTBSShort or sigHCrtShort or sigHTbsShort or sigFEMShort or sigP7Short


// machine entries. v7Quality: the machine grades ITSELF. A when the shift was
// external (MSS / external CHoCH), B when only a CISD or an internal CHoCH
// advanced it. A+ when the arming sweep was strong (≥ 3) in a CORE session,
// HTF and range side agree, a displacement body printed in the shift leg and
// the RR target is REAL — all read from the machine's own memory, not from the
// entry bar's luck. OFF restores v5.3: A by construction, A+ = whatever
// tierLong happens to say on the entry bar.
// v8 A+ for the machine: + sweep type · FIRST retest of the anchor · HTF alignment ·
// execution quality · clean path · no correlated conflict. A needs exec ≥ v8ExecA.
// v10 (V10-05 / V10-12): LEVEL 3 also needs the shift-leg FVG as the anchor, a
// dwell ≤ 2 bars and a clean path to the SELECTED TP2; A needs dwell ≤ 3 and the
// volatility-adjusted exec floor. Depth is scored, not gated (> 100 % by close
// already invalidated the anchor).
mcApL = suLMssQ == 3 and suLQual >= 3 and suLType >= v8ApLiq and suLSes >= 4 and suLVisit == 1 and suLPoiT <= 2 and not na(suLFvgBar) and suLDwell <= 2 and htfB > 0 and htfAlnL >= v8ApHtf and rangeOK and pdPos < 0.5  and execQL >= v8ExecAp and pathL2 >= V8_PATH_AP and corrB >= 0 and v5RrOkL
mcApS = suSMssQ == 3 and suSQual >= 3 and suSType >= v8ApLiq and suSSes >= 4 and suSVisit == 1 and suSPoiT <= 2 and not na(suSFvgBar) and suSDwell <= 2 and htfB < 0 and htfAlnS >= v8ApHtf and rangeOK and pdPos >= 0.5 and execQS >= v8ExecAp and pathS2 >= V8_PATH_AP and corrB <= 0 and v5RrOkS
mcTierL = mcApL ? 4 : suLMssQ >= 2 and suLVisit <= 1 and suLDwell <= 3 and execQL >= execAEff ? 3 : 2
mcTierS = mcApS ? 4 : suSMssQ >= 2 and suSVisit <= 1 and suSDwell <= 3 and execQS >= execAEff ? 3 : 2
// v7PdRev / v8 (V8-15): the CLASS is decided by CONTEXT, not by the producer.
// External structure AND the HTF bias agreeing with the trade = CONTINUATION
// (pullback, any range side); anything else is a REVERSAL and needs the correct
// side of the dealing range. Applied to EVERY candidate since v8.
pdOkL = not v7PdRev or not rangeOK or pdPos < 0.5  or contL
pdOkS = not v7PdRev or not rangeOK or pdPos >= 0.5 or contS
// v5.2 V3: anti-chase for the machine is measured from suL/suSSweepExt — the
// sweep wick this narrative was armed on, which the machine holds all the way
// to entry — not from the "in play" sweep, which has usually aged out by then.
mcLateL = v5Late == 0 or ((na(suLSweepExt) or close - suLSweepExt <= v5Late * atr * lateM) and (not dispUpLive or na(lastDispUpLo) or close - lastDispUpLo <= v5Late * atr * lateM))
mcLateS = v5Late == 0 or ((na(suSSweepExt) or suSSweepExt - close <= v5Late * atr * lateM) and (not dispDnLive or na(lastDispDnHi) or lastDispDnHi - close <= v5Late * atr * lateM))
// v10: the machine's own refusal reasons (the no-trade row and its Setup row say WHY)
mcRawL = sigMCLong
mcRawS = sigMCShort
mcWhyL = f_p5Add(f_p5Add(f_p5Add("", not v5RrOkL, v5BlkL ? "path blocked" : na(v5RrL) ? "no target" : "RR"), not mcLateL, "chase"), mcTierL < minRank, "tier<filter")
mcWhyS = f_p5Add(f_p5Add(f_p5Add("", not v5RrOkS, v5BlkS ? "path blocked" : na(v5RrS) ? "no target" : "RR"), not mcLateS, "chase"), mcTierS < minRank, "tier<filter")
// v8 (V8-01): a known target is a HARD gate for the machine too
sigMCLong  := sigMCLong  and longCtx  and mcTierL >= minRank and v5RrOkL and mcLateL and pdOkL and poiFreeL
sigMCShort := sigMCShort and shortCtx and mcTierS >= minRank and v5RrOkS and mcLateS and pdOkS and poiFreeS
// v5.3 F4 → v10: the machine reads M18's verdict (mcAccL / mcAccS, stamped after
// the arbiter below) on the bar after its entry and releases itself — no outside
// write into its state any more.

// engine trigger candidates: graded through the same layer model, then put
// through the v5 confirmation floor (MODULE 17B). The setup machine above is
// deliberately NOT floored — it already walked sweep → POI → shift → retest.
engTierOKL = tierLong  >= v5RankL and v5OkL
engTierOKS = tierShort >= v5RankS and v5OkS
sigSDLong   := sigSDLong   and longOK and engTierOKL and pdOkL
sig3Long    := sig3Long    and longOK and engTierOKL and pdOkL
sig4Long    := sig4Long    and longOK and engTierOKL and pdOkL
sigTLLong   := sigTLLong   and longOK and engTierOKL and pdOkL
sigCRTLong  := sigCRTLong  and longOK and engTierOKL and pdOkL
sigTBSLong  := sigTBSLong  and longOK and engTierOKL and pdOkL
sigHCrtLong := sigHCrtLong and longOK and engTierOKL and pdOkL
sigHTbsLong := sigHTbsLong and longOK and engTierOKL and pdOkL
sigFEMLong  := sigFEMLong  and longOK and engTierOKL and pdOkL
// v7 AGG: the Phase-7 models and the liquidity-trap engine used to be FINAL
// decisions with their own labels, stops and alerts. They are candidates now —
// same context, same floor, same premium/discount rule as every other trigger.
sigP7Long   := sigP7Long   and longOK and engTierOKL and pdOkL
sigSDShort   := sigSDShort   and shortOK and engTierOKS and pdOkS
sig3Short    := sig3Short    and shortOK and engTierOKS and pdOkS
sig4Short    := sig4Short    and shortOK and engTierOKS and pdOkS
sigTLShort   := sigTLShort   and shortOK and engTierOKS and pdOkS
sigCRTShort  := sigCRTShort  and shortOK and engTierOKS and pdOkS
sigTBSShort  := sigTBSShort  and shortOK and engTierOKS and pdOkS
sigHCrtShort := sigHCrtShort and shortOK and engTierOKS and pdOkS
sigHTbsShort := sigHTbsShort and shortOK and engTierOKS and pdOkS
sigFEMShort  := sigFEMShort  and shortOK and engTierOKS and pdOkS
sigP7Short   := sigP7Short   and shortOK and engTierOKS and pdOkS

anyLong  = sigMCLong  or sigSDLong  or sig3Long  or sig4Long  or sigTLLong  or sigCRTLong  or sigTBSLong  or sigHCrtLong  or sigHTbsLong  or sigFEMLong  or sigP7Long
anyShort = sigMCShort or sigSDShort or sig3Short or sig4Short or sigTLShort or sigCRTShort or sigTBSShort or sigHCrtShort or sigHTbsShort or sigFEMShort or sigP7Short

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 18A
// v10 (V10-10): ENTRY QUALITY SCORE 0–100 — liquidity 15 · HTF 15 · POI 15 ·
// shift 15 · displacement 10 · FVG 10 · retest 10 · target 5 · session 5.
// Machine candidates score from the machine's OWN memory (its arming sweep, its
// shift, its anchor, its visit); engine candidates from the live series and the
// shift lineage. The score can only REMOVE a tier (A ≥ scoreA, A+ ≥ scoreAp)
// and < minScore is NO TRADE — it never promotes: no bucket is reachable without
// the hard gate behind it (a random impulse scores 0 displacement, a 2nd visit
// scores 3 retest, a WEAK zone loses 8 POI points, a stale shift × 0.3).
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
f_score(bool isL) =>
    bool mc   = isL ? sigMCLong : sigMCShort
    // LIQUIDITY 15 — sweep in play (machine: its arming sweep) 8 · grade ≥ 3 +4 · type ≥ 2 +3
    bool liq  = mc or (isL ? sslInPlay : bslInPlay)
    int  lq   = mc ? (isL ? suLQual : suSQual) : (isL ? lastSslQual : lastBslQual)
    int  lt   = mc ? (isL ? suLType : suSType) : (isL ? lastSslType : lastBslType)
    int  sLiq = liq ? 8 + (lq >= 3 ? 4 : 0) + (lt >= 2 ? 3 : 0) : 0
    // HTF 15 — alignment 0–4 → 0 / 4 / 8 / 11 / 13 · HTF location +2 · bias conflict −5 · correlation +2 / −3
    int  aln  = isL ? htfAlnL : htfAlnS
    int  sHtf = aln >= 4 ? 13 : aln == 3 ? 11 : aln == 2 ? 8 : aln == 1 ? 4 : 0
    sHtf += (isL ? htfLocL : htfLocS) ? 2 : 0
    sHtf -= (isL ? htfB < 0 : htfB > 0) ? 5 : 0
    sHtf += (isL ? corrB > 0 : corrB < 0) ? 2 : (isL ? corrB < 0 : corrB > 0) ? -3 : 0
    sHtf := math.max(0, math.min(15, sHtf))
    // POI 15 — tier 1 HTF POI 15 · 2 OB / shift-leg FVG 12 · 3 OTE / QM / BPR 8 · 4 generic zone 5 · none 0; life 1st touch −2 · mitigated −4 · weak −8
    int  pt   = mc ? (isL ? suLPoiT : suSPoiT) : (isL ? poiTL : poiTS)
    int  lf   = mc ? 0 : (isL ? (inDemand ? nbLife : 0) : (inSupply ? nsLife : 0))
    int  sPoi = pt == 1 ? 15 : pt == 2 ? 12 : pt == 3 ? 8 : pt == 4 ? 5 : 0
    sPoi := math.max(0, sPoi - (lf == 1 ? 2 : lf == 2 ? 4 : lf >= 3 ? 8 : 0))
    // SHIFT 15 — grade 3 → 15 · 2 → 11 · 1 (CISD / CHoCH without a quality sweep) → 5, × age (≤ 1 bar 1.0 · A+ 0.85 · A 0.6 · stale 0.3)
    int  mq   = mc ? (isL ? suLMssQ : suSMssQ) : (isL ? shUpQ : shDnQ)
    int  ag   = mc ? f_ageQ(isL ? suLShiftBar : suSShiftBar) : (isL ? shAgeQL : shAgeQS)
    float agF = ag == 3 ? 1.0 : ag == 2 ? 0.85 : ag == 1 ? 0.6 : 0.3
    bool  hasSh = mc ? mq > 0 : not na(isL ? shUpBar : shDnBar)
    int  sMss = hasSh ? math.round((mq == 3 ? 15 : mq == 2 ? 11 : 5) * agF) : 0
    // DISPLACEMENT 10 — the shift's OWN displacement 3 → 10 · 2 → 7 · 1 → 3; an unrelated impulse scores 0
    int  dq   = mc ? (isL ? suLDispQ : suSDispQ) : (not na(isL ? shUpDispBar : shDnDispBar) ? (isL ? shUpDispQ : shDnDispQ) : 0)
    int  sDsp = dq >= 3 ? 10 : dq == 2 ? 7 : dq == 1 ? 3 : 0
    // FVG 10 — retesting the shift-leg FVG (machine: its anchor FVG) 10 · a zone anchor / another entry-grade FVG 4
    bool shFvg = mc ? not na(isL ? suLFvgBar : suSFvgBar) : (isL ? inShFvgL : inShFvgS)
    int  sFvg = shFvg ? 10 : (mc or (isL ? p6InFvgL : p6InFvgS)) ? 4 : 0
    // RETEST 10 — machine: first visit 6 (later 3) · dwell ≤ 2 +2 / 3 +1 · depth optimal +2 / shallow +1 / deep 0; engines: a POI retest this bar 5
    int  sRet = 0
    if mc
        int   dw = isL ? suLDwell : suSDwell
        float dp = (isL ? suLDepth : suSDepth) * 100
        sRet := ((isL ? suLVisit : suSVisit) == 1 ? 6 : 3) + (dw <= 2 ? 2 : dw == 3 ? 1 : 0) + (dp >= retDepthLo and dp <= retDepthHi ? 2 : dp < retDepthLo ? 1 : 0)
    else
        sRet := (isL ? retestLong or p6InFvgL or p6InObL : retestShort or p6InFvgS or p6InObS) ? 5 : 0
    // TARGET 5 — real TP2 with an acceptable RR and a clean path 5 · acceptable RR 3
    int  sTgt = (isL ? v5RrOkL : v5RrOkS) ? ((isL ? pathL2 : pathS2) >= V8_PATH_AP ? 5 : 3) : 0
    // SESSION 5 — core 5 · PM 3 · Asia / off-hours 0
    int  sSes = sesQ == 4 ? 5 : sesQ == 3 ? 3 : 0
    sLiq + sHtf + sPoi + sMss + sDsp + sFvg + sRet + sTgt + sSes
scoreLong  = f_score(true)
scoreShort = f_score(false)
// grade from the score — 4 ≥ scoreAp · 3 ≥ scoreA · 2 ≥ minScore · 0 = NO TRADE (minScore 0 = floor off, the cap still applies)
f_scoreTier(int s) => s >= scoreAp ? 4 : s >= scoreA ? 3 : (minScore == 0 or s >= minScore) ? 2 : 0
scTierL  = f_scoreTier(scoreLong)
scTierS  = f_scoreTier(scoreShort)
scoreOkL = scTierL > 0
scoreOkS = scTierS > 0
anyLong  := anyLong  and scoreOkL
anyShort := anyShort and scoreOkS

// ---- v7 ARBITER — one direction per bar, or none ------------------------------
// Class 0 = setup machine (full narrative) · 1 = narrative model (SB / FVG4) ·
// 2 = technical trigger. Final tier = the machine's own tier when it fired,
// else the engine ladder. A+ is withdrawn when the RR target is synthetic, when
// the other side ALSO raised a raw candidate (directional conflict, §9) or in
// the post-news state.
clsL = sigMCLong  ? 0 : sigP7Long  and p7NarL ? 1 : 2
clsS = sigMCShort ? 0 : sigP7Short and p7NarS ? 1 : 2
finTierL = sigMCLong  ? mcTierL : tierLong
finTierS = sigMCShort ? mcTierS : tierShort
// v10 (V10-10): the score can only REMOVE a tier
finTierL := math.min(finTierL, math.max(scTierL, 1))
finTierS := math.min(finTierS, math.max(scTierS, 1))
if finTierL == 4 and (na(v5RrL) or rawS or newsState == 2)
    finTierL := 3
if finTierS == 4 and (na(v5RrS) or rawL or newsState == 2)
    finTierS := 3
// a candidate graded BELOW the tier filter by the score is refused (the machine reads minRank, engines the regime-raised floor)
rankL = sigMCLong  ? minRank : v5RankL
rankS = sigMCShort ? minRank : v5RankS
anyLong  := anyLong  and finTierL >= rankL
anyShort := anyShort and finTierS >= rankS
// v10 (V10-12): ENTRY LEVEL — 1 AGGRESSIVE (B) · 2 CONFIRMED (A) · 3 INSTITUTIONAL (A+)
lvlL = finTierL == 4 ? 3 : finTierL == 3 ? 2 : 1
lvlS = finTierS == 4 ? 3 : finTierS == 3 ? 2 : 1
// rank = tier × 10 + (2 − class): the higher tier wins a mixed bar; at equal
// tier the machine beats a model beats a trigger; equal rank = NO TRADE.
// v5 I3 let the machine win ANY mixed bar — a B-tier machine (CISD-only shift)
// no longer outranks an A-tier engine on the other side.
v5Clash = anyLong and anyShort
if v5Clash
    int rkL = finTierL * 10 + 2 - clsL
    int rkS = finTierS * 10 + 2 - clsS
    if rkL > rkS
        anyShort := false
    else if rkS > rkL
        anyLong := false
    else
        anyLong  := false
        anyShort := false
// v8 (V8-14) evidence-class count (·ev n): removed in v10 (V10-18, metadata only).
// v8 (V8-15): setup class from context (see pdOkL); a breakout-trap sweep (type 7) is a REV by construction
clsTxtL = contL ? "CONT" : "REV"
clsTxtS = contS ? "CONT" : "REV"
// last rejection reason per side (debug table). Built when a raw candidate was
// refused this bar; cleared by a signal; persists otherwise.
// v10 (V10-11): HARD NO-TRADE ENGINE — every refusal names its reason. `cause`
// says WHY the ladder stopped below the floor (no external shift · no causal
// displacement · stale shift · POI weak / dead · 2nd visit); the machine's own
// reasons (path blocked · no target · RR · chase · tier) ride mcWhy.
f_rej(bool bias, bool kz, bool news, bool chop, bool cd, bool tier, bool flr, string why, bool pd, bool clash, bool pu, bool sc, int score, bool rk, bool mc, string mcWhy, string cause) =>
    string w = ""
    w := f_p5Add(w, not cfgOK, "config: HTF ≤ chart")
    w := f_p5Add(w, not bias,  "HTF conflict")
    w := f_p5Add(w, not kz,    "killzone")
    w := f_p5Add(w, not news,  newsState == 3 ? "pre-news" : newsState == 4 ? "post-news reprice" : "news window")
    w := f_p5Add(w, not chop,  "chop")
    w := f_p5Add(w, not cd,    "cooldown")
    w := f_p5Add(w, not mc and not tier, "tier<floor" + (cause != "" ? " (" + cause + ")" : ""))
    w := f_p5Add(w, not mc and not flr,  why)
    w := f_p5Add(w, mc and mcWhy != "",  mcWhy)
    w := f_p5Add(w, not pd,    "range side")
    w := f_p5Add(w, clash,     "clash")
    w := f_p5Add(w, not pu,    "POI used")
    w := f_p5Add(w, not sc,    "score " + str.tostring(score) + " < " + str.tostring(minScore))
    w := f_p5Add(w, sc and not rk, "score-graded below the tier filter")
    w == "" ? "gated" : w
f_cause(bool isL) =>
    string c = ""
    c := f_p5Add(c, na(isL ? shUpBar : shDnBar), "no ext shift")
    c := f_p5Add(c, not na(isL ? shUpBar : shDnBar) and not (isL ? chainL : chainS), "no causal displacement")
    c := f_p5Add(c, (isL ? chainL : chainS) and (isL ? shAgeQL : shAgeQS) == 0, "stale shift")
    c := f_p5Add(c, isL ? inDemand and nbLife >= 3 : inSupply and nsLife >= 3, "POI weak/dead")
    c := f_p5Add(c, isL ? p3BullIn2 : p3BearIn2, "FVG 2nd visit")
    c := f_p5Add(c, isL ? not sslInPlay : not bslInPlay, "no liquidity event")
    c
if rawL and not anyLong
    rejL := f_rej(biasFilter == "Off" or filtBias >= 0 or htfRevL, kzOK, newsOK, chopOKL, longCdOK,  tierLong  >= v5RankL, v5OkL, v5WhyL, pdOkL, v5Clash, poiFreeL, scoreOkL, scoreLong,  finTierL >= rankL, mcRawL, mcWhyL, f_cause(true))
if rawS and not anyShort
    rejS := f_rej(biasFilter == "Off" or filtBias <= 0 or htfRevS, kzOK, newsOK, chopOKS, shortCdOK, tierShort >= v5RankS, v5OkS, v5WhyS, pdOkS, v5Clash, poiFreeS, scoreOkS, scoreShort, finTierS >= rankS, mcRawS, mcWhyS, f_cause(false))
// v10: the machine's verdict, read by f_machine on the bar after its entry
mcAccL := sigMCLong  and anyLong
mcAccS := sigMCShort and anyShort
if anyLong
    rejL := "—"
if anyShort
    rejS := "—"

// v8 (V8-07): the drawn / tracked stop belongs to the ACCEPTED producer
sigSLLong  := f_slPick(sigMCLong,  sigP7Long,  slMcL, slP7L, slEngL)
sigSLShort := f_slPick(sigMCShort, sigP7Short, slMcS, slP7S, slEngS)
// stamp cooldowns from FINAL signal state only
if sigCRTLong and anyLong
    lastCrtLongBar := bar_index
if sigCRTShort and anyShort
    lastCrtShortBar := bar_index
if sigTBSLong and anyLong
    lastTbsLongBar := bar_index
if sigTBSShort and anyShort
    lastTbsShortBar := bar_index
if anyLong
    lastLongSigBar := bar_index
    usedPoiL := poiTopL
    usedPoiBarL := bar_index
if anyShort
    lastShortSigBar := bar_index
    usedPoiS := poiTopS
    usedPoiBarS := bar_index

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 18B
// ◇ PHASE 7 (v4) — the CLS breakout-classifier labels were REMOVED in v8.
// Display only: the verdict was read by nothing but debug row 23, and the
// weak-break read is duplicated by the ◬ LT setup chips and the ◆ ◈ ◇ sweep
// marks. ~330 raw tokens, paid for the v8 quality engines (MODULE 16E).
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// v7: the finalize block (p7Tgt / p7Rr / p7CdOk / p7AnyL / conflict / E-SL-TP
// lines / model label / alert() / p7Last* / the P8 breakeven trail) is GONE.
// The arbiter in MODULE 18 owns finalisation, MODULE 19 owns the trade lines and
// the tracker, MODULE 23 owns the single dynamic alert.

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 19
// TP / SL — structural stop + TP ladder + ACTIVE trade tracking (validation)
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var float trdEntry = na
var float trdSL    = na
var float trdTP1   = na
var float trdTP2   = na
var int   trdDir   = 0
var bool  trdTp1Hit = false
// validation counters (ARCH-10 — mechanical counts, NOT statistics).
// v5.2: cntA / cntAp / cntLong / cntShort were write-only after MODULE 22 (the
// debug table) was deleted — nothing read them. Removed; the three that feed
// the [TRADE] alerts stay.
var int cntTP1    = 0
var int cntTP2    = 0
var int cntSL     = 0

// v8 (V8-05): intrabar order is unknown. SL and an un-hit TP on the SAME bar is
// AMBIGUOUS — its own outcome, never a win or a loss. MFE / MAE in R are tracked
// per trade; outcomes are counted per tier (mechanical counts, NOT statistics).
var int   cntAmb  = 0
var float trdRisk = na
var float trdMfe  = 0
var float trdMae  = 0
if confirmed and trdDir != 0
    bool hitSl = trdDir == 1 ? low <= trdSL : high >= trdSL
    bool hitT1 = trdDir == 1 ? high >= trdTP1 : low <= trdTP1
    bool hitT2 = trdDir == 1 ? high >= trdTP2 : low <= trdTP2
    trdMfe := math.max(trdMfe, (trdDir == 1 ? high - trdEntry : trdEntry - low) / trdRisk)
    trdMae := math.max(trdMae, (trdDir == 1 ? trdEntry - low : high - trdEntry) / trdRisk)
    if hitSl and (hitT2 or (hitT1 and not trdTp1Hit))
        cntAmb += 1
        trdDir := 0
    else if hitSl
        cntSL += 1
        trdDir := 0
    else
        if hitT1 and not trdTp1Hit
            trdTp1Hit := true
            cntTP1 += 1
        if hitT2
            cntTP2 += 1
            trdDir := 0
// v5.3 F4 → v10: the machine's ACTIVE state resolves INSIDE f_machine against its
// own stop and the real TP2 (mcTgtL / mcTgtS below); a refused entry releases it
// through mcAccL / mcAccS (MODULE 18). No outside write into its state.

float entryP = na
float slP    = na
float tp1P   = na
float tp2P   = na
float tp3P   = na
bool  tp1Real = false
bool  tp2Real = false
bool  tp2Short = false          // v10: TP2 pays ≥ v5MinRr but less than the rrMult plan
bool  tp3Real = false
if (anyLong or anyShort) and confirmed
    entryP := close
    if anyLong
        slP := not na(sigSLLong) and sigSLLong < entryP ? sigSLLong : math.min(low, low[1]) - SL_PAD_ATR * atr
    else
        slP := not na(sigSLShort) and sigSLShort > entryP ? sigSLShort : math.max(high, high[1]) + SL_PAD_ATR * atr
// v11 (V11-01): RE-RUN THE TARGET ENGINE AGAINST THE STOP THE TRADE ACTUALLY USES.
// f_v5Gate (M17B) measured f_tgt against the highest-ranked RAW candidate's stop
// — f_slPick runs machine > model > engine BEFORE the gates — while MODULE 19
// draws, tracks and alerts on the ACCEPTED producer's stop. When the machine
// proposed a wide stop and an engine won the bar, TP2 was "the best fresh level
// paying ≥ rrMult × the MACHINE's risk" printed against the ENGINE's risk: the
// E-line RR, the alert RR, the journal RR and the tracked TP2 all described a
// trade nobody took. f_tgt is a pure function of (side, entry, stop), so
// re-running it here costs one call and no state, and na inputs propagate to na
// targets exactly as the rows already handle. The GATE is deliberately NOT
// changed — it must judge the candidate it ranked, not the one that won.
[ldT1, ldT2, ldT3, ldRr, ldBlk, ldSh] = f_tgt(anyLong, entryP, slP)
if (anyLong or anyShort) and confirmed
    float risk = math.abs(entryP - slP)
    // v10 (V10-04): the ladder is the SAME target engine the gate used (f_tgt, M17B):
    // TP1 = the internal objective (nearest fresh level paying ≥ 1 R, not TP2) ·
    // TP2 = the selected target (≥ rrMult, else ≥ v5MinRr flagged "<plan") ·
    // TP3 = a fresh PWH/PWL (else PDH/PDL) beyond TP2 — the HTF objective.
    // A consumed level is never a target (§7). Each row falls back to 1R /
    // rrMult R / 3R for the DRAWING only and says so — the gate already refused
    // a setup with no real TP2 unless min RR is switched off.
    tp1Real := not na(ldT1)
    tp1P := tp1Real ? ldT1 : anyLong ? entryP + risk : entryP - risk
    tp2Real := not na(ldT2)
    tp2Short := tp2Real and ldSh
    tp2P := tp2Real ? ldT2 : anyLong ? entryP + rrMult * risk : entryP - rrMult * risk
    tp3Real := not na(ldT3) and math.abs(ldT3 - entryP) > math.abs(tp2P - entryP)
    tp3P := tp3Real ? ldT3 : anyLong ? entryP + 3 * risk : entryP - 3 * risk
    // v10: the machine's ACTIVE state resolves against the real TP2 (f_machine reads it next bar)
    if sigMCLong and anyLong
        mcTgtL := tp2P
    if sigMCShort and anyShort
        mcTgtS := tp2P
    // arm validation tracking — v5.2 V6: only while FLAT. This block used to
    // overwrite a live tracked trade, so the older trade's TP1 / TP2 / SL
    // outcome was never counted and its [TRADE] alert never fired. The drawn
    // E / SL / TP lines are unaffected: they still follow every signal.
    if trdDir == 0
        trdEntry := entryP
        trdSL    := slP
        trdTP1   := tp1P
        trdTP2   := tp2P
        trdDir   := anyLong ? 1 : -1
        trdTp1Hit := false
        trdRisk  := risk
        trdMfe   := 0
        trdMae   := 0

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 20
// VISUALIZATION
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
plot(showLevels ? lastRes : na, "Resistance (last swing high)",
     color = color.new(COL_BEAR, 50), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(showLevels ? lastSup : na, "Support (last swing low)",
     color = color.new(COL_BULL, 50), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(showStruct ? protLowE : na, "Protected low (external)",
     color = color.new(COL_BULL, 15), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 2)
plot(showStruct ? protHighE : na, "Protected high (external)",
     color = color.new(COL_BEAR, 15), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 2)
plot(showPdwl ? pdh : na, "Prev day high",  color = color.new(color.silver, 55), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(showPdwl ? pdl : na, "Prev day low",   color = color.new(color.silver, 55), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(showPdwl ? pwh : na, "Prev week high", color = color.new(color.silver, 70), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 2)
plot(showPdwl ? pwl : na, "Prev week low",  color = color.new(color.silver, 70), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 2)

// sweep marks with quality (◆ = swing, ◈ = engineered pool)
// Converted from plotchar to f_mark labels — see the note at f_mark (MODULE 3).
f_mark(showSweeps and sslSweep and confirmed, false, "◆", color.new(COL_BULL, 0))
f_mark(showSweeps and bslSweep and confirmed, true,  "◆", color.new(COL_BEAR, 0))
f_mark(showSweeps and eqlSwept,               false, "◈", color.new(COL_BULL, 0))
f_mark(showSweeps and eqhSwept,               true,  "◈", color.new(COL_BEAR, 0))
f_mark(showSweeps and pdlSweep,               false, "◇", color.new(COL_BULL, 20))
f_mark(showSweeps and pdhSweep,               true,  "◇", color.new(COL_BEAR, 20))
f_mark(showTL and tlUpBreak,                  false, "✕", color.new(COL_BEAR, 20))
f_mark(showTL and tlDnBreak,                  true,  "✕", color.new(COL_BULL, 20))
f_mark(showSesHL and sesHiSwept,              true,  "▿", color.new(COL_BEAR, 15))
f_mark(showSesHL and sesLoSwept,              false, "▵", color.new(COL_BULL, 15))
f_mark(showSesHL and sesHiBroke,              true,  "⇡", color.new(COL_BULL, 15))
f_mark(showSesHL and sesLoBroke,              false, "⇣", color.new(COL_BEAR, 15))

bgcolor(not paintKZ or not timeframe.isintraday ? na : inSB ? color.new(color.teal, 92) : inLon ? color.new(color.blue, 94) : inNY ? color.new(color.orange, 94) : inAsia ? color.new(color.purple, 95) : na, title = "Killzones")
bgcolor(paintNews and timeframe.isintraday and inNews ? color.new(color.red,  90) : na, title = "Scheduled volatility window")

// ---- merged signal label (one per direction per bar, tier-tagged) --------------
// CE10117 compression: one builder for both directions (the two blocks were
// mirror copies of ten if-branches). Same lines, same order, same text.
f_jn(string a, bool c, string p) => c ? (a == "" ? p : a + "\n" + p) : a
f_sigTxt(bool mc, bool sd, bool s3, bool s4, bool tl, bool crt, bool tbs, bool hc, bool ht, bool fem, bool p7, string tier, string zn, string ote, string p7t) =>
    string t = ""
    t := f_jn(t, mc,  "◉ SETUP " + tier)
    t := f_jn(t, sd,  zn + " 50%" + ote)
    t := f_jn(t, s3,  "IB break")
    t := f_jn(t, s4,  "Doji rev")
    t := f_jn(t, tl,  "TL sweep")
    t := f_jn(t, crt, "CRT")
    t := f_jn(t, tbs, "TSoup")
    t := f_jn(t, hc,  "HTF " + htfTf + " CRT")
    t := f_jn(t, ht,  "HTF " + htfTf + " TSoup")
    t := f_jn(t, fem, "◎ FEM " + htfTf + "→LTF")
    t := f_jn(t, p7,  "◇ " + p7t)
    t

// v7: the narrative behind the signal, in the order the brief reads it —
// liquidity event · session · structure · POI · range side · RR. One line under
// the tier; the same string rides the dynamic alert (MODULE 23).
f_m(string a, bool c, string p) => c ? (a == "" ? p : a + " · " + p) : a
f_meta(bool isL) =>
    bool mc  = isL ? sigMCLong : sigMCShort
    bool swp = isL ? sslInPlay : bslInPlay
    bool mss = isL ? recentMssUp : recentMssDn
    bool ech = isL ? extChUpRec : extChDnRec
    int  lt  = mc ? (isL ? suLType : suSType) : (isL ? lastSslType : lastBslType)
    int  lq  = mc ? (isL ? suLQual : suSQual) : (isL ? lastSslQual : lastBslQual)
    string m = isL ? clsTxtL : clsTxtS
    m := f_m(m, mc, "SETUP-" + str.tostring(isL ? suLId : suSId))                 // v10 (V10-07)
    m := f_m(m, swp or mc, (isL ? "SSL " : "BSL ") + f_liqTxt(lt) + " q" + str.tostring(lq))
    m := f_m(m, not swp and not mc and (isL ? recentEngLo : recentEngHi), "pool taken")
    m := f_m(m, timeframe.isintraday, sesName)
    m := f_m(m, mss, "ext MSS")
    m := f_m(m, not mss and ech, "ext CHoCH")
    m := f_m(m, not mss and not ech and (isL ? recentChUp : recentChDn), "iCHoCH")
    m := f_m(m, isL ? recentCisdUp : recentCisdDn, "CISD")
    m := f_m(m, isL ? p6InFvgL : p6InFvgS, "FVG")
    m := f_m(m, isL ? p6InObL : p6InObS, "OB")
    m := f_m(m, isL ? inDemand : inSupply, isL ? "Demand" : "Supply")
    m := f_m(m, rangeOK, pdPos < 0.5 ? "Discount" : "Premium")
    m := f_m(m, true, "HTF " + str.tostring(isL ? htfAlnL : htfAlnS) + "/4 · exec " + str.tostring(isL ? execQL : execQS) + ((isL ? pathL : pathS) >= V8_PATH_AP ? " · path ✓" : " · path ✗"))
    // v11 (V11-01): the RR of the ladder actually drawn (accepted producer's
    // stop), not the gate's RR against whichever candidate ranked highest.
    f_m(m, true, na(ldRr) ? "TP unknown" : "RR 1:" + str.tostring(math.round(ldRr * 10) / 10) + (ldSh ? " <plan" : "") + (ldBlk ? " ·path✗" : ""))
metaL = anyLong  ? f_meta(true)  : ""
metaS = anyShort ? f_meta(false) : ""

// wrapped in a function — CE10295 fix: the main scope hit Pine's compiled-size
// limit; function bodies compile separately. Verbatim v3 logic, zero change.
// v9 (§30): FORENSIC JOURNAL record for the signal on this bar (label tooltip)
// v10 (V10-07): the record answers the operator's questions in order — which
// liquidity event, which shift, its displacement, its FVG, which visit, how deep,
// how long, the POI's life, the target and the score. Engine signals carry the
// shift LINEAGE (f_shift) in place of the machine's memory.
f_jour(bool isL) =>
    bool mc  = isL ? sigMCLong : sigMCShort
    int  shB = mc ? (isL ? suLShiftBar : suSShiftBar) : (isL ? shUpBar : shDnBar)
    int  mq  = mc ? (isL ? suLMssQ : suSMssQ) : (isL ? shUpQ : shDnQ)
    int  dq  = mc ? (isL ? suLDispQ : suSDispQ) : (not na(isL ? shUpDispBar : shDnDispBar) ? (isL ? shUpDispQ : shDnDispQ) : 0)
    int  fvB = mc ? (isL ? suLFvgBar : suSFvgBar) : (isL ? shUpFvgBar : shDnFvgBar)
    int  lf  = isL ? (inDemand ? nbLife : 0) : (inSupply ? nsLife : 0)
    (mc ? "SETUP-" + str.tostring(isL ? suLId : suSId) : "ENG-" + str.tostring(bar_index)) + " · " + str.format_time(time, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", "America/New_York") + " NY · " + regime + " · vol " + volTxt + " · news " + str.tostring(newsState) + " · corr " + str.tostring(corrB) +
     "\nchain: liq " + f_ageTxt(mc ? (isL ? suLArmBar : suSArmBar) : (isL ? lastSslBar : lastBslBar)) + " → shift " + f_ageTxt(shB) + " q" + str.tostring(mq) + " → disp q" + str.tostring(dq) + (dq == 0 ? " (none causal)" : "") + " → FVG " + f_ageTxt(fvB) + (na(fvB) ? " (zone anchor)" : "") +
     " → retest #" + str.tostring(mc ? (isL ? suLVisit : suSVisit) : 1) + (mc ? " dwell " + str.tostring(isL ? suLDwell : suSDwell) + "b depth " + str.tostring((isL ? suLDepth : suSDepth) * 100, "#") + "%" : "") +
     "\nPOI tier " + str.tostring(mc ? (isL ? suLPoiT : suSPoiT) : (isL ? poiTL : poiTS)) + " @ " + str.tostring(isL ? poiTopL : poiTopS, format.mintick) + " · life " + f_lifeTxt(lf) + " · exec " + str.tostring(isL ? execQL : execQS) + " · path " + str.tostring(isL ? pathL2 : pathS2) +
     "\nscore " + str.tostring(isL ? scoreLong : scoreShort) + " · L" + str.tostring(isL ? lvlL : lvlS) + " · RR " + (na(ldRr) ? "—" : str.tostring(math.round(ldRr * 10) / 10)) + " (gate " + (na(isL ? v5RrL : v5RrS) ? "—" : str.tostring(math.round((isL ? v5RrL : v5RrS) * 10) / 10)) + ")"
f_v4SigLabels() =>
    string longTxt = f_sigTxt(sigMCLong, sigSDLong, sig3Long, sig4Long, sigTLLong, sigCRTLong, sigTBSLong, sigHCrtLong, sigHTbsLong, sigFEMLong, sigP7Long, f_tierTxt(mcTierL), "Demand", inOTEbuy ? " +OTE" : "", p7TxtL)
    string shortTxt = f_sigTxt(sigMCShort, sigSDShort, sig3Short, sig4Short, sigTLShort, sigCRTShort, sigTBSShort, sigHCrtShort, sigHTbsShort, sigFEMShort, sigP7Short, f_tierTxt(mcTierS), "Supply", inOTEsell ? " +OTE" : "", p7TxtS)
    // v7: tier · direction · producers agreeing · score / narrative line / producers
    if anyLong and longTxt != ""
        longTxt := f_tierTxt(finTierL) + " LONG · L" + str.tostring(lvlL) + " · " + str.tostring(scoreLong) + "\n" + metaL + "\n" + longTxt
        int rowSL = f_dcRow(bar_index, false, longTxt, 0)
        if rowSL >= 0
            label.new(bar_index, f_dcY(low, false, rowSL), longTxt, yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_label_up,
                 color = color.new(COL_BULL, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = sigSize, tooltip = v9Journal ? f_jour(true) : "")
    if anyShort and shortTxt != ""
        shortTxt := f_tierTxt(finTierS) + " SHORT · L" + str.tostring(lvlS) + " · " + str.tostring(scoreShort) + "\n" + metaS + "\n" + shortTxt
        int rowSS = f_dcRow(bar_index, true, shortTxt, 0)
        if rowSS >= 0
            label.new(bar_index, f_dcY(high, true, rowSS), shortTxt, yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_label_down,
                 color = color.new(COL_BEAR, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = sigSize, tooltip = v9Journal ? f_jour(false) : "")
f_v4SigLabels()

// ---- entry / SL / TP lines of the most recent signal ---------------------------
// wrapped in a function (CE10295 fix) — the drawing objects were only used
// here, so their var state moved inside. Verbatim v3 logic, zero change.
// CE10117 compression: five identical line+label pairs → one row helper writing
// into two arrays. Same five rows, same colours, same text, one delete loop.
var v5TrdLn = array.new<line>()
var v5TrdLb = array.new<label>()
f_trdRow(int x2, float p, color c, string tag) =>
    array.push(v5TrdLn, line.new(bar_index, p, x2, p, color = c, style = line.style_dashed))
    array.push(v5TrdLb, label.new(x2, p, tag, style = label.style_label_left,
         color = color.new(c, 20), textcolor = color.white, size = drawSize))
f_v4TradeLines() =>
    if showTrade and (anyLong or anyShort) and not na(entryP)
        if array.size(v5TrdLn) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(v5TrdLn) - 1
                line.delete(array.get(v5TrdLn, i))
                label.delete(array.get(v5TrdLb, i))
            array.clear(v5TrdLn)
            array.clear(v5TrdLb)
        int x2 = bar_index + TRADE_BARS
        // v7: this printed tp2P / risk — and tp2P IS rrMult × risk, so every trade
        // read "RR 2". Now: RR to the real liquidity target when one exists,
        // otherwise the plan multiple flagged SYNTHETIC.
        float rrReal = ldRr                                   // v11 (V11-01): measured to the drawn TP2 from the drawn SL
        rrTxt = na(rrReal) ? str.tostring(rrMult) + " synthetic" : str.tostring(math.round(rrReal * 10) / 10) + " →liq"
        f_trdRow(x2, entryP, color.gray, "E " + str.tostring(entryP, format.mintick) + " · RR 1:" + rrTxt + " (plan, not promise)")
        f_trdRow(x2, slP,    COL_BEAR,   "SL " + str.tostring(slP, format.mintick))
        f_trdRow(x2, tp1P, color.new(COL_BULL, 45), "TP1 " + str.tostring(tp1P, format.mintick) + (tp1Real ? " ·liq" : " ·1R"))
        f_trdRow(x2, tp2P, color.new(COL_BULL, 20), "TP2 " + str.tostring(tp2P, format.mintick) + (tp2Real ? (tp2Short ? " ·liq <plan" : " ·liq") : " ·" + str.tostring(rrMult) + "R synthetic"))
        f_trdRow(x2, tp3P, COL_BULL,     "TP3 " + str.tostring(tp3P, format.mintick) + (tp3Real ? " ·HTF liq" : " ·3R synthetic"))
f_v4TradeLines()

// ---- HTF POI boxes + FEM locked FVG + machine anchor (last bar only) -----------
// wrapped in a function (CE10295 fix) — box state moved inside, verbatim logic
// CE10117 compression: six near-identical context boxes → one helper + one
// array. Same six boxes, same borders, backgrounds and captions.
var v5PoiBx = array.new<box>()
f_poiBox(int x1, float t, float b, color c, int bd, int bg, string txt) =>
    array.push(v5PoiBx, box.new(x1, t, bar_index + TRADE_BARS, b,
         border_color = color.new(c, bd), bgcolor = color.new(c, bg),
         border_style = line.style_dashed, text = txt, text_size = drawSize,
         // CENTRE — the third anchor, so HTF POI captions stop colliding with
         // the typed-FVG captions still on the right edge
         text_color = color.new(c, 0), text_halign = text.align_center))
f_v4PoiBoxes() =>
    if barstate.islast
        if array.size(v5PoiBx) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(v5PoiBx) - 1
                box.delete(array.get(v5PoiBx, i))
            array.clear(v5PoiBx)
        if showPoi and not na(hPoiBTop)
            f_poiBox(bar_index - 10, hPoiBTop, hPoiBBot, COL_BULL, 50, 95,
                 "HTF " + htfTf + " FVG · demand POI")
        if showPoi and not na(hPoiSTop)
            f_poiBox(bar_index - 10, hPoiSTop, hPoiSBot, COL_BEAR, 50, 95,
                 "HTF " + htfTf + " FVG · supply POI")
        if useFEM and femL == 3
            f_poiBox(femLFvg, femLTop, femLBot, COL_BULL, 35, 92, "◎ FEM FVG · await retest")
        if useFEM and femS == 3
            f_poiBox(femSFvg, femSTop, femSBot, COL_BEAR, 35, 92, "◎ FEM FVG · await retest")
        if suL == 3 and not na(suLAnchorT)
            f_poiBox(nz(suLFvgBar, bar_index - 5), suLAnchorT, suLAnchorB, COL_BULL, 20, 90, "◉ SETUP anchor · await retest")
        if suS == 3 and not na(suSAnchorT)
            f_poiBox(nz(suSFvgBar, bar_index - 5), suSAnchorT, suSAnchorB, COL_BEAR, 20, 90, "◉ SETUP anchor · await retest")
f_v4PoiBoxes()

// ---- OTE box: removed in v9 (display only, ~85 raw). inOTEbuy / inOTEsell and
// the Range-pos dashboard row are unchanged.

// PERF: extend live drawings once on the last bar
// wrapped in a function (CE10295 fix) — mutates drawing objects only, verbatim
f_v4ExtendV3() =>
    if barstate.islast
        if array.size(zones) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(zones) - 1
                z = array.get(zones, i)
                box.set_right(z.bx, bar_index + 1)
                line.set_x2(z.mid, bar_index + 1)
        if array.size(eqhLns) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(eqhLns) - 1
                line.set_x2(array.get(eqhLns, i), bar_index + 1)
        if array.size(eqlLns) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(eqlLns) - 1
                line.set_x2(array.get(eqlLns, i), bar_index + 1)
f_v4ExtendV3()

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 21
// DASHBOARD — Context / Liquidity / Location / Trigger / Setup / Risk
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
f_biasTxt(int b) => b > 0 ? "▲ Bull" : b < 0 ? "▼ Bear" : "—"
f_biasCol(int b) => b > 0 ? color.new(COL_BULL, 75) : b < 0 ? color.new(COL_BEAR, 75) : color.new(color.gray, 75)
f_qualTxt(int q) => q >= 4 ? "institutional" : q == 3 ? "strong" : q == 2 ? "valid" : q == 1 ? "weak" : "—"
f_suTxt(int s, int v, bool inA, bool hasA) => s == 0 ? "idle" : s == 1 ? "SWEPT" : s == 2 ? "AT POI" : s == 3 ? (not hasA ? "SHIFTED · no POI yet" : inA ? "RETEST #" + str.tostring(v) + " active" : v == 0 ? "POI set · await 1st retest" : "retest #" + str.tostring(v) + " left") : "TRIGGERED"

// CE10117 compression: one row helper instead of 2 fully-specified table.cell
// calls per row (same cells, same colours, same tooltips — pure token saving)
f_dr(table t, int r, string a, string b, color bg, string tip = "") =>
    table.cell(t, 0, r, a, bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 85), text_color = color.white, text_size = dashSize, tooltip = tip)
    table.cell(t, 1, r, b, bgcolor = bg, text_color = color.white, text_size = dashSize)

// wrapped in a function (CE10295 fix) — table state moved inside, verbatim logic
f_v4Dashboard() =>
    var table dash = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 20,
         border_color = color.new(color.gray, 70), border_width = 1)
    if showDash and barstate.islast
        rowBg = color.new(color.gray, 85)
        table.cell(dash, 0, 0, "LQ-SD-PA v11", bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 60), text_color = color.white, text_size = dashSize)
        table.cell(dash, 1, 0, cfgOK ? regime + " · vol " + volTxt : "⚠ CONFIG: HTF ≤ chart", bgcolor = not cfgOK ? color.new(color.red, 30) : volReg == 3 ? color.new(color.red, 50) : regime == "TRENDING" ? f_biasCol(extDir) : regime == "CHOP" ? color.new(color.red, 70) : rowBg,
             text_color = color.white, text_size = dashSize)
        f_dr(dash, 1, "HTF bias", (biasFilter == "Off" ? "filter off" : "filter " + biasFilter + " " + f_biasTxt(bFilt)) + "\n1H " + f_biasTxt(b60) + " · D " + f_biasTxt(bD), f_biasCol(htfB))
        f_dr(dash, 2, "Structure", "int " + (msDir > 0 ? "▲" : msDir < 0 ? "▼" : "—") + " · ext " + (extDir > 0 ? "▲" : extDir < 0 ? "▼" : "—"), f_biasCol(extDir))
        sweepTxt = (sslInPlay ? "SSL " + f_liqTxt(lastSslType) + " " + f_qualTxt(lastSslQual) + " " + f_ageTxt(lastSslBar) : "") + (sslInPlay and bslInPlay ? " · " : "") + (bslInPlay ? "BSL " + f_liqTxt(lastBslType) + " " + f_qualTxt(lastBslQual) + " " + f_ageTxt(lastBslBar) : "")
        f_dr(dash, 3, "Sweep in play", sweepTxt == "" ? "none" : sweepTxt, rowBg)
        f_dr(dash, 4, "Range pos", na(pdPos) ? "—" : (pdPos >= 0.5 ? "Premium " : "Discount ") + str.tostring(pdPos * 100, "#") + "%" + (inOTEbuy ? " ·OTE buy" : inOTEsell ? " ·OTE sell" : ""), rowBg)
        f_dr(dash, 5, "Next demand", na(nbTop) ? "none" : str.tostring(nbBot, format.mintick) + "–" + str.tostring(nbTop, format.mintick) + (nbFresh ? " ·fresh" : ""), color.new(COL_BULL, 80))
        f_dr(dash, 6, "Next supply", na(nsBot) ? "none" : str.tostring(nsBot, format.mintick) + "–" + str.tostring(nsTop, format.mintick) + (nsFresh ? " ·fresh" : ""), color.new(COL_BEAR, 80))
        trigTxt = (recentMssUp ? "MSS▲ " : recentChUp ? "CHoCH▲ " : recentBosUp ? "BOS▲ " : "") + (recentCisdUp ? "CISD▲ " : "") +
             (recentMssDn ? "MSS▼ " : recentChDn ? "CHoCH▼ " : recentBosDn ? "BOS▼ " : "") + (recentCisdDn ? "CISD▼" : "")
        f_dr(dash, 7, "Trigger", trigTxt == "" ? "none" : trigTxt, rowBg)
        f_dr(dash, 8, "◉ Setup long",  f_suTxt(suL, suLVisit, suLIn, not na(suLAnchorT)) + (suL == 0 and suLReason != "" ? "\n↳ " + suLReason : ""), suL >= 1 ? color.new(COL_BULL, 60) : rowBg)
        f_dr(dash, 9, "◉ Setup short", f_suTxt(suS, suSVisit, suSIn, not na(suSAnchorT)) + (suS == 0 and suSReason != "" ? "\n↳ " + suSReason : ""), suS >= 1 ? color.new(COL_BEAR, 60) : rowBg)
        f_dr(dash, 10, "Session", sesName + (timeframe.isintraday ? " · " + f_sesQTxt(sesQ) : ""), rowBg)
        f_dr(dash, 11, "News state", not timeframe.isintraday ? "—" : newsState == 1 ? "⚠ WINDOW" : newsState == 3 ? "⚠ PRE-NEWS" : newsState == 4 ? "post-news · REPRICE (no entries)" : newsState == 2 ? "post-news · confirmation" : "clear",
             newsState == 1 or newsState == 4 ? color.new(color.red, 60) : newsState == 2 or newsState == 3 ? color.new(color.orange, 60) : rowBg, "Fixed clock windows — NOT a live economic calendar. v10: NORMAL · PRE-NEWS (newsPreMin before) · NEWS RISK · POST-NEWS REPRICE (newsRepMin after, nothing enters the first impulse) · POST-NEWS CONFIRMATION (machine may enter, engines need the whole narrative, no A+)")
        riskTxt = trdDir == 0 ? "flat" : (trdDir == 1 ? "LONG " : "SHORT ") + str.tostring(trdEntry, format.mintick) +
             " SL " + str.tostring(trdSL, format.mintick) + (trdTp1Hit ? " ·TP1✓" : "") + (trdDir == 0 ? "" : " · MFE " + str.tostring(trdMfe, "#.#") + "R MAE " + str.tostring(trdMae, "#.#") + "R")
        f_dr(dash, 12, "Active trade", riskTxt, trdDir == 1 ? color.new(COL_BULL, 70) : trdDir == -1 ? color.new(COL_BEAR, 70) : rowBg)
        noTrade = anyLong or anyShort ? "" : not cfgOK ? "NO TRADE · HTF / bias TF must be ABOVE the chart TF" : regime == "CHOP" ? "NO TRADE · chop" : inNews and timeframe.isintraday and useNews ? "NO TRADE · volatility window" :
             newsState == 3 ? "NO TRADE · pre-news" : newsState == 4 ? "NO TRADE · post-news reprice" : volReg == 3 ? "CAUTION · extreme volatility — machine only" :
             suL == 0 and suS == 0 and not sslInPlay and not bslInPlay ? "NO TRADE · no liquidity event" : "waiting"
        f_dr(dash, 13, "Verdict", (anyLong ? "LONG signal" : anyShort ? "SHORT signal" : noTrade) +
             "\n◈ " + v5Mode + " gate — L: " + (v5WhyL == "" ? "clear" : "needs " + v5WhyL) + " · S: " + (v5WhyS == "" ? "clear" : "needs " + v5WhyS) +
             "\nRR to TP2  L " + (na(v5RrL) ? "—" : str.tostring(math.round(v5RrL * 10) / 10)) + (v5BlkL ? " ·path blocked" : "") + " · S " + (na(v5RrS) ? "—" : str.tostring(math.round(v5RrS * 10) / 10)) + (v5BlkS ? " ·path blocked" : ""),
             anyLong ? color.new(COL_BULL, 40) : anyShort ? color.new(COL_BEAR, 40) : rowBg,
             "Second line = the confirmation floor (MODULE 17B). 'clear' means an engine / model / trap candidate would be accepted right now; otherwise these are the layers still missing. The setup machine takes only its RR, anti-chase and known-target tests from it.")
        // ◈ v8 quality row — the soft scores behind the tier decision
        f_dr(dash, 14, "◈ quality",
             "L " + clsTxtL + " · exec " + str.tostring(execQL) + " · HTF " + str.tostring(htfAlnL) + "/4 · path " + str.tostring(pathL) +
             "\nS " + clsTxtS + " · exec " + str.tostring(execQS) + " · HTF " + str.tostring(htfAlnS) + "/4 · path " + str.tostring(pathS) +
             (v8CorrSym == "" ? "" : "\ncorr " + (corrB > 0 ? "▲ supports longs" : corrB < 0 ? "▼ supports shorts" : "—")),
             rowBg, "v8 soft scores — they can only REMOVE a tier, never add one. Class from context (CONT = external structure AND HTF agree, else REV) · exec = confirmation-candle quality 0–100 (A ≥ 60, A+ ≥ 75 by default) · HTF = filter EMA + HTF structure + HTF POI + daily EMA · path = clean-path score to the liquidity target (A+ ≥ 75)")
        // ◈ v7 arbiter row (replaces the v4 models row — the models are candidates now)
        f_dr(dash, 15, "◈ Arbiter",
             "L " + (rawL ? (anyLong ? "✓ " + f_tierTxt(finTierL) + " L" + str.tostring(lvlL) : "✗ refused") : "—") +
             " · S " + (rawS ? (anyShort ? "✓ " + f_tierTxt(finTierS) + " L" + str.tostring(lvlS) : "✗ refused") : "—") +
             "\nSB stage L" + str.tostring(p7SbStL) + " / S" + str.tostring(p7SbStS),
             anyLong ? color.new(COL_BULL, 60) : anyShort ? color.new(COL_BEAR, 60) : rowBg,
             "every producer (machine · engines · models) is a CANDIDATE; one direction survives per bar, or none. L = entry level (1 aggressive · 2 confirmed · 3 institutional).")
        // ◈ v10 score + causal chain row
        f_dr(dash, 16, "◈ Score / chain",
             "L " + str.tostring(scoreLong) + " → " + (scTierL == 0 ? "NO TRADE" : f_tierTxt(scTierL)) + " · S " + str.tostring(scoreShort) + " → " + (scTierS == 0 ? "NO TRADE" : f_tierTxt(scTierS)) +
             "\nshift L " + f_ageTxt(shUpBar) + " q" + str.tostring(shUpQ) + (chainL ? " ✓disp" : " ✗disp") + (chainFvgL ? " ✓FVG" : " ✗FVG") + " · S " + f_ageTxt(shDnBar) + " q" + str.tostring(shDnQ) + (chainS ? " ✓disp" : " ✗disp") + (chainFvgS ? " ✓FVG" : " ✗FVG") +
             "\nvol " + volTxt + " " + str.tostring(volPct, "#") + "% · POI life L " + f_lifeTxt(nbLife) + " / S " + f_lifeTxt(nsLife),
             rowBg, "v10 ENTRY QUALITY SCORE 0–100 (liquidity 15 · HTF 15 · POI 15 · shift 15 · displacement 10 · FVG 10 · retest 10 · target 5 · session 5) and the grade it allows — it can only REMOVE a tier. CHAIN = the last external shift per side: its age, grade, whether ITS OWN displacement printed (≤ maxDispDelay bars) and whether ITS OWN FVG exists (≤ maxFvgDelay bars). Volatility regime = ATR percentile. POI life = the nearest zone's lifecycle.")
        // ◈ v10 no-trade row — always visible: the operator's "why not"
        f_dr(dash, 17, "⚙ No-trade",
             "L " + rejL + "\nS " + rejS,
             rowBg, "the reason the last raw candidate on each side was refused (v10 hard no-trade engine): HTF conflict · killzone · pre-news / news / reprice · chop · cooldown · tier<floor (no ext shift · no causal displacement · stale shift · POI weak/dead · FVG 2nd visit · no liquidity event) · liq / poi / struct / disp layers · chase · path blocked · no target · RR · extreme vol · range side · clash · POI used · score")
        if showDbg
            f_dr(dash, 18, "⚙ Target",
                 "↑ TP2 " + (na(v5T2L) ? "none" : str.tostring(v5T2L, format.mintick) + (v5ShL ? " <plan" : "")) + " · TP1 " + (na(v5T1L) ? "—" : str.tostring(v5T1L, format.mintick)) + (v5BlkL ? " · PATH BLOCKED" : "") +
                 "\n↓ TP2 " + (na(v5T2S) ? "none" : str.tostring(v5T2S, format.mintick) + (v5ShS ? " <plan" : "")) + " · TP1 " + (na(v5T1S) ? "—" : str.tostring(v5T1S, format.mintick)) + (v5BlkS ? " · PATH BLOCKED" : ""),
                 rowBg, "v10 target engine: the selected TP2 (best fresh level paying ≥ rrMult, else ≥ min RR flagged <plan) and the internal TP1. PATH BLOCKED = the nearest opposing FRESH level sits inside minPathR × risk, so price reacts there before the trade is paid (v11: this replaced the raw nearest-RR figure, which said the same thing less clearly).")
            f_dr(dash, 19, "⚙ Outcomes",
                 "TP2 " + str.tostring(cntTP2) + " · SL " + str.tostring(cntSL) + " · amb " + str.tostring(cntAmb) + " · news " + str.tostring(newsState),
                 rowBg, "tracked outcomes over the loaded history: TP2 / SL / SL+TP on one bar (ambiguous) — mechanical counts, NOT a win rate · news state 0 normal · 1 risk · 2 post-confirmation · 3 pre · 4 reprice")
f_v4Dashboard()

// MODULE 22 (debug table) REMOVED in v5.1 — 574 raw tokens reclaimed to pay
// for the MODULE 3D declutter layer without going over CE10117. It was the
// showDbg engine-state table: developer-only, default OFF, and its rows
// (machine state, alignment scores, regime, counters) are on the dashboard
// in MODULE 21. f_dg() and the showDbg input went with it.

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 23
// ALERTS — state transitions only, layer-tagged. Use "Once per bar close".
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
tL = finTierL          // v7: the arbiter's tier, not a recomputation
tS = finTierS
alertcondition(anyLong  and tL >= 4, "[SIGNAL] A+ LONG",  "A+ LONG — full narrative (sweep → POI → shift → retest) on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition(anyShort and tS >= 4, "[SIGNAL] A+ SHORT", "A+ SHORT — full narrative on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition(anyLong  and tL == 3, "[SIGNAL] A LONG",   "A-tier LONG on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition(anyShort and tS == 3, "[SIGNAL] A SHORT",  "A-tier SHORT on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition(sigMCLong or sigMCShort, "[SIGNAL] ◉ Setup machine entry", "Setup state machine entry on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition(anyLong,  "[SIGNAL] Any LONG",  "LONG signal on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition(anyShort, "[SIGNAL] Any SHORT", "SHORT signal on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition(sigFEMLong or sigFEMShort, "[SIGNAL] ◎ Fractal entry model", "FEM execution on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
// setup lifecycle
alertcondition((suL == 1 and suL[1] != 1) or (suS == 1 and suS[1] != 1), "[SETUP] Armed (quality sweep)", "Setup armed by a quality sweep on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition((suL == 2 and suL[1] != 2) or (suS == 2 and suS[1] != 2), "[SETUP] POI tapped",            "Setup reached its POI on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition((suL == 3 and suL[1] != 3) or (suS == 3 and suS[1] != 3), "[SETUP] Structure shifted",     "Setup structure shift — awaiting retest on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition((suL == 0 and suL[1] >= 1 and suL[1] <= 3) or (suS == 0 and suS[1] >= 1 and suS[1] <= 3),
     "[SETUP] Invalidated / expired", "Setup invalidated or expired on {{ticker}} {{interval}} — reason on the dashboard Setup row")
// trade management
alertcondition(cntTP1 > cntTP1[1], "[TRADE] TP1 hit", "TP1 (1R) touched on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition(cntTP2 > cntTP2[1], "[TRADE] TP2 hit", "TP2 touched on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition(cntSL  > cntSL[1],  "[TRADE] SL hit",  "Stop touched on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition(cntAmb > cntAmb[1], "[TRADE] SL + TP same bar (ambiguous)", "SL and TP touched on ONE bar on {{ticker}} {{interval}} — outcome unknown, not counted as win or loss")
// v7 AGG: ONE dynamic alert per final signal, carrying the narrative — replaces
// the separate P7 and LT alert() feeds. Create ONE alert on "Any alert()
// function call" to receive it together with the [TRIG] / [LIQ] / [POI] / [CTX]
// feed below.
if (anyLong or anyShort) and confirmed
    alert(f_tierTxt(anyLong ? finTierL : finTierS) + (anyLong ? " LONG " : " SHORT ") + "L" + str.tostring(anyLong ? lvlL : lvlS) + " · score " + str.tostring(anyLong ? scoreLong : scoreShort) + " · " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period + " · " + (anyLong ? metaL : metaS) + " · E " + str.tostring(entryP, format.mintick) + " · SL " + str.tostring(slP, format.mintick) + " · TP1 " + str.tostring(tp1P, format.mintick) + " · TP2 " + str.tostring(tp2P, format.mintick), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
// ---- OUTPUT-LIMIT FIX (RE10140): TRIG / LIQ / POI / CTX moved to alert() ----
// These 16 were named alertconditions. Pine counts every alertcondition against
// the SAME 64-slot budget as plot/plotchar/bgcolor, and the script was 18 over,
// so they now ride the alert() feed instead. Nothing stopped firing and no
// message text changed — but they are no longer separate rows in the alert
// dropdown: create ONE alert on "Any alert() function call" to receive them.
// The SIGNAL / SETUP / TRADE / LT / v4 alerts below are untouched and still
// selectable by name. To promote any line here back to its own dropdown row,
// swap it for an alertcondition — each one costs a slot, and after this pass
// the script has roughly a dozen free.
f_a(bool c, string msg) =>
    if c
        alert(msg, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
    c
sym = " on " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period
// triggers
f_a(mssUp or mssDn,                     "[TRIG] MSS — sweep + displaced structural shift" + sym)
// liquidity
f_a(pdhSweep or pdlSweep,               "[LIQ] Previous day high/low swept" + sym)
f_a(sesHiSwept or sesLoSwept,           "[LIQ] Session level raided" + sym)
f_a(trapUpEvt or trapDnEvt,             "[LIQ] Breakout trap — accepted break failed inside " + str.tostring(TRAP_WIN) + " bars" + sym)
// context
f_a(inNews and not inNews[1],           "[CTX] Scheduled volatility window started" + sym + " — entries suppressed")
// v7 AGG: the five [LT] alertconditions are gone — a trap is a candidate of
// the arbiter, so a confirmed trap fires through [SIGNAL] like everything else,
// and its pattern rides the dynamic alert above. Six output slots reclaimed
// (with the [v4] row below).

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ MODULE 23B
// ◇ PHASE 8 (v4) — the [v4] Any model signal row is gone (v7 AGG): a model fire
// is a line inside the single signal and rides [SIGNAL] + the dynamic alert.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
